## Rent-comp pass on the round-10 entrants (run 2026-09-12 ~1:30-3:00am ET, files 27/27a/27b, script rentcomp_underwrite.py)
- Method: Redfin ZIP rental searches with the 1-bed filter (subject ZIP plus neighbors), Zillow rental and market-trend pages, Craigslist within a few miles, the Redfin rental history of the nearest rented house on the block, and HUD's FY2026 FMR and SAFMR workbooks (huduser.gov/portal/datasets/fmr/fmr2026/FY26_FMRs.xlsx and fy2026_safmrs.xlsx; the .odn summary pages return blank to scrapers, the revised SAFMR workbook breaks openpyxl on a bad datetime, so parse the sheet XML directly). Zillow's `_rb` address-search path is blocked for the MCP unlocker; `/homedetails/<slug>/<zpid>_zpid/` works once the zpid is known (Trulia's page carries it). No RentCast key on file; Rentometer needs an account.
- Result: 133 Hugh Caldwell Rd Charlotte -> NEAR-MISS (1-bed comps $1,100-1,300, base $1,200: rent-to-price 0.79%, CoC -1.8%, DSCR 0.90; needs $1,373/unit, i.e. voucher tenants at the 28214 SAFMR of $1,650 gross; ask the agent for the leases). 610/612 S 2nd St Pinetops -> stays ENTRANT (606 S 2nd St, two doors down, rented at $825-850 three times since Sep 2025; base $725/unit: 1.27%, CoC 7.3%, DSCR 1.39 on framework taxes, ~10.8% on the likely $420 tax bill). File 14 updated: Charlotte score -6.3 (#37), Pinetops -0.7 (#24).
- `rentcomp_underwrite.py` is the template: put the property facts and rent cases in `P`, the comps in `C`, run, and it writes 27b, 27a and updates file 14 with the same `uw()` formula and penalties as round10_final.py.

