## File 14 naming (note added 2026-09-14)
File 14 is the living ranking. Its filename ("14 Live status and ranking of the 42 tracked candidates (2026-09-11).csv") is an identifier, not a count: it held 42 rows when created and holds 55 as of 2026-09-14, and rentcomp_underwrite.py, petersburg_unknowns.py, files 27 and 28, and the memory notes all point at that exact name. Keep the filename stable; read the live count from the file itself and cite it in whichever memo updates it.
- `petersburg_unknowns.py` (2026-09-14): the unknown-unknowns pass on 1934 Oakland St. Same uw() as rentcomp_underwrite.py plus an extra_opex argument for owner-paid water on a single-metered duplex. Writes 28a/28b and updates file 14.

- `decision_board_0914.py` (2026-09-14): builds `29a Decision board, merged and corrected` from the imported claude.ai advisory board (30a in `_advisory/2026-09-14 session/`), with verified Petersburg FY2027 taxes ($1.22), the $133,333 DSCR floor flag, NCDOR next-revaluation years, FEMA SFHA results, and gates-first ranking. File 29 is the route memo. Intake fields to add to round templates: unit mix, zoning conformity, meters/owner-paid services, implied-tax-rate + NC reval year, rental-listing depth per ZIP, FEMA SFHA when First Street >= 5.
- File 30 (2026-09-14): campaign-level unknown-unknowns (conventional rate ~7.4%, cap-rate arithmetic behind the 8% bar, PM fee reality, NC insurance settlement, ZIP rent direction, Portsmouth voucher standards, 2026 VA/NC law changes). decision_board_0914.py now rebases on advisory 31a and adds voucher_standard_2026. Intake fields to add: pm_fee_schedule, roof_age, rent_yoy_direction, voucher_standard, prepay_terms, appraisal_condition_risk.


## Weekly re-sweep automation (built 2026-09-14)

Desktop scheduled task `ogo-weekly-duplex-sweep` (Mondays 6:43 AM local; runs only while the Claude desktop app is open, otherwise at next launch; prompt kept in `weekly_task_prompt.md`). It re-sweeps the 100 highest-stock ZIPs (`sweep_zips.json`: 519 of the 724 listings found in the complete sweep; Zillow slugs carried from the round files or GeoNames-derived), refreshes every tracked row in file 14, and appends anything that passes the gates to file 14 marked UNREVIEWED. Nothing is ever dropped automatically; Najum reviews.

How it moves data: the fetching runs INSIDE the Composio remote workbench (`sweep_remote.py`, exec'd from Dropbox each run) using the workbench's `run_composio_tool` helper with the four Bright Data accounts in rotation (10 threads, about 20 seconds per 40 pages); results are written to `_sweeps/<date>/` on Dropbox with `DROPBOX_UPLOAD_FILE`, the PC's Dropbox client syncs them down, and the local `weekly_sweep.py` does everything else (seen-index diff in `seen_index.csv`, Census geocode with the cache in `model/geo_cache.json`, tract gates from `model/`, knockouts, underwriting with `constants.json`, file 14 folding, tracked refresh, report). The direct Bright Data MCP servers and the REST API with their tokens do not work (hang / 407), so the Composio route is the only fetch leg.

Stages (all `python weekly_sweep.py <stage> --date=YYYY-MM-DD`): plan -> [remote_setup, remote_fetch_lists x5, remote_parse_lists] -> wait listings_raw.csv, wait fetch_counts.json, ingest -> [remote_details(shortlist, "details"), remote_details(tracked, "tracked")] -> wait details.json, prep -> (view photos, write judgments.json) -> underwrite -> wait tracked.json, refresh -> report. `--dry` on underwrite/refresh leaves file 14 untouched.

First run 2026-09-14 (the build test): 200 of 200 list pages, 553 listings across the 100 ZIPs, 156 new to the seen index (the seed missed some of the September 9-11 rows), 13 price cuts, 15 shortlisted, 12 OUT on the photos and remarks (land, single-family, quads, packages, a shell at 420 Mount Vernon Ave Portsmouth, tarps at 3809 Virginia St Raleigh), 3 underwritten (132 Kemper Rd Danville, 311 Arch St Henderson, 2311 Nickey Ave Fayetteville), 55 tracked rows refreshed with no real change. Lessons: Redfin files some in-ZIP-looking cards under "Nearby homes" (556 Bellwood Rd) and hides pending listings from list pages, so "off the list" is not "sold"; Zillow homedetails pages fetch fine (only Zillow's /homes/ search path is robots-blocked); Redfin's markdown has no pending pill, the history's newest event carries it; `mc-gaheysville-va-22840` is the only bad slug in the top 100 (fixed to `mcgaheysville`).

Files: `sweep_remote.py`, `weekly_sweep.py`, `sweep_zips.json`, `seen_index.csv`, `constants.json` (tax, insurance, drive time, CrimeGrade; "auto <date>" entries were looked up by the task), `model/` (tract model + geocode cache + GeoNames, copied out of the Temp scratchpads), `weekly_task_prompt.md`, `_sweeps/weekly_tally.csv`, `_sweeps/<date>/{report.md, scored.csv, results.csv, tracked_changes.csv, judgments.json, photos/}`.

