## Advisory folder convention (adopted 2026-09-14)
The claude.ai advisory project's outputs live under `_advisory/` (permanent parent) with one dated subfolder per submission, e.g. `_advisory/2026-09-14 session/`. Files keep the `CLAUDE.AI` prefix and their own numbering; main-folder numbering is Claude Code's. See `_advisory/README.md`. The folder previously named `_advisory (claude.ai session, 2026-09-14)` was moved to `_advisory/2026-09-14 session` on 2026-09-14; `decision_board_0914.py` SRC path updated.

## 2026-09-15 assimilation pass (main files 32 / 32a / 32b)
- `assimilate_0915.py`: builds `32a Decision board, rebased on advisory files 33-35 and the 9-15 verification pass` from 29a + `_advisory/2026-09-14 session pm/CLAUDE.AI 33c ... .json` + `_sweeps/2026-09-14/tracked.json`, applies the Claude Code overrides (Portsmouth meter and service-line layers, rental-inspection district layers, Danville 2026 UDC, FY2027 tax rates, FY2026 FMRs, Superfund distances), adds rows w1 (132 Kemper) and w2 (2311 Nickey), and patches 23 file 14 rows. Re-runnable, but it APPENDS notes to file 14: restore `_backup_14_before_0915.csv` first if re-running.
- `write_32b_0915.py`: writes the jurisdiction rules ledger (tax rate and cycle, rental inspection program and lookup instrument, lead service line inventory, zoning code status, nonconforming lapse, state preemption status, HUD FY2026 2BR FMR) for ten jurisdictions.
