sold in 2024 and two refinanced in 2023. THIRD SELLER TEXT (Trulia/Zillow record 80879434, undated, before the 8/27/2026 FSBO.com listing): 'Tenants on month to month leases at $875.00', 'AC last replaced 10 years ago', 'Roof replace 12 years ago', 'floor have been recently replaced in both units', 'washer and dryer hookups', 'tenant pays all utilities', 'No owner financing', 'looking to sale as soon as possible' - so the stated rent FELL from $875 to $850, the tenancies are month to month (not 'established'), and the seller's own roof years disagree (2016 in the 2017 MLS remarks and the 2026 text; 12 years ago in the third). The owner's own 2/2024 ask for unit A was $1,000 (Trulia unit record, removed 2/12/2024). METERS: PWC 120Water carries one service-line asset for 741 and one for 745 (two meters, per-unit) - advisory 45's 'two lids' assumption confirmed; owner_paid 0 stands. E911: 741 (LT 37 A, east) and 745 (LT 37 B, west) both typed APT on the PIN, assigned 10/11/2002 (reproduced). ASSESSMENT HISTORY: $86,700 (2012-2016) -> $43,300 at the 2017 revaluation -> $238,100 at the 2025 revaluation; the 2017 halving was sector-wide (711 Tamarack half $47,300 -> $29,400 while the single-family house at 737 rose to $104,400), so it is not a damage event; the county's sales-comparison factor is 1.85x cost for the two whole-duplex parcels against 1.35x for the 96 halves (an appeal argument only if a record error can be shown; G.S. 105-287). STORMWATER: the 2026 line is $168 because the city's FY2027 residential fee is tiered by impervious building area (tier 2 = 2,501-4,800 sf = $14/month); the '$84 per parcel' convention in 32b is corrected. CRIME (city layers, 2-year window 9/24/2024-9/24/2026): 400 m ring 90 persons / 169 property / 12 society (Pecan was 15 / 50 / 14) - the ring holds the 620-unit Lake in the Pines complex (700-946 Tamarack) and the Rosehill Rd strip; 60 m ring 1 / 2 / 0; at the units: vandalism at 741 on 3/13/2024 and larceny by trickery at 745 on 3/2/2024, a simple domestic at 741 on 4/24/2023 (unfounded) and three 2022 reports at 745. FEMA Zone X; tract 37051002402. RENT: achieved Stoneleigh $1,025 (reproduced); NEW asks 3545 Torbay $1,099 (renovated, 9/2026) and the renovated 1176 Landau half $1,250 (11/2/2025, removed in 19 days); Lake in the Pines 2BR $873-1,419 with a free month through 10/6/2026. At the ask: CoC -3.5% in place, 0.6% at the owner's $1,000, 1.3% at $1,025, 7.3% only at $1,250 renovated; 8% needs $1,275 a unit; renovating both units to $1,250 (assumption $40,000) reaches 8% only at $160,000 and is 25% of price against file 08's 10% cap. INSURANCE: advisory 45a re-applied the 10/1/2026 step ($1,680 already carries it; $1,764 is 10/2027) - its recomputed grid is the 10/2027 grid; 45c's grid at $1,680 is the current one and reproduces. HOA: 'Stoneleigh Villas Homeowner Association' is a live NC non-profit (SOS 1093388, formed 4/16/2009, office on this block); neither listing discloses dues; COVENANTS OF RECORD READ 9/24 (ROD Corp search 'STONELEIGH VILLAS', 8 names / 13 entries; three instruments fetched): (a) Restrictive Covenants for Stoneleigh Villas Section One, Book 2842 Page 483-486, recorded 10/12/1981 by the developer O & N Investments Inc (4 pages, read in full): par. 1 permits 'one-detached, single-family dwelling or two (2) to four (4) family dwellings' up to 2.5 stories on any numbered lot (the duplex use is EXPRESSLY permitted by covenant); par. 2 and 10 minimum 850 sf per unit in two- to four-family dwellings (the subject's 948 sf units comply), brick or block foundations, 'no residence or structure shall use asbestos siding or exposed cinder block wall'; par. 4, 7, 8, 9, 14 reserve written consent of the developer or its successors for outbuildings, front-of-structure fences (except developer privacy fences), 'alterations, additions, or changes of any kind ... to the structure or design', masonry work and home occupations (dormant unless a successor asserts them); par. 5 no defective vehicles, bicycles, garbage cans or toys nearer the street than the front corner; par. 6 common pets only; par. 11 runs with the land to 9/1/2011 then auto-extends in ten-year periods (now 2021-2031) unless a recorded majority vote of lot owners amends; par. 12 any lot owner may enforce; par. 15 ten-foot side-line utility easement; par. 16 developer may subject the lots to a PWC underground-electric or street-lighting contract with a continuing monthly payment per building owner. NO leasing or rental restriction, NO association, NO assessment. (b) 'Declaration of Protective & Restrictive Covenants for Stoneleigh Villas Subdivision', Book 8093 Page 58-59, recorded 3/9/2009 by two signers styled 'the owners of two homes in the subdivision': purports to make 'all owners' members of an association, levy $40 monthly dues payable to a private company at a PO Box, fine $500 per violation up to $3,000, and mandate fences, security alarms or bars, curb numbers and security lights, with a 20-year term - one month before the 'Stoneleigh Villas Homeowner Association' non-profit was formed (4/16/2009) with its office at 731 Tamarack Dr. (c) 'Termination of Protective & Restrictive Covenants', Book 9768 Page 433, recorded 12/8/2015 by the then owners of 731 Tamarack Dr (Lot 35, Section One): recites that the prior owner of 731 executed the 2009 declaration, that the co-signer 'never owned property in Stoneleigh Villas Subdivision', that 731 was 'the only property encumbered with the Declaration', and terminates it. READ: no HOA, dues, assessment or leasing restriction binds Lot 37; the 2009 attempt bound one lot and is terminated; the 1981 covenants govern and permit the duplex; a title examiner will note (b) and (c) under the subdivision name. NC next reval 2031 (45 and 45c said 2033; 45a corrected). Photo basis void (2017 FRAR set) reproduced; novice YELLOW unverified. | 9/20: verified 2026 bill $3,256.38 (assessed $238,100; stormwater $168 = two ERUs; Nationstar flag = m