9,"208 Scarborough St Unit A AND B, Spring Lake, NC 28390",185000,"ACTIVE (for sale) - PARK, fails G5 at the building's own $795 rent (9/25)","9/23 advisory 46/47 (claude.ai) | 9/25 CLAUDE CODE 41 assimilation: PARK, P 0.01",-2.0,-0.6,0.97,"YELLOW-verify / C3 interiors, C3-C4 exterior; 2012-era condensers; occupied unit unseen",D+,4.2,3.7,1,,"crime D+ -0.5; drive 4.2h -2; DSCR<1.2 -2; G5 FAIL at own rent (0.86%); density-nonconforming duplex (11,000 sf needed)","9/20: verified 2026 bill $1,620.84 (assessed $59,600; county 0.4990 + Spring Lake 0.7410 + recreation 0.05; town sanitation is NOT on the county bill and was not retrieved); CoC 2.5 / 1.3 / 0.1%, DSCR 1.13 / 1.07 / 1.00 at the board's $1,800; Spring Lake is on the LGC Unit Assistance List. File 14's 12.2% rested on a stale rent line - corrected. P ~0.03. || CLAUDE CODE 41 (9/25 evening; advisory 46/47 verified): PARK stands, FAILS G5 at the building's own rent; P cut to 0.01 (chain 0.05 x 0.70 x 0.60 x 0.70 x 0.85 x 0.60 = 0.0075; advisory 0.02). RENT/TAX (reproduced): 795 a unit is the building's own April 2026 ask (Redfin history 4/12 'Listed for Rent 795', 5/1 'Rental Removed'; apartments.com 208A ad); the 2026 bill 1,620.84 reproduces line by line and the refuse (792 = 2 x 396) and stormwater (60) lines ARE on the county bill (35a/40a's 'no sanitation lines' text withdrawn); the Town's FY2027 schedule keeps 33 a month a unit and 5 an ERU, and the FY2027 tax rate 0.741 is unchanged. Grid S1-S5 reproduce to the dollar. NEW AND LOAD-BEARING: (1) the county deed chain (camapwa) carries FOUR priced sales, not one: 32,000 (9/2008), 17,000 (12/2016), 117,000 (6/3/2021, stamps 234), 160,000 (6/7/2023, stamps 320), after a 2004 trustee's deed to the Secretary of Veterans Affairs; the 2021 gallery in _evidence is the 2016-2021 owner's renovation sale; (2) the Register of Deeds index (through 9/24/2026) holds ONE instrument under the record owner's name, the 2023 deed: NO deed of trust, lien or lis pendens, matching the absence of a lender tax-service vendor on the 2023-2026 bills (the 2022 bill carried CoreLogic for the prior owner): the seller has no payoff floor and no forced-sale pressure; (3) ZONING: Sec. 42-63.3 permits 'Dwelling, single & multiple-family' in R-6, but Sec. 42-192 requires 6,000 sf for the first dwelling unit plus 5,000 for the second (11,000 sf, 60 ft frontage) against 6,033 sf and about 50 ft, and the 42-190(4) lot-of-record exception covers single-family only: the duplex is DENSITY-NONCONFORMING; 42-112(e) bars rebuilding as before if casualty damage exceeds 50 percent of reproducible value (county RCN 86,448), 42-112(d) requires dimensional conformity if a remodel exceeds one-third (28,816), 42-112(f) one-year discontinuance; the board's 'CONFORM' becomes 'use P / structure NONCONF (density)' and a county-planning determination joins the chain (0.60); (4) 'MCO' is unsupported: not among the 18 districts of Article II, no overlay polygon, no such string in the county's 2021 ordinance; R6 came from the Town-initiated 2007 blanket rezoning P07-03 (145 parcels from R6A and R6/MHO); (5) PERMITS: the Town runs its own Inspections Department (CivicPlus portal), so the advisory's empty county permit layers prove nothing; G.S. 160D-1110(c)'s 40,000 exemption names single-family residences only, so the 2023 reroof and 2024 mini-split/electrical work needed Town permits (renovation fee 120-180): ask for the permit numbers; (6) dated Street View: Sep 2007 yellow asbestos-substrate cottage, Jun 2012 already vinyl-sided WITH a wall condenser, May 2022 grey roof and occupied, Jan 2024 new dark roof: the 'mini-splits 2024' claim is at most a partial replacement of 14-year-old equipment (S6 reserve); continuous occupancy 2012-2024; (7) the Town's refuse roll has billed TWO units on every bill since 2021 (two-unit evidence); Spring Lake's E911 convention is one APT-typed point per duplex (205, 208, 306, 310), so the Pecan second-point rule does not transfer. TOWN: LGC control 10/5/2021 to 8/1/2024 (not 7/15); on the 10/6/2025 Unit Assistance List; 37,500 of sales tax withheld 9/9/2025 for the missing FY2022-2024 audits (status unverified); unrestricted fund balance about 8 percent vs a 35 percent policy; DEQ DISTRESSED water/sewer unit (designations 2/4/2026; scores 10/5b/2b/2b/1b, b = missing audits); WWTP NC0030970 1.5 MGD major permit, 2025 flow 0.880 MGD (59 percent), 8 of 12 quarters with a violation identified, NOVs 1/2024-9/2025, no penalties, 4 SSOs in 2025; not on the DWR moratorium list; water bought from PWC and Harnett, a DBP monitoring violation 11/2025. Water/sewer FY2027 retail rates unchanged (minimum 30.87, 5,000 gal 127.95 = S4 1,535 owner-paid if one meter); deposits 200. REVALUATION: Cumberland's next is 2031 (advisory said 2033); at the sector-median factor the 2031 tax is about 1,889 (S5b), at the 2023 price 2,916 (S5). Sector: the twelve V Capital duplexes carry 300 stamps EACH (150,000 each, twelve deeds, not an allocation). GRID (new): S5b CoC -1.1 / -2.4 / -3.5; S6 (8,000 condenser reserve) -0.6 / -1.7 / -2.7; S7 (795+850) 0.2 / -1.1 / -2.3; S8 (10% vacancy) -2.3 / -3.5 / -4.7; S9 (water + 2031 sector tax) -3.7 / -5.0 / -6.2; S10 (10/2027 insurance) -0.8 / -2.0 / -3.2; year one with one turnover NOI 9578, CoC -2.1 at 6.75. Price points at own rent and 6.75: 160,000 -> 2.2 / DSCR 1.12; 150,000 -> 3.6 / 1.19; 137,000 -> 5.7 / 1.31; 125,000 -> 8.0 / 1.43. WATCH: a cut to 165,000 or below; leases at 850 or better; Town permit numbers; a county-planning density/casualty answer; the Town's FY2022-2025 audits filed; the September 2026 UAL.",https://www.redfin.com/NC/Spring-Lake/208-Scarborough-St-28390/unit-B/home/187409413
