g the absence of a lender tax-service vendor on the 2023-2026 bills (the 2022 bill carried CoreLogic for the prior owner): the seller has no payoff floor and no forced-sale pressure; (3) ZONING: Sec. 42-63.3 permits 'Dwelling, single & multiple-family' in R-6, but Sec. 42-192 requires 6,000 sf for the first dwelling unit plus 5,000 for the second (11,000 sf, 60 ft frontage) against 6,033 sf and about 50 ft, and the 42-190(4) lot-of-record exception covers single-family only: the duplex is DENSITY-NONCONFORMING; 42-112(e) bars rebuilding as before if casualty damage exceeds 50 percent of reproducible value (county RCN 86,448), 42-112(d) requires dimensional conformity if a remodel exceeds one-third (28,816), 42-112(f) one-year discontinuance; the board's 'CONFORM' becomes 'use P / structure NONCONF (density)' and a county-planning determination joins the chain (0.60); (4) 'MCO' is unsupported: not among the 18 districts of Article II, no overlay polygon, no such string in the county's 2021 ordinance; R6 came from the Town-initiated 2007 blanket rezoning P07-03 (145 parcels from R6A and R6/MHO); (5) PERMITS: the Town runs its own Inspections Department (CivicPlus portal), so the advisory's empty county permit layers prove nothing; G.S. 160D-1110(c)'s 40,000 exemption names single-family residences only, so the 2023 reroof and 2024 mini-split/electrical work needed Town permits (renovation fee 120-180): ask for the permit numbers; (6) dated Street View: Sep 2007 yellow asbestos-substrate cottage, Jun 2012 already vinyl-sided WITH a wall condenser, May 2022 grey roof and occupied, Jan 2024 new dark roof: the 'mini-splits 2024' claim is at most a partial replacement of 14-year-old equipment (S6 reserve); continuous occupancy 2012-2024; (7) the Town's refuse roll has billed TWO units on every bill since 2021 (two-unit evidence); Spring Lake's E911 convention is one APT-typed point per duplex (205, 208, 306, 310), so the Pecan second-point rule does not transfer. TOWN: LGC control 10/5/2021 to 8/1/2024 (not 7/15); on the 10/6/2025 Unit Assistance List; 37,500 of sales tax withheld 9/9/2025 for the missing FY2022-2024 audits (status unverified); unrestricted fund balance about 8 percent vs a 35 percent policy; DEQ DISTRESSED water/sewer unit (designations 2/4/2026; scores 10/5b/2b/2b/1b, b = missing audits); WWTP NC0030970 1.5 MGD major permit, 2025 flow 0.880 MGD (59 percent), 8 of 12 quarters with a violation identified, NOVs 1/2024-9/2025, no penalties, 4 SSOs in 2025; not on the DWR moratorium list; water bought from PWC and Harnett, a DBP monitoring violation 11/2025. Water/sewer FY2027 retail rates unchanged (minimum 30.87, 5,000 gal 127.95 = S4 1,535 owner-paid if one meter); deposits 200. REVALUATION: Cumberland's next is 2031 (advisory said 2033); at the sector-median factor the 2031 tax is about 1,889 (S5b), at the 2023 price 2,916 (S5). Sector: the twelve V Capital duplexes carry 300 stamps EACH (150,000 each, twelve deeds, not an allocation). GRID (new): S5b CoC -1.1 / -2.4 / -3.5; S6 (8,000 condenser reserve) -0.6 / -1.7 / -2.7; S7 (795+850) 0.2 / -1.1 / -2.3; S8 (10% vacancy) -2.3 / -3.5 / -4.7; S9 (water + 2031 sector tax) -3.7 / -5.0 / -6.2; S10 (10/2027 insurance) -0.8 / -2.0 / -3.2; year one with one turnover NOI 9578, CoC -2.1 at 6.75. Price points at own rent and 6.75: 160,000 -> 2.2 / DSCR 1.12; 150,000 -> 3.6 / 1.19; 137,000 -> 5.7 / 1.31; 125,000 -> 8.0 / 1.43. WATCH: a cut to 165,000 or below; leases at 850 or better; Town permit numbers; a county-planning density/casualty answer; the Town's FY2022-2025 audits filed; the September 2026 UAL.",https://www.redfin.com/NC/Spring-Lake/208-Scarborough-St-28390/unit-B/home/187409413
