as no multifamily exception; 30-7.B.8.a.3-4 (rebuild to prior density) sits under Nonconforming USES and applies to 'a structure housing any nonconforming use' - so Ord. S2025-008 (two-family now P) moved SF-6 duplexes OUT of the section that carries the safety net. City letter needed; P(two-unit rebuild allowed) 0.35, not even. Insurance: advisory 44 double-applied the 10/1/2026 step (the board's $1,680 already carries it; $1,764 is the 10/1/2027 figure). Seller TAI Enterprise Inc is a three-truck intrastate carrier (USDOT 2473625) at the owner's mailing address, not a flipper; both portals show 29 days, 28 Redfin views, 134 Zillow views, 6 saves, no cut. Not in a local historic district (city map 9/2014: Haymount LHD ends at Bragg Blvd/Hillside Ave, 2 km away). 2023 and 2025 bills were advertised delinquent and paid (2025: $3,403.87 with interest, garnishment and advertisement fees, $3,283.35 paid 8/3/2026 by the closing law firm); 2026 bill $3,150.56 unpaid, interest from 1/6/2027. By hand: NC SOS record for TAI (Cloudflare gate) and the eCourts Portal search for estate 21E000508-260 (human-verification gate). | 9/23 photo read (2 exterior frames only): RED on evidence - 1946 cottage with probable asbestos-cement siding (stained), one visible front door, two electric meters, window unit, 'other' heat, no interior frames for a $225,000 flip listed 31 days after a $50,000 buy. Metrics unchanged (CoC -2.7%, DSCR 0.85). OUT stands, P ~0.01. | 9/20: verified 2026 bill $3,150.56 (assessed $235,800 on 928 sf / 1946; no tax line before); SELLER FLAG: sold 6/24/2025 for $20,000 and 7/24/2026 for $50,000 to TAI Enterprise Inc, listed 8/24/2026 at $225,000 (4.5x in a month); prior owners' 2023 and 2025 bills ADVERTISED (delinquent); window units, 'other' heat. CoC -2.7 / -4.0 / -5.2%, DSCR 0.85. OUT. P ~0.01.",https://www.redfin.com/NC/Fayetteville/2614-Pecan-Dr-28303/home/125249017
