 clear, so no short-sale dynamic and no recorded mechanics' claim to date. The owners' only other parcels are in Macclesfield, so the Town's demolition-lien reach does not touch them. TAX (reproduced): the 2026 bill 26A470433368300 is $419.35 and OPEN (levied 9/1, interest 1/6/2027) = 28,527 x 1.47; 2007-2025 all paid; not on the 2025 delinquent advertisement; the county's $150 solid-waste fee bills only the unincorporated area and Leggett. Town rate history 0.46 (FY23) -> 0.58 (FY24 on) held through the 1/1/2024 reappraisal (county 0.95 -> 0.89); Town tax base $65.6M, property-tax revenue $413,000, electric transfer $312,924 = 22.6% of the general fund. ZONING (reproduced and sharpened): county layer M-1 with the lot 95 m inside the polygon; the Town's 2022 map scan puts the LI block at 2nd and Cobb; the Table of Uses (rendered) lists the duplex P only in R-30, R-12, R-10MH, R-7, RMF and OI; Sections 70.05.A.3, 70.06.A.2, 70.06.A.5 and 70.06.A.6 read verbatim (180 days; 60 percent of tax value = $12,916). NEW: the Town FAQ says no zoning permit is required for interior repairs, so a two-family zoning permit for the 2025-26 work is unlikely to exist; the trail is the county electrical/building permits and the Town's two meter sets. STATE LAW (new): G.S. 160D-108(d) gives a 24-month floor only to statutory vesting created by a development permit; S.L. 2025-94 s.29 (law 10/6/2025) added the 'use by right attached to the property' sentence to 160D-108(c); H765 (which would void the 180-day clock) is stuck in House Finance since 5/6/2025. Ask under G.S. 160D-108(h) for a written vested-rights determination (appealable de novo). STREET VIEW SERIES (new): Jan 2008 and May 2013 occupied; Apr 2022 porch stacked with furniture seven months before the tax sale; May 2025 mown and empty with a sign stand at the curb, old windows; Feb 2026 bare dirt, temporary porch posts, new doors - no tenancy visible after April 2022, so a >180-day vacancy between the 11/2022 sale and the remodel is the base case (P about 0.8) unless the Town's utility accounts show otherwise. SEWER (corrected): the DWR list entry is '90% Rule imposed' 5/19/2021 (15A NCAC 02T .0118 = no sewer-line EXTENSION permits until expansion plans are filed), not a statutory moratorium; average flow 0.145 MGD in 2025 = 48% of the 0.3 MGD permit (59% in 2024, 37% Jan-Jul 2026); the Town wrote DEQ in 2026 to lift it. WWTP RECORD (new): 7 state penalties since 11/2021 ($4,779), NOVs 10/2024-6/2026, fecal coliform 525% over limit in Q3 2025, BOD 41% in Q2 2026, 4 of 12 quarters in noncompliance. DEQ distressed list of 2/16/2026 lists Pinetops (score 7); not on the FY2024 UAL; the Sept 2026 UAL is unpublished. UTILITIES (reproduced plus trend): sewer admin charge 24.23 (2023) -> 28.85 (2026), +19%; taps 350/350 -> 1,350/1,000; rental meter deposit 475 (FY27), 150/50 with reference on the July 2026 sheet; sanitation $25 per account; electric 15.49 + 0.1542/kWh; tenant utilities about $195-235 a month. FLOOD (new): Zone X reproduced; the NC OneMap Hurricane Matthew flood-extent raster is NoData at the lot (nearest modelled flooding about 1 km SE along the creek corridor); an unnamed intermittent stream lies 133 m away; AE 1,169 m. LISTING 9/25: $113,900, 74 days, 36 views, 4 favorites, MLS 'Slab foundation' against the vents in frame 9; Zillow carries no for-sale record (Rent Zestimate $1,189 for the building); no rental listing for 610 or 612; 101 E Reason St cut to $1,100. Block: 602, 606 and 614 (plus the lot) are investor- or LLC-owned. GRID: advisory S0-S7 reproduce exactly; new S8 (punch list $12,000 cash) CoC 7.9 / 7.0 / 6.1; S9 (+$3,500 title reserve) 7.4 / 6.5 / 5.7; S10 (re-listed tax with the 10/2027 step) 8.5 / 7.2 / 6.0; year-one lease-up NOI 7819, CoC 3.3 at 6.75. Photo basis reproduced (9 frames, C3 interior / C4 exterior). WATCH: Town determination; county permit numbers; list price at or under 105,000; DEQ letter lifting the 90% rule; the Sept 2026 UAL.",https://www.redfin.com/NC/Pinetops/610-612-S-2nd-St-27864/home/203129412
