26,"2614 Pecan Dr, Fayetteville, NC 28303",225000,ACTIVE (for sale),,-13.7,-2.7,0.85,YELLOW (walk: exterior bids 2-4x the 10% cap; RED candidates open),F,4.2,3.7,1 (NFHL Zone X),no (outside the Haymount LHD; city map 9/2014),YELLOW -4; crime F -3; drive 4.2h -2; DSCR<1.2 -2,"CLAUDE CODE 38 (9/24; advisory 44 verified): OUT stands, P about 0.005 (chain 0.06 x 0.35 x 0.25 x 0.15 x 0.60 = 0.0005, displayed with a 10x allowance). Withdrawn: the '6/24/2025 $20,000 sale' - the county's own deed chain (camapwa DeedDetails) runs 1986 warranty deed $42,000 -> survivorship 12/3/2020 -> estate file 21-E-508 (two heirs, 50/50, 2/22/2021) -> $0 quitclaim between the two heirs 5/9/2025 (12231/0577) -> warranty deed to TAI Enterprise Inc 7/24/2026 ($100 stamps = $50,000, 12584/0183); no June 2025 instrument exists, and the companion quitclaim 12231/0580 the same morning moved 2604 (the 1955 duplex) and 2608 Pecan to the other heir, so the 2025 deeds were a division between the estate's two heirs. NEW: the county E911 layer carries '2616 PECAN DR' as its own address point typed APT on this PIN (2614 is APT too; neighbours are HOM) - documentary support for the two-unit use under the 30-7.A.3 burden, with two-unit county and city solid-waste fees on every bill from 2012 to 2026 and the county R2-DUPLEX class. Rent on comps $800 a unit ($1,600; band $1,550-1,700) REPRODUCED (Redfin 28303 1BR small-property asks $750-825 for 576-900 sf; Zillow 28303 1BR average $945, 18 of 40 in the $700-800 bins). Water: PWC's 120Water inventory carries ONE service-line asset for 2614 and none for 2616, while both other duplexes on the street carry two (2604 'A/B', 2703 two) - owner-paid water and sewer is the base case (P 0.75), about $1270/yr on the 5/2026 water and 5/2025 sewer schedules. 8% price $107,900 at 6.75% tenant-paid, $92,600 owner-paid water; DSCR 1.20 price $128,400 / $110,300. Casualty: 30-7.C.1 routes a nonconforming STRUCTURE with a conforming USE to Article 30-7.C, whose C.5 rule has no multifamily exception; 30-7.B.8.a.3-4 (rebuild to prior density) sits under Nonconforming USES and applies to 'a structure housing any nonconforming use' - so Ord. S2025-008 (two-family now P) moved SF-6 duplexes OUT of the section that carries the safety net. City letter needed; P(two-unit rebuild allowed) 0.35, not even. Insurance: advisory 44 double-applied the 10/1/2026 step (the board's $1,680 already carries it; $1,764 is the 10/1/2027 figure). Seller TAI Enterprise Inc is a three-truck intrastate carrier (USDOT 2473625) at the owner's mailing address, not a flipper; both portals show 29 days, 28 Redfin views, 134 Zillow views, 6 saves, no cut. Not in a local historic district (city map 9/2014: Haymount LHD ends at Bragg Blvd/Hillside Ave, 2 km away). 2023 and 2025 bills were advertised delinquent and paid (2025: $3,403.87 with interest, garnishment and advertisement fees, $3,283.35 paid 8/3/2026 by the closing law firm); 2026 bill $3,150.56 unpaid, interest from 1/6/2027. By hand: NC SOS record for TAI (Cloudflare gate) and the eCourts Portal search for estate 21E000508-260 (human-verification gate). | 9/23 photo read (2 exterior frames only): RED on evidence - 1946 cottage with probable asbestos-cement siding (stained), one visible front door, two electric meters, window unit, 'other' heat, no interior frames for a $225,000 flip listed 31 days after a $50,000 buy. Metrics unchanged (CoC -2.7%, DSCR 0.85). OUT stands, P ~0.01. | 9/20: verified 2026 bill $3,150.56 (assessed $235,800 on 928 sf / 1946; no tax line before); SELLER FLAG: sold 6/24/2025 for $20,000 and 7/24/2026 for $50,000 to TAI Enterprise Inc, listed 8/24/2026 at $225,000 (4.5x in a month); prior owners' 2023 and 2025 bills ADVERTISED (delinquent); window units, 'other' heat. CoC -2.7 / -4.0 / -5.2%, DSCR 0.85. OUT. P ~0.01.",https://www.redfin.com/NC/Fayetteville/2614-Pecan-Dr-28303/home/125249017
