Fayetteville / Cumberland,NC,"county $0.499 + city $0.4495 = $0.9485 per $100 of the county's sales-comparison value (unchanged on the 2026 bills, verified 9/19) PLUS owner-billed fees on the same bill: county household solid-waste fee $130 per dwelling unit (FY2025 and FY2026 schedules), city solid-waste fee $285 per dwelling unit for FY2027 ($275 FY2026), city stormwater $84 per parcel; a duplex pays $914 of fees on the 2026 bill","Cumberland bill details (BillDetails.aspx) for the four Squirrel parcels, 2023-2026; county solid-waste fee schedules FY25/FY26; cityviewnc 5/13/2025 (FY2026 fees); city Trash & Recycling page (FY2027)","county 8-year cycle: 2025, next 2033; NC does not reassess on sale",NO (G.S. 160D-1207 bars periodic rental inspections absent cause),"n/a for rental inspection. Instruments: parcels gis.co.cumberland.nc.us/server/rest/services/Tax/Parcels/MapServer/0 (OWNER, VCS sector, CONDITION class A/F/P/U + % depreciation, REVENUE_STAMPS); bills taxpwa.co.cumberland.nc.us/PublicWebAccess/BillSearchResults.aspx?ParcelNum=<PIN> then BillDetails.aspx?BillPk= (itemized fees, lender tax-service flag, payer names); police incidents gismaps.fayettevillenc.gov/cofopendatagis (Persons/Property/Society layers, 2010-present, address LIKE and 400 m buffer); zoning gismaps.fayettevillenc.gov/cofopendatagis/rest/services/DevelopmentServices/Zoning/MapServer/0; residential renovation permits: NOT in the county EnerGov layer or the city open-data permits layer; IDT Plans portal (login) or Development Services 910-433-1329",n/a,PWC 'Operation Clean & Clear' inventory (lookup not scriptable; the Cumberland GIS viewer has no service-line layer),https://www.faypwc.com/operation-clean-clear/,"UDO Chapter 30 (2011) in force on enCodePlus; Table 30-4.A.2 Use Table amended by Ord. S2024-017B (10/28/2024, retail rows), S2025-008 (4/14/2025: two- to four-family SF-6 cell changed S -> P) and S2026-015 (5/26/2026, MAC column); read the use table at doc-view.aspx?secid=9434 (server-rendered), not doc-viewer.aspx; ordinance PDFs at doclibrary.aspx?id= are image-only","CORRECTED 9/19: 'Dwelling, two- to four-family' is P (permitted by right) in SF-6, SF-10 and MR-5 and S in SF-15 since Ord. S2025-008 of 4/14/2025 (the 3/26/2024 Stamper Rd SUP predates it). Dimensional: SF-6 needs 6,000 sf of lot area PER UNIT (12,000 sf for a duplex) and 60 ft of width, so 1960s duplexes on 6,970 sf lots are nonconforming as to density (30-7.C structure rules, no discontinuance clock outside the NPO overlay; >50% casualty rebuild must conform per 30-7.C.5 unless 30-7.B.8(3) is applied). Design standards 30-4.C.2.a.2 apply to new two- to four-family",30-7.B.5: 365 consecutive days for nonconforming USES (renovation tolls the clock only with approvals); 30-7.C.2: nonconforming STRUCTURES with a conforming use have no clock outside the NPO district; 30-7.A.5: change of ownership does not end a nonconformity,"HB 765 'Save the American Dream Act' (would have required duplex/triplex/quad by right in residential zones of cities of 125,000 or more, effective 1/1/2026) is STUCK: last action 5/6/2025, re-referred to House Finance. SB 205 (housing regulatory reform): last action 6/11/2025, re-referred to House Rules. No NC preemption enacted (UNC SOG bulletin PZLB 36 on 2025 planning legislation: zero duplex hits)","$1,251 (Fayetteville HMFA); 1BR $1,113",none checked,"0 Rhew, 13 Rogers, 11 Edgar, w2 Nickey, 6/4/5 Squirrel, 26 Pecan, 14 Varsity, 9 Scarborough (Spring Lake); 9/19: 6/4/5 + w4 (429) Squirrel zoning -> PASS with density nonconformity; 417 one-household fee roll 2023-2026",2026-09-19,https://www.ncleg.gov/BillLookUp/2025/H765; https://www.ncleg.gov/BillLookUp/2025/S205; https://www.fayettevillenc.gov/Media-Releases/Council-adopts-FY-2027-Budget-No-tax-increases; https://online.encodeplus.com/regs/fayetteville-nc/doc-view.aspx?secid=9434; https://online.encodeplus.com/regs/fayetteville-nc/doclibrary.aspx?id=e4fbed26-0830-47b5-a01b-2fd26b2464f5; https://taxpwa.co.cumberland.nc.us/PublicWebAccess/; https://www.cumberlandcountync.gov/docs/default-source/solid-waste-documents/fee-schedules/solid-waste-fees-fy26.pdf
