.25.pdf; https://www.fayettevillenc.gov/City-Departments/Public-Services/Stormwater/Stormwater-Utility-Fee-Structure-Updates; http://www.davidbcraig.com/; https://www.cumberlandcountync.gov/docs/default-source/tax-documents/delinquent-taxes/delinquent_taxes__2024.pdf; https://www.cumberlandcountync.gov/docs/default-source/tax-documents/delinquent-taxes/delinquent_taxes__2025.pdf; https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_105/GS_105-375.html; https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_47E/GS_47E-2.html
Rocky Mount (Nash / Edgecombe),NC,"city $0.69 FY27 (up 7 cents) + Nash $0.63 FY27 or Edgecombe $0.89 FY27 = 1.32 or 1.58 per $100 of the 2024 revaluation value; the COUNTY bills the county levy only (Edgecombe WebPAAS; Nash county portal) and the CITY bills its own levy through Tyler Munis Citizen Self Service (rockymountnc.munisselfservice.com/css/citizens/RealEstate); no solid-waste, stormwater or recreation line on either bill - refuse, stormwater, water, sewer, electric and gas are on the RMPU utility account; 9/25: subject 2026 = county 610.21 + city 473.08 = 1,083.29; 9/25 night (Nash side, 918 Star): the COUNTY bills through its own Munis CSS (nashcountync.munisselfservice.com, parcel 030537, bill-number search) while the card sits on iasWorld (taxdata.nashcountync.gov); 2026 = county 493.92 + city 540.96 = 1,034.88 on 78,400; a 2025 renovation shows on the 1/1/2026 value (18,060 -> 78,400; card 'Remodeled Year 2025') under G.S. 105-287(a)(2b) - read both Munis AssessmentHistory pages before modelling a 'seller-year' tax","Rocky Mount Telegram 7/9/26; Nash budget adoption; Edgecombe budget; city FY2027 budget adoption news flash 6/22/2026 (69 cents, $269.7M, $30 vehicle fee); WebPAAS and Munis bills for PIN 3759-99-9614",Nash 2024 -> 2032; Edgecombe 2024 -> 2032,"NO (G.S. 160D-1207); Community Code cases (dept 159) are logged in Munis and published on the city's ArcGIS Online as ViolationsAddress (137,504 geocoded cases) and Code_test_map picompln; primary-violation codes seen: GRAS (overgrowth), PN01 (public nuisance), Z001 (zoning/fence permit); status CBO = complied by owner","n/a. Instruments (9/25): city AGOL org 4MdqIsNzxG7xyTvf (928 feature services; search q=orgid:...): External_Viewer_WFL1 (54 AddressPoints with MUNIS_PIN suffixes per dwelling, 55 Buildings with type and year, 17 Zoning, 10 Neighborhoods, 22 Flood Data 2010, 5/9 historic districts, 4 garbage zones, 45 contours), CRM_Parcel_Master 67 (OwnerName, Bookpage, values, Ward), All_Crimes_for