inventory exists (city Survey123 'Water Service Line Material Survey' and 'Lead Service Line Field Survey' results layers hold 13, 133, 2 and 81 records, none within 300 m of Daughtry); ask RMPU for the classification per address",RMPU / Utility Services 252-972-1250 (Call Center); AGOL survey123 results layers (partial),"LDC on Municode Supp. 89 codified through O-2024-41 (6/24/2024); adopted text amendments since, per the city LDC page (read 9/25): O-2024-58 (8/26/2024 sign amortization), O-2024-82 (12/9/2024 fences and walls), O-2025-5 (1/13/2025 plat certificates), O-2025-6 (1/13/2025 clarifying edits: deletes the 'Dwelling, single-family' rows, B-4/B-5 intent, notice tables, board of adjustment reversals at four-fifths, Sec. 1205), O-2025-64 (9/8/2025 pocket neighborhoods in R-8, R-6, R-6MFA, PDR, O-I; 15,000 sf; 4-12 dwellings), O-2026-xx (4/13/2026 internet cafes); outdoor lighting pending; none touches Chapter 11 or the R-10 two-family cell","Sec. 503 Table 5-1: 'Dwelling, two- to four-family' x only in R-6 MFA and PDR (and O-I, O-I(2), B-1 in Table 5-2); blank in A-1, R-15, R-10, R-8, R-6, MHP; no special-use route; 'Accessory dwelling' x in EVERY residential district incl. R-10 under Sec. 507.C (one extra self-contained unit, same lot and ownership, at most 50% of the principal's gross floor area, no owner-occupancy clause); Sec. 601: R-10 10,000 sf / 10,000 per DU / 75 ft width; R-6MFA two-family 7,000 sf / 3,500 per DU / 60 ft; 50 x 150 platted lots are nonconforming lots of record (602/1102) - Daughtry (id 2) NONCONF use + NONCONF lot","Ch. 11 (read verbatim 9/25): 1105.A.3 land uses cease > 180 days -> conform, 'nonconforming uses that have existed for over fifty (50) years are exempt'; 1105.B.4 a nonconforming use of a structure 'discontinued or abandoned for a period of one hundred eighty (180) consecutive days' may not resume; 1107.A 180 consecutive days 'or for more than eighteen (18) months in any three (3) year period'; 1103.B and 1107.B: damage above 66 2/3% of replacement cost -> rebuild only in conformity (appeal to the board of adjustment); 1101.B.1 'no change of title, possession or right to possession of property shall be construed to prevent the continuance of a nonconforming use'; 1105.B.1 no enlargement or structural alteration; STATE: G.S. 160D-108 and S.L. 2025-94 s.29 per files 40/41; ask for a written 160D-108(h) determination; Sec. 602.B (9/25 night): a duplex or multifamily structure 'in accordance with the table of permitted uses and lot area regulations may be constructed and occupied on a lot having less than sixty (60) feet of lot frontage' with 8 and 10 ft side yards; Table 6-2 prior lots of record (50 ft before 8/15/1946: 15 ft front, 20 ft rear); with 1102 (area) an R-6MFA duplex on a 50 x 100 lot of record can be rebuilt",see Fayetteville row,"$1,143 (Rocky Mount MSA FY2026); FY2027 (10/1/2026) 2BR $1,167, 1BR $972; SAFMR 27801 2BR $1,130 (FY2027; FY2026 was $1,110), 27864 $1,130; not a mandatory SAFMR metro; RMHA 2025 utility allowances (City of Rocky Mount): water 2BR $29, sewer $42, trash $16","LGC: Rocky Mount placed on the September 2026 Unit Assistance List (LGC release 9/4/2026, FY2025 audits, with Cary, Greensboro, Zebulon); 4/1/26 LGC warning; S.L. 2026-27 bars electric and gas transfers; WRAL 9/11/2026: fund balance $100M to $20M, at least $30M of cuts, 'good progress', three residents died after summer-2026 power disconnections. UTILITIES: council 3/30/2026 raised rates about 15% effective 4/1/2026 (electric +14.75%, gas +10.58%, water +15.08% = $23.51 per 3,000 gal, sewer +15.05% = $29.28 per 3,000 gal, environmental services +14.86% = $21.25 a month, stormwater $6 to $8 per ERU; about $45 a household a month); residential deposits up to $325. ENVIRONMENT (Edgecombe side, N Daughtry): DSCA dry-cleaner sites DC330003 Prestige Cleaners (620 E Thomas St, Assessment, groundwater risk Higher) and DC330002 Thorne's (502 Rose St, NFA); five closed gas-station USTs on N Raleigh St; no brownfield, inactive hazardous site or landfill within 500 m; 50 housing-code-violation parcels within 300 m of Daughtry (11/2023 layer). NASH SIDE (918 Star): no DSCA / IHS / brownfield / landfill / NPDES in 500 m; UST incidents 173-492 m and closed USTs 163-468 m in the Gold / Pine / Carter warehouse district (I-1 / I-2 zoning 76-99 m from the Happy Hill R-6MFA block). STATUTES: G.S. 105-378(a) ten-year bar on tax-lien enforcement (Nash still carries 2008-2010 and 2015 bills on 918 Star); G.S. 45-36.24(b)(1)a: a pre-10/1/2011 deed of trust with a stated maturity expires 15 years after maturity and is deemed satisfied of record (918 Star's 2007 purchase-money DT expired 5/1/2025)","22 Pine (Nash), 21 Star (Nash), 2 Daughtry (Edgecombe), r10a Pinetops (Edgecombe county rate only); 9/25 late: 2 Daughtry rebased (advisory 48, file 42): PARK-HOLD, G6 FAIL on the documented roll, P 0.03; 9/25 night: 21 Star rebased (advisory 49, file 43): OUT, withdrawn from both markets 9/21-9/23, P 0.01",2026-09-25,https://www.rockymountnc.gov/CivicAlerts.aspx?AID=159; https://www.nctreasurer.gov/news/press-releases/2026/04/01/local-government-commission-warns-rocky-mount-no-further-missteps-will-be-tolerated; https://house.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/SessionLaws/PDF/2025-2026/SL2026-27.pdf; https://www.nctreasurer.gov/news/press-releases/2026/09/04/lgc-applies-financial-oversight-standards-larger-local-governments; https://www.wral.com/news/local/rocky-mount-financial-crisis-progress-brad-briner-treasurer-auditor-september-2026/; https://www.wral.com/news/local/rocky-mount-utility-rate-increase-financial-recovery-march-2026/; https://www.rockymountnc.gov/m/newsflash/home/detail/141; https://www.rockymountnc.gov/m/newsflash/home/detail/185; https://www.rockymountnc.gov/DocumentCenter/View/105/Water-and-Sewer-Retail-Rates-PDF; https://www.rockymountnc.gov/170/Rates-Fees; https://www.rockymountnc.gov/234/Land-Development-Code; https://www.rockymountnc.gov/DocumentCenter/View/7526/