Cherryville / Gaston,NC,"FY2026-27: Gaston County 0.599 (held; levied by the FY2027 budget ordinance Section II, adopted 5/12/2026; 0.81 -> 0.61 at the 2023 reappraisal, 0.599 since FY2025) + City of Cherryville 0.48 (held; Section 6 of the city's FY2026-27 budget ordinance) = 1.079 per 100 of the 1/1/2023 reappraisal value; no fee lines on the county bill (sanitation is on the city utility bill at 17 a cart); 307 S Jacob: 2,152.39 on 199,480 (2024-2026), 2,174.33 in 2023 (county 0.61); bills due 9/1, interest from 1/6; the county collects for the city","gastonnc.devnetwedge.com parcel view (taxing districts and payment history, data date 2026-09-24); gastongov.com FY2027 adopted budget PDF (DocumentCenter/View/9277); cityofcherryville.com 2026-2027 proposed budget PDF (ugd/3f73de_81ac672f...); read 9/25/2026 (round 16)","Gaston: FOUR-YEAR cycle adopted by the commissioners in 2025; last reappraisal 1/1/2023 (307 S Jacob 67,980 -> 199,480, +193 percent; ring ratios to 2021-2026 sales 0.73-1.53, median 1.08), next 1/1/2027 (notices of value February 2027, values online late February, informal appeal 30 days from the notice, bills July 2027; public meetings 9/29, 10/7, 10/8/2026); the 2019 reappraisal preceded it; NC does not reassess on sale; SL 2026-8 does not touch Gaston","NONE (no rental registration or periodic inspection); City Code Ch. 8 Article V (8-121 to 8-134) is the unsafe-buildings / unfit-dwellings article under G.S. 160A-441 et seq. (complaint by a public authority or five residents, or the inspector's own motion; hearing 10-30 days; repair or vacate orders; the city manager sets the procedure); building, electrical and plumbing codes are the county's, enforced by the Gaston County inspection department inside the city (8-37, 8-62, 8-92); no IPMC adoption found","n/a. Gaston / Cherryville instruments (9/25/2026): county property record gastonnc.devnetwedge.com/parcel/view/<6-digit parcel>/<tax year> (plain curl: class, tax code, neighbourhood, assessed and market values by year, taxing districts, billing and payment history 2008+, owner, transfer history with book/page/type/price, CAMA card, land; images at /PropertyImages/ASRIMG/<year>/<id>.JPG and /PropertyImages/CAMA/<year>/<parcel>-1.JPG; the PRC endpoint loads by script); NC OneMap parcels (cntyname='Gaston' is CASE-SENSITIVE; altparno = the 6-digit parcel) and AddressNC (unit points); Register of Deeds gastonnc.courthousecomputersystems.com (Courthouse Computer Systems: Accept the disclaimer, open /LRSearch/LRIndex?searchTabID=0, serialize form QueryFields_ExecuteSearch and POST it to /LRSearch/ExecuteSearch with X-Requested-With to get the results grid HTML; the Image index /Image/ImageIndex?SearchTabID=0 takes book and page and redirects to /Image/ShowDocImage?...BookNum=&PageNum= whose viewer iframe names a /ProcessedImages/<stamp>.pdf that curl fetches; GetDetails answers 500 outside the session); permits: EnerGov CSS selfservice.gastongov.com/energov_prod/selfservice#/search is BLIND to address keywords (no results for a 2022 new-build duplex) and its API answers 500 - ask Building Inspections; Gaston GIS gis.gastongov.com resets plain connections (script app); city zoning ordinance text PDF and zoning map PDFs (street labels in the text layer; districts by hatch against the legend; PyMuPDF crop around the street label), city code chapters as scanned PDFs (OCR; the chapter links are partly mislabelled), city budgets 2018-2027 and audits 2018-2024 as PDFs on /city-budets-and-audits (sic); DEQ distressed assessments (deq.nc.gov water-infrastructure item J-1/J-2), LSL inventory (July 2025 statewide PDF), LWSP ncwater.org/wudc/app/lwsp/report.php?pwsid=01-36-030; ECHO DFR by FRS id 110000915528 (WWTP NC0044440); HCV PHA ghanc.org (403 to curl; Apify web-fetch serves pages, curl serves its PDFs)","no rental permit; G.S. 42-42 governs (one CO alarm per unit per level; smoke alarms; heating in good and safe order); the city furnishes electric meters (30-76(a)) and requires one per housekeeping unit (30-90(c)-(d)); no resale of electricity (30-82); sewer billed on 100 percent of metered water (30-163); deposits 250 for good credit (100 electric, 100 water, 50 sewer), twice the 12-month average for bad credit; application fee 25; transfer 'back into Landlord name' 15; late fee 15 or 3 percent; non-payment fee 50; cut-off if unpaid by 5 pm on the 25th","City of Cherryville PWSID NC0136030 (state 01-36-030): DEQ July 2025 statewide inventory, submitted 10/24/2024: lead 0, galvanized requiring replacement 0, non-lead 1,562, lead status UNKNOWN 1,602 (51 percent); own Indian Creek surface plant 3.2 MGD; 35 miles of mains (cast iron 35 percent, asbestos-cement 10, galvanized 3); oldest meters 61 years; no leak-detection program (2024 LWSP)","deq.nc.gov/water-resources/pws/lead-service-line-inventory-july-2025/open (PDF, grep the PWSID); ncwater.org LWSP report; city Water and Sewer Division 704-435-1737","Zoning Ordinance of 1/14/2002, amended through 12/8/2025 (218-page text PDF on /planning-and-zoning); zoning map PDFs (undated); Subdivision Ordinance 1977 amended through 5/2024; no UDO; the city does its own zoning (county planning calendar linked for county staff); zoning permit fees FY2026-27: two-family dwelling 150, remodel 50, addition 75, fence 25; no zoning-letter fee line","R-9 'Single and Two-Family Medium Density Residential': 7.4.1 permitted uses = all R-15 uses, two-family dwellings, rest homes / nursing care / continuing care; 7.4.2 special uses incl. multi-family at up to 8 units per acre and planned residential developments; 7.4.3 minimum lot: single-family 9,000 sf, two-family 13,000 sf, multi-family 20,000 sf for the first three units; front setback 30 ft, side 8 ft (+10 on a street side), rear 25 ft, height 35 ft; minimum lot width two-family 80 ft with 35 ft at the right-of-way; RMF also permits two-family by right; R-12 and R-15 do not list two-family (advisory 53 read; not re-read)","Sec. 8.5.1: a recorded lot short on area or width may be used for any permitted use if the structure meets the yard requirements; 8.6 front-setback relief to the block average (15 ft floor); 8.3.4: a residential structure damaged below 80 percent of its tax value may be reconstructed at similar size and shape, and for ANY destruction a building permit must be secured within 180 days or reconstruction 'shall not be allowed' unless the Board of Adjustment grants relief (advisory 53 read); G.S. 160D-108(d) 24-month statutory vesting lapse","Cherryville (6,078 in 2020) is far below the 50,000 threshold of G.S. 160D-917 (S.L. 2026-59 s.44 ADU mandate): not applicable; S.L. 2026-39 (no minimum dwelling size, no minimum parking counts) applies from 1/1/2027; S.L. 2025-94 vesting; no duplex or middle-housing mandate reaches Cherryville; R-9 already permits two-family by right","Charlotte-Concord-Gastonia NC-SC HUD Metro FMR Area (METRO16740M16740), a MANDATORY SAFMR metro: FY2027 metro FMR 1BR 1,640 / 2BR 1,785; 28021 SAFMR FY2026 1BR 930 / 2BR 1,030, FY2027 (10/1/2026) 0BR 980 / 1BR 1,020 (918-1,122) / 2BR 1,120 (1,008-1,232); PHA = Gastonia Housing Authority (340 W Long Ave Gastonia, 704-349-5098; administers the HCV for Gaston County; 'located in a designated SAFMR area'; payment standards and allowances unpublished; 9/2026 notice of downward standard adjustments in certain ZIPs; FY2027 plan 'limited voucher issuance'); GHA's 2001 HQS variations: 100 amps per dwelling unit minimum, GFCI/grounding, screens unless central air, R-19 ceilings, treated-lumber steps, no unvented fuel-burning room heaters","FEMA Zone X at 307 S Jacob (NFHL 37071C); Cherryville WWTP NPDES NC0044440 (736 Tot Dellinger Rd; major POTW 2.0 MGD at about 650,000 gpd): ECHO 'Violation Identified' in 11 of 12 quarters to 6/30/2026, 0 SNC, 4 informal actions (NOV 12/9/2022), no penalty, permit expired 7/31/2026 'Admin Continued'; own water plant on Indian Creek; DEQ viability score 5 (2025; 7-8 in 2021-2022), NOT designate