Fayetteville / Cumberland,NC,"county $0.499 + city $0.4495 = $0.9485 per $100 of the county's sales-comparison value (unchanged on the 2026 bills, verified 9/19) PLUS owner-billed fees on the same bill: county household solid-waste fee $130 per dwelling unit (FY2025 and FY2026 schedules), city solid-waste fee $285 per dwelling unit for FY2027 ($275 FY2026), city stormwater $84 per parcel; a duplex pays $914 of fees on the 2026 bill; 9/23: Cumberland INFORMAL appeals for tax year 2027 are open now with a 2/5/2027 deadline (decisions ~April 2027; on-site appraiser review); the 2026 window closed 5/20/2026; sales-comparison values are the county cost value times a per-sector factor (0329MF 2.07, 0055MF 2.985), so appeals need a record error, not a market argument (G.S. 105-287); 9/23 evening: A101 income values are a sector MODEL (VCS 6033: '1 BEDROOM UNITS' $5,520/yr and '2 BEDROOM UNITS' $6,000/yr per unit, 5% vacancy, 40% expenses, 10.499% overall rate) - re-running the model at market rents at the 2031 revaluation roughly doubles a duplex's value ($62,500 -> ~$115,000); 9/24 evening CORRECTION: the city stormwater fee is NOT $84 per parcel - FY2027 residential parcels are tiered by impervious building area (tier 1 <2,500 sf $84/yr, tier 2 2,501-4,800 sf $168/yr, tier 3 >4,800 sf $252/yr; 77/22/1% of parcels); a 1,896 sf duplex with patios and pads (741 Tamarack) bills $168, a 928 sf duplex (2614 Pecan) $84; read the line from each bill","Cumberland bill details (BillDetails.aspx) for the four Squirrel parcels, 2023-2026; county solid-waste fee schedules FY25/FY26; cityviewnc 5/13/2025 (FY2026 fees); city Trash & Recycling page (FY2027)","county cycle SHORTENED: last 2025, NEXT 2031 (Board of Commissioners resolution 3/2/2026: six-year cycle, then possibly four-year with 2035; CityView 3/3/2026); the '2033' carried since file 29a is stale; NC does not reassess on sale","NO (G.S. 160D-1207 bars periodic rental inspections absent cause); RENTAL ACTION MANAGEMENT PROGRAM (RAMP), City Code Ch. 14 Secs. 14-95 to 14-113 (Ord. S2012-003 eff. 7/1/2012): registration after 3+ verified violations in 12 months (14-97) or a disorder-activity count at or above the 90th-percentile threshold (14-101; windows set 1/1 and 7/1 from the prior six months, Appendix A point weights); mandatory meeting, remedial action plan, six-month reviews, revocation, nuisance referral; a registered seller must report the purchaser within 30 days; fee $500 (FY25 fee schedule), civil penalty $50/$100/$500 per day; state ceiling G.S. 160D-1207(c) (top 10% or >4 violations, $500 cap); ask RAMP status for every Fayetteville row","n/a for rental inspection. Instruments: parcels gis.co.cumberland.nc.us/server/rest/services/Tax/Parcels/MapServer/0 (OWNER, VCS sector, CONDITION class A/F/P/U + % depreciation, REVENUE_STAMPS); bills taxpwa.co.cumberland.nc.us/PublicWebAccess/BillSearchResults.aspx?ParcelNum=<PIN> then BillDetails.aspx?BillPk= (itemized fees, lender tax-service flag, payer names); police incidents gismaps.fayettevillenc.gov/cofopendatagis (Persons/Property/Society layers, 2010-present, address LIKE and 400 m buffer); zoning gismaps.fayettevillenc.gov/cofopendatagis/rest/services/DevelopmentServices/Zoning/MapServer/0; residential renovation permits: NOT in the county EnerGov layer or the city open-data permits layer; IDT Plans portal (login) or Development Services 910-433-1329; 9/23 evening: COUNTY CAMA CARDS serve to plain curl at taxpwa.co.cumberland.nc.us/camapwa/ (PropertySummary / BuildingDetails / IncomeDetails?VCS= / SaleDetails?VCS= / LandDetails / OutbuildingDetails / DeedDetails / DocumentDetails .aspx?PARCELPK=<PARCEL_PK from the parcel layer>): deed chains with stamps and instrument types, building cards with bedrooms/baths/exterior/depreciation, and the INCOME MODEL behind every A101 value (unit types, rent per unit, expense ratio, overall rate); PWC lead-service-line dashboard pws-ptd.120wateraudit.com/fayettevillepwc (browser only; two-entry addresses suggest two service records); 9/24: COUNTY E911 ADDRESS POINTS gis.co.cumberland.nc.us/server/rest/services/E911/Addresses/MapServer/0 (ADDRESS, TYPE APT/HOM, PIN, LM_NAME, OLD_ADD) - a second unit address typed APT on the parcel's PIN is documentary two-unit evidence for the 30-7.A.3 burden; PWC 120Water GraphQL counts per address (one asset per metered service: 2614 Pecan one, 2604 and 2703 Pecan two each); county Inspections/CodeEnforcementComplaints and Planning/Permits layers are COUNTY jurisdiction only (0 hits inside the city); Imagery/CC1968 and CC2023 export without a token, CC1982-CC2021 need one; the county's 'Advertisement of Unpaid Real Estate Taxes' PDFs (cumberlandcountync.gov/docs/default-source/tax-documents/delinquent-taxes/delinquent-taxes__<year>.pdf) list parcel, owner and amount by street; the city's official Local Historic Districts map (9/2014 PDF on the Historic Preservation page) is the HLO instrument the zoning layer lacks; the 2025 Schedule of Values PDF (9.5 MB) carries the exterior-wall code key (03 = MAS/ABST/OLD WOOD) but no heating key in its text layer; 9/24 evening: BILL PAYER COLUMN - read the 'Paid By' of every prior bill, not only the status: 'DAVID B CRAIG, ATTORNEY' = the county's tax-foreclosure attorney (davidbcraig.com: 'represents the County of Cumberland in the tax foreclosure matters'; payoffs by certified funds only) so the year was redeemed out of a foreclosure file; a servicer/CoreLogic payment after the interest date = escrow advance; 'YYYY - 700/850' = escrow batch on time. COUNTY OWNER LIKE query for an individual seller lists their other parcels; their bills show whether the default is portfolio-wide. The 2024 and 2025 advertisements live at cumberlandcountync.gov/docs/default-source/tax-documents/delinquent-taxes/delinquent_taxes__YYYY.pdf (underscore pattern; the 2023 file uses the hyphen pattern with ?sfvrsn=782cbf11_2). ROD: the Full System name search reaches deeds of trust and their note amounts; the row's 'Image - N page(s)' button then 'Open in new tab' yields PDFs/User_0_<timestamp>.pdf, which curl fetches (image-only; PyMuPDF) - fetching it ends the browser session. PWC 120Water per-address asset counts (741 and 745 Tamarack one each = per-unit meters). Trulia unit records ('741 Tamarack Dr #A') and a property's second Zillow zpid carry the owner's earlier rent asks and listing texts",n/a,PWC 'Operation Clean & Clear' inventory (lookup not scriptable; the Cumberland GIS viewer has no service-line layer),https://www.faypwc.com/operation-clean-clear/,"UDO Chapter 30 (2011) in force on enCodePlus; Table 30-4.A.2 Use Table amended by Ord. S2024-017B (10/28/2024, retail rows), S2025-008 (4/14/2025: two- to four-family SF-6 cell changed S -> P) and S2026-015 (5/26/2026, MAC column); read the use table at doc-view.aspx?secid=9434 (server-rendered), not doc-viewer.aspx; ordinance PDFs at doclibrary.aspx?id= are image-only; 9/20: overlays - the zoning layer encodes /MHO and /CZ suffixes only; 'NPO' = Noise-Accident Potential Overlay (airport/military), NOT neighborhood preservation; Murchison Road Corridor Overlay (MCO, 30-3.H.8) and the NCO district-specific standards (30-3.H.9.e) are '[Placeholder]' sections with no adopted text; historic overlays (HLO) are not in the layer","CORRECTED 9/19: 'Dwelling, two- to four-family' is P (permitted by right) in SF-6, SF-10 and MR-5 and S in SF-15 since Ord. S2025-008 of 4/14/2025 (the 3/26/2024 Stamper Rd SUP predates it). Dimensional: SF-6 needs 6,000 sf of lot area PER UNIT (12,000 sf for a duplex) and 60 ft of width, so 1960s duplexes on 6,970 sf lots are nonconforming as to density (30-7.C structure rules, no discontinuance clock outside the NPO overlay; >50% casualty rebuild must conform per 30-7.C.5 unless 30-7.B.8(3) is applied). Design standards 30-4.C.2.a.2 apply to new two- to four-family; 9/23 CORRECTION: lot area PER UNIT for two- to four-family is 7,500 sf in SF-10 (duplex 15,000 sf, width 75 ft, coverage 30%, setbacks 30/10/35) and 6,000 sf in SF-6 (12,000) per the 30-3.D.3 and 30-3.D.4 tables; SF-15 lists 15,000 (single-family column; two- to four-family is S there); MR-5 reads '5,000 for 1st unit, then 4,000' - read at the ordinance before use; 814 Varsity (SF-10, GIS 14,584 sf) sits on the line and its plat (PB 18 PG 44) is unread","30-7.B.5: 365 consecutive days for nonconforming USES (renovation tolls the clock only with approvals); 30-7.C.2: nonconforming STRUCTURES with a conforming use have no clock outside the NPO district; 30-7.A.5: change of ownership does not end a nonconformity; 9/24 CASUALTY ROUTING (Article 30-7 read in full): 30-7.C.1 sends a nonconforming STRUCTURE with a conforming USE to 30-7.C, whose C.5 rule restores >50% damage only in conformity (no multifamily exception); 30-7.B.8.a.3-4 (rebuild to prior density; duplex named; permit 6 months, start 12, up to 36 with the City Manager; Article 30-5 and buffers first) sits under Nonconforming USES and B.8.a.1 covers 'a structure housing any nonconforming use' - since Ord. S2025-008 made two-family P in SF-6, density-nonconforming duplexes need a broad city reading to reach B.8.a.3 (P 0.35); one Development Services determination covers Rhew, Edgar, Nickey, Squirrel, Varsity and Pecan; 30-5.A.4 requires 2 spaces per unit on any rebuild and 30-5.A.5.a requires existing two- to four-family parking to sit in a vehicular use area","HB 765 'Save the American Dream Act' (would have required duplex/triplex/quad by right in residential zones of cities of 125,000 or more, effective 1/1/2026) is STUCK: last action 5/6/2025, re-referred to House Finance. SB 205 (housing regulatory reform): last action 6/11/2025, re-referred to House Rules. No NC preemption enacted (UNC SOG bulletin PZLB 36 on 2025 planning legislation: zero duplex hits)","$1,251 (Fayetteville HMFA); 1BR $1,113; FY2027 (effective 10/1/2026): Fayetteville HMFA 0/1/2/3/4 BR $1,302 / $1,334 / $1,476 / $1,937 / $2,380; SAFMR 2BR 28301 $1,250, 28303 $1,470, 28304 $1,710, 28311 $1,500, 28390 $1,320; NOT a mandatory SAFMR metro; FMHA payment standard unpublished","none checked; HUD CHOICE NEIGHBORHOODS: Murchison Choice planning area = tracts 10 and 11 (bounded by Pamalee Dr / Greensboro Rd NW, Cross Creek E, Edgecombe Rd / Filter Plant Dr S, Little Cross Creek W); $25,115,578 FY2025 CNI Implementation Grant announced 9/2/2026; 60 + 110 public-housing units replaced, 323 apartments + 35 homes, construction late 2027 over eight years, relocation by transfer or VOUCHER; rows 11 Edgar and w2 Nickey are inside tract 11","0 Rhew, 13 Rogers, 11 Edgar, w2 Nickey, 6/4/5 Squirrel, 26 Pecan, 14 Varsity, 9 Scarborough (Spring Lake); 9/19: 6/4/5 + w4 (429) Squirrel zoning -> PASS with density nonconformity; 417 one-household fee roll 2023-2026; 9/20: 2026 fee stack applied to 0 Rhew, 13 Rogers, 11 Edgar, w2 Nickey, 14 Varsity, 26 Pecan, r4d Tamarack; 9 Scarborough (Spring Lake) billed at county 0.4990 + town 0.7410 + recreation 0.0500 with town sanitation off the county bill; 9/23: 14 Varsity rebased (advisory 42), 13 Rogers and 26 Pecan photo-read, FY2027 FMR/SAFMR on all Fayetteville rows; 9/23 evening: 13 Rogers rebased (advisory 43); next revaluation 2031 applied to every Cumberland row; 9/24: 26 Pecan rebased (advisory 44); casualty routing reading applies to 0 Rhew, 11 Edgar, w2 Nickey, 6/4/5/w4 Squirrel, 14 Varsity; 9/24 evening: r4d Tamarack rebased (advisory 45); stormwater tier rule applies to every Fayetteville row's fee line; the bill-payer rule applies to every Cumberland row",2026-09-24,https://www.ncleg.gov/BillLookUp/2025/H765; https://www.ncleg.gov/BillLookUp/2025/S205; https://www.fayettevillenc.gov/Media-Releases/Council-adopts-FY-2027-Budget-No-tax-increases; https://online.encodeplus.com/regs/fayetteville-nc/doc-view.aspx?secid=9434; https://online.encodeplus.com/regs/fayetteville-nc/doclibrary.aspx?id=e4fbed26-0830-47b5-a01b-2fd26b2464f5; https://taxpwa.co.cumberland.nc.us/PublicWebAccess/; https:/