Pinetops / Edgecombe,NC,"county $0.89 + Town $0.58 = $1.47 per $100 (FY2024-25 through FY2026-27); Town 0.46 in FY2022-23, 0.58 from FY2023-24 and held through the 2024 reappraisal (county 0.95 -> 0.89); NO county solid-waste fee inside the Town (the $150 fee bills unincorporated residents and Leggett); the county collects the Town's tax (tax code C03); 2026 bills levied 9/1, interest from 1/6/2027","NCDOR 2022-23, 2023-24, 2024-25 workbooks; Town FY27 budget ordinance DOC004; WebPAAS bill 26A470433368300 ($419.35 on $28,527)","county reappraisal effective 1/1/2024 (notices 2/2024), eight-year cycle, next 2032; non-reappraisal-year changes for physical improvements under G.S. 105-287(a)(2b) at the 2024 schedule of values; the WebPAAS card's 'Date Last Appraised' field is stale","NO (G.S. 160D-1207); the county Inspections Office 're-inspects vacant buildings' and issues building permits for Pinetops (252-641-7808, permit@edgecombeco.com); Town minimum-housing/demolition ordinances used on S Second St (205, 512, 309) with demolition costs as a tax lien reaching the owner's other property within the Town or one mile","n/a. Instruments: NC OneMap parcels (owner names; county layer 10 was empty 9/25); Edgecombe WebPAAS taxpa.edgecombecountync.gov (POST search by PIN ####-##-####-##, then ?DEST=pDetail with pKEY, then pBLDG/pLAND/pCOLL with txtPIN: card, land, 20-year bill list); Cott ROD eSearch guest (index; images via the HTML5 viewer); county 'Delinquent Tax Listings' PDF; county E911 address points layer 5; Pinetops zoning layer 17 (pre-2021 names); Town documents at townofpinetopsnc.com/documents/288/; EPA ECHO DFR and effluent chart for NC0020435; DWR moratorium list; DEQ distressed lists; Google photometa/streetviewpixels for dated Street View",n/a,Town completed its service-line inventory (2025 CCR: 'prepared an inventory of all service lines ... visit the Town Hall to request a copy'); four groundwater wells,"Town Hall, 101 E Hamlet St, 252-827-4435 (copy on request)","Town Zoning Ordinance Revised 2021 (NCGS 160D amendment adopted 6/1/2021; 'does not affect the zoning of any property'); districts A-1, AR, R-30, R-20, R-20MH, R-12, R-10MH, R-7, RMF, B-1, B-2, B-3, O-I, LI; the county-hosted layer 17 still uses AR-20, RMH-7, R-7, R-12, B-1, B-2, B-3, M-1; the Town's posted map is a 2022 'Proposed Zoning' scan; the Town called M-1 'Light Industrial' in its 11/17/2022 planning agenda; zoning permit $25, required for accessory structures, additions and new homes, NOT for interior repairs (Town FAQ)","Two-Family Dwelling P by zoning permit in R-30, R-12, R-10MH, R-7, RMF and O-I; not permitted in LI, B-1, B-2, B-3, A-1, AR, R-20, R-20MH; duplex minimum lot 15,000 sf / 85 ft (R-7, RMF), 18,000 / 95 (R-10MH), 20,000 / 100 (R-12), 40,000 / 120 (R-30); two-family side yards 15-20 ft; a 50 x 150 in-town lot is nonconforming for a duplex everywhere","Article VIII 70.05.A.3 and 70.06.A.6: a nonconforming use that ceases by vacancy or non-use for more than 180 continuous days may resume only in conformity (the lot judged as a whole; one empty apartment does not end the right); 70.05.A.2 no increase in units; 70.06.A.2 major repair, reconstruction or damage above 60% of tax value rebuilds only in conformity (repairs within 12 months, complete in two years); 70.06.A.5 the Board may approve restoring an 'existing and occupied' one- or two-family residence damaged by fire or other causes, on the same footprint if on a nonconforming lot; 70.08 protects work under a building permit issued before an amendment. STATE: G.S. 160D-108(d) 24-month discontinuance applies to statutory vesting from a development permit, not to this common-law clock; 160D-108(h) written vested-rights determination with de novo appeal; S.L. 2025-94 s.29 (10/6/2025) rewrote 160D-108(c)","H765 'Save the American Dream Act' (would enact 160D-108.2: nonconformities protected from local amendments, reconstruction by right, inconsistent ordinances void from 10/1/2025) stuck in House Finance since 5/6/2025, no 2026 action; S.L. 2025-94 s.29 enacted only the vested-rights clarification","Rocky Mount MSA FY2026 2BR $1,143 (1BR $918); SAFMR 27864 1BR $860; FY2027 2BR $1,167, 1BR $972, SAFMR 27864 2BR $1,130 (not a mandatory SAFMR metro)","Pinetops WWTP NC0020435 (0.3 MGD): DWR '90% Rule imposed' 5/19/2021 (15A NCAC 02T .0118: no sewer-line extension permits until expansion plans are filed; not a statutory moratorium), Town letter to DEQ 8/2026 to lift it; flows 48% of permit in 2025; ECHO: 7 state penalties since 11/2021 ($4,779), NOVs 10/2024-6/2026, fecal coliform 525% over limit Q3 2025, BOD 41% Q2 2026, 4 of 12 quarters in noncompliance. DEQ distressed unit (list 2/16/2026, score 7); not on the FY2024 UAL; electric fund transfers $312,924 to the general fund (22.6%). Utilities: water 14.17 + 4.22-4.60, sewer 28.85 + 8.29-8.75 (+19% since 2023), storm 2, sanitation 25/account, electric 15.49 + 0.1542/kWh (from Wilson wholesale), taps 1,350/1,000, rental meter deposit 475 (FY27). Flood: Zone X at the subject; Hurricane Matthew 2016 modelled flooding along the creek corridor about 1 km SE and near the WWTP; 200+ rescued in the Pinetops area 10/9/2016. Legacy ECHO registrations on E Cobb St (advisory 50, not re-verified)","r10a 610-612 S 2nd St (file 40, 9/25/2026)",2026-09-25,https://townofpinetopsnc.com/documents/288/ARTICLE_8_-_NONCONFORMING_SITUATIONS.pdf; https://townofpinetopsnc.com/documents/288/ARTICLE_4_-_Dimen._Standards.pdf; https://townofpinetopsnc.com/documents/288/Table_of_Uses_final_revisions__revised.pdf; https://townofpinetopsnc.com/documents/288/ARTICLE_10_Administration.pdf; https://townofpinetopsnc.com/documents/288/ZONINGMAP.pdf; https://townofpinetopsnc.com/building-permits-and-inspections; https://townofpinetopsnc.com/documents/288/DOC004.pdf; https://townofpinetopsnc.com/documents/288/Water_Rates.pdf; https://townofpinetopsnc.com/documents/288/Electric_Rates.pdf; https://townofpinetopsnc.com/documents/288/JUNE1MINUTES__1_.pdf; https://townofpinetopsnc.com/documents/288/November_4_2025_minutes.pdf; https://townofpinetopsnc.com/documents/288/August_4__2026_Agenda_Packet.pdf; https://townofpinetopsnc.com/documents/288/Pinetops_2025_CCR.pdf; https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_160D/GS_160D-108.html; https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/SessionLaws/PDF/2025-2026/SL2025-94.pdf; https://www.ncleg.gov/BillLookUp/2025/H765; https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_105/GS_105-287.html; https://www.deq.nc.gov/water-resources/nc-dwr-moratorium-list/open; https://deq.nc.gov/water-infrastructure/distressed-list-website-2-16-2026/download?attachment=; https://echodata.epa.gov/echo/dfr_rest_services.get_dfr?p_id=NC0020435; https://echodata.epa.gov/echo/eff_rest_services.get_effluent_chart?p_id=NC0020435&parameter_code=50050; http://reports.oah.state.nc.us/ncac/title%2015a%20-%20environmental%20quality/chapter%2002%20-%20environmental%20management/subchapter%20t/15a%20ncac%2002t%20.0118.pdf; https://taxpa.edgecombecountync.gov/paas/; https://cotthosting.com/ncedgecombeexternal/User/Login.aspx; https://www.edgecombecountync.gov/news_detail_T5_R366.php; https://www.edgecombecountync.gov/departments/solid_waste_landfill/solid_waste_permits.php; https://www.ncdor.gov/2024-2025taxratesxlsx/open; https://www.ncdor.gov/2023-24-tax-ratesxlsx/open; https://www.ncdor.gov/2022-23taxratesxlsx/open; https://services.nconemap.gov/secure/rest/services/NC1Map_Parcels/MapServer/1; https://services.nconemap.gov/secure/rest/services/Matthew_Flood_Extent/ImageServer; https://gis.edgecombecountync.gov/arcgis/rest/services/webmap/MapServer/17
Spring Lake / Cumberland,NC,"county $0.499 + Town $0.741 + recreation district $0.05 = $1.29 per $100 of the county's sales-comparison value (2025 and 2026 bills; the Town kept 0.741 for FY2027 by the schedule adopted 6/22/2026 against a 48.79-cent revenue-neutral rate after the 2025 revaluation; FY2025 had raised it 9.1 cents; highest municipal rate in the county) PLUS Town fees on the same county bill: SPRING LAKE 3000 REFUSE TAX = solid waste availability $32 + litter $1 a month = $396 per residential unit per year ($792 for a duplex; $614 through 2023) and RES STORM WATER $5 per ERU a month = $60 a parcel; 2026 bills due 9/1, interest from 1/6/2027; the county collects for the Town","Cumberland BillDetails 2021-2026 for PIN 0501-55-7750; TOSL FY2026-2027 Rate and Fee Schedule (adopted 6/22/2026, amended 8/18/2026) pp. 1-3; FY2026 adopted budget message","Cumberland: last 2025, next 2031 (BOC resolution 3/2/2026); sector 4076MF (Spring Lake multi-family) values 47 of 53 parcels by sales comparison at a factor on cost with median 1.873 (min 0.354, max 4.689); no income values in the sector; G.S. 105-287 lets the assessor pick up the 2023-24 work in a non-reappraisal year (effective year still 1946)","NO periodic program found (G.S. 160D-1207); minimum-housing code enforced through the Code Enforcement Inspector (in the Police Department; Minimum Housing Appeals Board exists); FY2026 budget added a $96,000 code enforcement officer and filled the building inspector post 'to focus on blight and minimum housing'; Town Inspections Department issues ALL building permits inside the Town (CivicPlus Community Development portal civicgov4.com/nc_springlake; 910-985-7265); the county's EnerGov/permit/code layers do not cover the Town; G.S. 160D-1110(c)'s $40,000 exemption names single-family residences only, so duplex roof, HVAC and electrical work needs a Town permit (renovation fee $120 to $10,000, $145 to $20,000, $180 to $50,000; zoning permit $60 per building; zoning verification letter $30)","n/a. Instruments: county parcel layer (ZONING field 'R6-RESIDENTIAL DIST', VCS 4076MF, CITY_LIMITS SPRING LAKE); county CCZoning layer 1 (Jurisdiction 'Spring Lake', CASE_NO); camapwa cards by PARCEL_PK (BuildingDetails needs &BldgCardNum=1&SectionNum=1; DeedDetails carries stamps and prices back to 1991); taxpwa BillDetails (refuse and stormwater lines carry no rate column: reconcile to Total Billed); E911 layer (ONE point typed APT per duplex in Spring Lake: 205, 208, 306, 310; two points only for the four-unit 112/114); Register of Deeds ccrodinternet.org (Full System, Human radio; Directory link off-canvas: click through javascript_tool; Index Detail from a screenshot); Town documents at townofspringlake.com/rates/ (FY2027 schedule PDF with text; earlier fee sheets image-only), /inspections-department/, /general-public-works/ (CCRs 2014-2025, WWTP reports 2014-2025); JPB packets at cumberlandcountync.gov (case P07-03 2/6/2007); Google photometa/streetviewpixels for dated frames (2007, 2012, 2022, 2024 on Scarborough St)",n/a,"Town completed its service-line inventory (2025 CCR: 'prepared an inventory of all service lines ... To access this inventory, please email townmanager@townofspringlake.com'); water is surface water purchased from Fayetteville PWC and Harnett Regional Water; 2025 CCR reports a Disinfection Byproducts monitoring-and-reporting violation for 11/2025","email townmanager@townofspringlake.com (copy on request); Town Hall 300 Ruth St, 910-605-1634; Water Department 910-703-8912","Spring Lake Code of Ordinances Chapter 42 Zoning (Municode, through 8/2025; Ord. (2021)1 of 6-28-2021 was the 160D conformity amendment), administered by Cumberland County Planning (CAMA 'Planning Jurisdiction COUNTY'; Town has no planning staff); 18 districts in Article II (RR, R-15, R-10, R-6A, R-6, R-5A, R-5, PND, O&I, HS(P), C(P), C-1, C-3, CB, M(P), M-1(P), M-2, CD); no MCO or military corridor overlay in the ordinance, the county overlay layer or the county's 2021 ordinance (Redfin's 'MCO' panel is unsupported); the R6 on Scarborough St dates from case P07-03 (2/2007), a Town-initiated rezoning of 145 parcels from R6A and R6/MHO after the R6/MHO text was repealed 4/10/2006","Sec. 42-35(1)(e) R-6 'designed for a mix of single- and multi-family dwellings'; Sec. 42-63.3 use matrix 'Dwelling, single & multiple-family' = P in R-6 and R-6A (no separate two-family row); Sec. 42-192 R-6 minimum lot: 6,000 sf for the first dwelling unit, 5,000 sf for each of the second and third, 5,000 for four and more; frontage 60 ft; front 25 ft from the right-of-way; side 10 ft (one story) / 12 (two); rear 30 ft. A duplex therefore needs 11,000 sf and 60 ft; Scarborough St lots of the 1946 R G Creech plat run about 5,700-6,500 sf and 50 ft, so every duplex on them is DENSITY-NONCONFORMING (208 and 302 Scarborough). Sec. 42-190(4) lets a short lot of record be built on only 'as a building site for a single-family residence' (within 17 percent); 42-190(1) one main residential building per lot; 42-190(3) contiguous lots in common ownership are combined","Sec. 42-112(f): resumption of a nonconforming use barred after discontinuance 'regardless of intent, for a continuous period of one year'; 42-112(e): a damaged nonconforming structure 'may be reconstructed and used as before if it is done within one year of such damage' unless damage exceeds '50 percent of its then reproducible value or its bulk, exclusive of foundations', after which repair, reconstruction or use must conform; 42-112(d): a nonconforming structure 'remodeled or rebuilt to an extent exceeding one-third of its then reproducible value, as determined by the administrative officer' must be brought into conformity with the district's dimensional requirements; 42-112(c) no change to another nonconforming use; 42-112(a) no extension or value enhancement except as provided; no change-of-ownership clause. County RCN for 208 Scarborough 86,448 (one-third 28,816; half 43,224). STATE: G.S. 160D-108(d) 24-month clause covers permit-created statutory vesting only; 160D-108(h) written determination (de novo appeal) is the instrument; H765 stuck in House Finance since 5/6/2025",as for Fayetteville / Cumberland: no NC duplex preemption enacted (H765 and S205 dead in committee); S.L. 2025-94 s.29 vested-rights clarification only,"Fayetteville HMFA FY2026 2BR $1,251 (1BR $1,113); FY2027 (10/1/2026) 0/1/2/3/4 BR $1,302 / $1,334 / $1,476 / $1,937 / $2,380; SAFMR 28390 FY2027 0/1/2/3 BR $1,140 / $1,150 / $1,320 / $1,780 (not a mandatory SAFMR metro; FMHA payment standard unpublished; rent reasonableness caps a voucher rent at unassisted comps)","TOWN FINANCES: LGC impounded the books 10/5/2021 (former finance director wrote 500,000+ in personal checks; unapproved 1 million loan) and returned control effective 8/1/2024 (vote 7/9-10/2024); on the LGC Unit Assistance List (10/6/2025 list, FY2024 data); LGC withheld $37,500 of sales tax 9/9/2025 for the missing FY2022-2024 audits (FY2022 to Cherry Bekaert due 2/28/2026, FY2023-2025 contracted to Carr Riggs & Ingram; filing unverified 9/25/2026); unrestricted general-fund balance about 8 percent vs a 35 percent policy (FY2026 message); sales-tax share halved by the county's 7/1/2025 ad valorem switch; interim/new town manager in 2026. UTILITY: DEQ/SWIA and LGC DISTRESSED designation for water and sewer as of 2/4/2026 (assessment scores 10 / 5b / 2b / 2b / 1b, b = missing audit data; VUR-eligible; $1.5M grant + $3.4M loans 7/2026); water and sewer +17 percent 1/1/2025, FY2027 retail rates unchanged: minimum $10.64 water + $20.23 sewer = $30.87 at 0 gal, $86.37 at 3,000 gal, $127.95 at 5,000 gal ('average'), $242.14 at 10,000; deposits $200 (owner or renter) + $20 account fee; late fee $25 after the 18th, cut-off after the 25th; system development fees $1.89/$4.58 per gpd on new connections from 7/1/2026. WWTP NC0030970 (350 Harps St, Little River): MAJOR NPDES permit, 1.5 MGD, expires 5/31/2028; 2025 flow 0.880 MGD (59 percent); ECHO 8 of 12 quarters with a violation identified (none significant), state NOVs 1/9/2024, 6/4/2024, 7/2/2024, 9/30/2025, no penalties; 4 sanitary sewer overflows in 2025; NOT on the DWR moratorium list. Water purchased from PWC and Harnett Regional Water; DBP monitoring violation 11/2025. Flood: Zone X at 208 Scarborough. Fort Bragg Special Interest Area (county notification layer)","9 Scarborough (file 41, 9/25/2026): tax lines, density rule, fee schedule, utility rates, finances; the 35a/40a 'no solid-waste or stormwater lines' text is withdrawn",2026-09-25,https://www.townofspringlake.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/TOSL-Rate-Fee-Schedule-FY2027-Amended-8-18-26.pdf; https://www.townofspringlake.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/WATER-SEWER-RATE-FEE-SCHEDULE.pdf; https://www.townofspringlake.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/FY25-26-TOSL-Budget-Adopted-6-23-25-Amended-8-11-25.pdf; https://www.townofspringlake.com/rates/; https://www.townofspringlake.com/inspections-department/; https://www.civicgov4.com/nc_springlake/portal/index.php; https://www.townofspringlake.com/general-public-works/; https://www.townofspringlake.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2025-Spring-Lake-CCR-Water-Quality-Report.pdf; https://www.townofspringlake.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/2025-WWTP-Annual-Performance-Report.pdf; https://www.zoneomics.com/code/spring-lake-NC/chapter_2; https://www.zoneomics.com/code/spring-lake-NC/chapter_3; https://www.zoneomics.com/code/spring-lake-NC/chapter_5; https://www.zoneomics.com/code/spring-lake-NC/chapter_8; https://library.municode.com/nc/spring_lake/codes/code_of_ordinances?nodeId=PTIICOOR_CH42ZO; https://cumberlandcountync.gov/CustomUserControls/Planning/Documents/JPB/packets/2007/February/PBWEB-02-06-07.pdf; https://www.cumberlandcountync.gov/docs/default-source/planning-documents/ordinances/county/completed/county-zoning-ordinance__03-15-2021.pdf; https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_160D/G