Fayetteville / Cumberland,NC,"county $0.499 + city $0.4495 = $0.9485 per $100 of the county's sales-comparison value (unchanged on the 2026 bills, verified 9/19) PLUS owner-billed fees on the same bill: county household solid-waste fee $130 per dwelling unit (FY2025 and FY2026 schedules), city solid-waste fee $285 per dwelling unit for FY2027 ($275 FY2026), city stormwater $84 per parcel; a duplex pays $914 of fees on the 2026 bill; 9/23: Cumberland INFORMAL appeals for tax year 2027 are open now with a 2/5/2027 deadline (decisions ~April 2027; on-site appraiser review); the 2026 window closed 5/20/2026; sales-comparison values are the county cost value times a per-sector factor (0329MF 2.07, 0055MF 2.985), so appeals need a record error, not a market argument (G.S. 105-287); 9/23 evening: A101 income values are a sector MODEL (VCS 6033: '1 BEDROOM UNITS' $5,520/yr and '2 BEDROOM UNITS' $6,000/yr per unit, 5% vacancy, 40% expenses, 10.499% overall rate) - re-running the model at market rents at the 2031 revaluation roughly doubles a duplex's value ($62,500 -> ~$115,000); 9/24 evening CORRECTION: the city stormwater fee is NOT $84 per parcel - FY2027 residential parcels are tiered by impervious building area (tier 1 <2,500 sf $84/yr, tier 2 2,501-4,800 sf $168/yr, tier 3 >4,800 sf $252/yr; 77/22/1% of parcels); a 1,896 sf duplex with patios and pads (741 Tamarack) bills $168, a 928 sf duplex (2614 Pecan) $84; read the line from each bill","Cumberland bill details (BillDetails.aspx) for the four Squirrel parcels, 2023-2026; county solid-waste fee schedules FY25/FY26; cityviewnc 5/13/2025 (FY2026 fees); city Trash & Recycling page (FY2027)","county cycle SHORTENED: last 2025, NEXT 2031 (Board of Commissioners resolution 3/2/2026: six-year cycle, then possibly four-year with 2035; CityView 3/3/2026); the '2033' carried since file 29a is stale; NC does not reassess on sale","NO (G.S. 160D-1207 bars periodic rental inspections absent cause); RENTAL ACTION MANAGEMENT PROGRAM (RAMP), City Code Ch. 14 Secs. 14-95 to 14-113 (Ord. S2012-003 eff. 7/1/2012): registration after 3+ verified violations in 12 months (14-97) or a disorder-activity count at or above the 90th-percentile threshold (14-101; windows set 1/1 and 7/1 from the prior six months, Appendix A point weights); mandatory meeting, remedial action plan, six-month reviews, revocation, nuisance referral; a registered seller must report the purchaser within 30 days; fee $500 (FY25 fee schedule), civil penalty $50/$100/$500 per day; state ceiling G.S. 160D-1207(c) (top 10% or >4 violations, $500 cap); ask RAMP status for every Fayetteville row","n/a for rental inspection. Instruments: parcels gis.co.cumberland.nc.us/server/rest/services/Tax/Parcels/MapServer/0 (OWNER, VCS sector, CONDITION class A/F/P/U + % depreciation, REVENUE_STAMPS); bills taxpwa.co.cumberland.nc.us/PublicWebAccess/BillSearchResults.aspx?ParcelNum=<PIN> then BillDetails.aspx?BillPk= (itemized fees, lender tax-service flag, payer names); police incidents gismaps.fayettevillenc.gov/cofopendatagis (Persons/Property/Society layers, 2010-present, address LIKE and 400 m buffer); zoning gismaps.fayettevillenc.gov/cofopendatagis/rest/services/DevelopmentServices/Zoning/MapServer/0; residential renovation permits: NOT in the county EnerGov layer or the city open-data permits layer; IDT Plans portal (login) or Development Services 910-433-1329; 9/23 evening: COUNTY CAMA CARDS serve to plain curl at taxpwa.co.cumberland.nc.us/camapwa/ (PropertySummary / BuildingDetails / IncomeDetails?VCS= / SaleDetails?VCS= / LandDetails / OutbuildingDetails / DeedDetails / DocumentDetails .aspx?PARCELPK=<PARCEL_PK from the parcel layer>): deed chains with stamps and instrument types, building cards with bedrooms/baths/exterior/depreciation, and the INCOME MODEL behind every A101 value (unit types, rent per unit, expense ratio, overall rate); PWC lead-service-line dashboard pws-ptd.120wateraudit.com/fayettevillepwc (browser only; two-entry addresses suggest two service records); 9/24: COUNTY E911 ADDRESS POINTS gis.co.cumberland.nc.us/server/rest/services/E911/Addresses/MapServer/0 (ADDRESS, TYPE APT/HOM, PIN, LM_NAME, OLD_ADD) - a second unit address typed APT on the parcel's PIN is documentary two-unit evidence for the 30-7.A.3 burden; PWC 120Water GraphQL counts per address (one asset per metered service: 2614 Pecan one, 2604 and 2703 Pecan two each); county Inspections/CodeEnforcementComplaints and Planning/Permits layers are COUNTY jurisdiction only (0 hits inside the city); Imagery/CC1968 and CC2023 export without a token, CC1982-CC2021 need one; the county's 'Advertisement of Unpaid Real Estate Taxes' PDFs (cumberlandcountync.gov/docs/default-source/tax-documents/delinquent-taxes/delinquent-taxes__<year>.pdf) list parcel, owner and amount by street; the city's official Local Historic Districts map (9/2014 PDF on the Historic Preservation page) is the HLO instrument the zoning layer lacks; the 2025 Schedule of Values PDF (9.5 MB) carries the exterior-wall code key (03 = MAS/ABST/OLD WOOD) but no heating key in its text layer; 9/24 evening: BILL PAYER COLUMN - read the 'Paid By' of every prior bill, not only the status: 'DAVID B CRAIG, ATTORNEY' = the county's tax-foreclosure attorney (davidbcraig.com: 'represents the County of Cumberland in the tax foreclosure matters'; payoffs by certified funds only) so the year was redeemed out of a foreclosure file; a servicer/CoreLogic payment after the interest date = escrow advance; 'YYYY - 700/850' = escrow batch on time. COUNTY OWNER LIKE query for an individual seller lists their other parcels; their bills show whether the default is portfolio-wide. The 2024 and 2025 advertisements live at cumberlandcountync.gov/docs/default-source/tax-documents/delinquent-taxes/delinquent_taxes__YYYY.pdf (underscore pattern; the 2023 file uses the hyphen pattern with ?sfvrsn=782cbf11_2). ROD: the Full System name search reaches deeds of trust and their note amounts; the row's 'Image - N page(s)' button then 'Open in new tab' yields PDFs/User_0_<timestamp>.pdf, which curl fetches (image-only; PyMuPDF) - fetching it ends the browser session. PWC 120Water per-address asset counts (741 and 745 Tamarack one each = per-unit meters). Trulia unit records ('741 Tamarack Dr #A') and a property's second Zillow zpid carry the owner's earlier rent asks and listing texts",n/a,PWC 'Operation Clean & Clear' inventory (lookup not scriptable; the Cumberland GIS viewer has no service-line layer),https://www.faypwc.com/operation-clean-clear/,"UDO Chapter 30 (2011) in force on enCodePlus; Table 30-4.A.2 Use Table amended by Ord. S2024-017B (10/28/2024, retail rows), S2025-008 (4/14/2025: two- to four-family SF-6 cell changed S -> P) and S2026-015 (5/26/2026, MAC column); read the use table at doc-view.aspx?secid=9434 (server-rendered), not doc-viewer.aspx; ordinance PDFs at doclibrary.aspx?id= are image-only; 9/20: overlays - the zoning layer encodes /MHO and /CZ suffixes only; 'NPO' = Noise-Accident Potential Overlay (airport/military), NOT neighborhood preservation; Murchison Road Corridor Overlay (MCO, 30-3.H.8) and the NCO district-specific standards (30-3.H.9.e) are '[Placeholder]' sections with no adopted text; historic overlays (HLO) are not in the layer","CORRECTED 9/19: 'Dwelling, two- to four-family' is P (permitted by right) in SF-6, SF-10 and MR-5 and S in SF-15 since Ord. S2025-008 of 4/14/2025 (the 3/26/2024 Stamper Rd SUP predates it). Dimensional: SF-6 needs 6,000 sf of lot area PER UNIT (12,000 sf for a duplex) and 60 ft of width, so 1960s duplexes on 6,970 sf lots are nonconforming as to density (30-7.C structure rules, no discontinuance clock outside the NPO overlay; >50% casualty rebuild must conform per 30-7.C.5 unless 30-7.B.8(3) is applied). Design standards 30-4.C.2.a.2 apply to new two- to four-family; 9/23 CORRECTION: lot area PER UNIT for two- to four-family is 7,500 sf in SF-10 (duplex 15,000 sf, width 75 ft, coverage 30%, setbacks 30/10/35) and 6,000 sf in SF-6 (12,000) per the 30-3.D.3 and 30-3.D.4 tables; SF-15 lists 15,000 (single-family column; two- to four-family is S there); MR-5 reads '5,000 for 1st unit, then 4,000' - read at the ordinance before use; 814 Varsity (SF-10, GIS 14,584 sf) sits on the line and its plat (PB 18 PG 44) is unread","30-7.B.5: 365 consecutive days for nonconforming USES (renovation tolls the clock only with approvals); 30-7.C.2: nonconforming STRUCTURES with a conforming use have no clock outside the NPO district; 30-7.A.5: change of ownership does not end a nonconformity; 9/24 CASUALTY ROUTING (Article 30-7 read in full): 30-7.C.1 sends a nonconforming STRUCTURE with a conforming USE to 30-7.C, whose C.5 rule restores >50% damage only in conformity (no multifamily exception); 30-7.B.8.a.3-4 (rebuild to prior density; duplex named; permit 6 months, start 12, up to 36 with the City Manager; Article 30-5 and buffers first) sits under Nonconforming USES and B.8.a.1 covers 'a structure housing any nonconforming use' - since Ord. S2025-008 made two-family P in SF-6, density-nonconforming duplexes need a broad city reading to reach B.8.a.3 (P 0.35); one Development Services determination covers Rhew, Edgar, Nickey, Squirrel, Varsity and Pecan; 30-5.A.4 requires 2 spaces per unit on any rebuild and 30-5.A.5.a requires existing two- to four-family parking to sit in a vehicular use area","HB 765 'Save the American Dream Act' (would have required duplex/triplex/quad by right in residential zones of cities of 125,000 or more, effective 1/1/2026) is STUCK: last action 5/6/2025, re-referred to House Finance. SB 205 (housing regulatory reform): last action 6/11/2025, re-referred to House Rules. No NC preemption enacted (UNC SOG bulletin PZLB 36 on 2025 planning legislation: zero duplex hits)","$1,251 (Fayetteville HMFA); 1BR $1,113; FY2027 (effective 10/1/2026): Fayetteville HMFA 0/1/2/3/4 BR $1,302 / $1,334 / $1,476 / $1,937 / $2,380; SAFMR 2BR 28301 $1,250, 28303 $1,470, 28304 $1,710, 28311 $1,500, 28390 $1,320; NOT a mandatory SAFMR metro; FMHA payment standard unpublished","none checked; HUD CHOICE NEIGHBORHOODS: Murchison Choice planning area = tracts 10 and 11 (bounded by Pamalee Dr / Greensboro Rd NW, Cross Creek E, Edgecombe Rd / Filter Plant Dr S, Little Cross Creek W); $25,115,578 FY2025 CNI Implementation Grant announced 9/2/2026; 60 + 110 public-housing units replaced, 323 apartments + 35 homes, construction late 2027 over eight years, relocation by transfer or VOUCHER; rows 11 Edgar and w2 Nickey are inside tract 11","0 Rhew, 13 Rogers, 11 Edgar, w2 Nickey, 6/4/5 Squirrel, 26 Pecan, 14 Varsity, 9 Scarborough (Spring Lake); 9/19: 6/4/5 + w4 (429) Squirrel zoning -> PASS with density nonconformity; 417 one-household fee roll 2023-2026; 9/20: 2026 fee stack applied to 0 Rhew, 13 Rogers, 11 Edgar, w2 Nickey, 14 Varsity, 26 Pecan, r4d Tamarack; 9 Scarborough (Spring Lake) billed at county 0.4990 + town 0.7410 + recreation 0.0500 with town sanitation off the county bill; 9/23: 14 Varsity rebased (advisory 42), 13 Rogers and 26 Pecan photo-read, FY2027 FMR/SAFMR on all Fayetteville rows; 9/23 evening: 13 Rogers rebased (advisory 43); next revaluation 2031 applied to every Cumberland row; 9/24: 26 Pecan rebased (advisory 44); casualty routing reading applies to 0 Rhew, 11 Edgar, w2 Nickey, 6/4/5/w4 Squirrel, 14 Varsity; 9/24 evening: r4d Tamarack rebased (advisory 45); stormwater tier rule applies to every Fayetteville row's fee line; the bill-payer rule applies to every Cumberland row",2026-09-24,https://www.ncleg.gov/BillLookUp/2025/H765; https://www.ncleg.gov/BillLookUp/2025/S205; https://www.fayettevillenc.gov/Media-Releases/Council-adopts-FY-2027-Budget-No-tax-increases; https://online.encodeplus.com/regs/fayetteville-nc/doc-view.aspx?secid=9434; https://online.encodeplus.com/regs/fayetteville-nc/doclibrary.aspx?id=e4fbed26-0830-47b5-a01b-2fd26b2464f5; https://taxpwa.co.cumberland.nc.us/PublicWebAccess/; https://www.cumberlandcountync.gov/docs/default-source/solid-waste-documents/fee-schedules/solid-waste-fees-fy26.pdf; https://www.fayettevillenc.gov/files/content/main/v/17/city-departments/economic-community-development/murchison-choice-neighborhood-initiative/murchison-choice-neighborhoods-transformation-plan.pdf; https://www.murchisonchoice.com/s/2022-Murchison-CN-Plan-Housing-Market-Analysis.pdf; https://www.law.cornell.edu/cfr/text/40/745.83; https://online.encodeplus.com/regs/fayetteville-nc/doc-view.aspx?secid=9381; https://online.encodeplus.com/regs/fayetteville-nc/doc-view.aspx?secid=4; https://www.fayettevillenc.gov/files/sharedassets/main/v/1/development-services/documents/guidance-documents/city-fee-schedule-fy25.pdf; https://www.cumberlandcountync.gov/departments/tax-group/tax/real-estate-gis-mapping/real-property-value-and-appeal; https://www.huduser.gov/portal/datasets/fmr/fmr2027/FY27_FMRs.xlsx; https://www.cityviewnc.com/stories/county-to-appraise-property-every-6-years/; https://taxpwa.co.cumberland.nc.us/camapwa/; https://www.faypwc.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/Service-Regulations-and-Charges-Revised-5.1.24-Final.pdf; https://pws-ptd.120wateraudit.com/fayettevillepwc; https://gis.co.cumberland.nc.us/server/rest/services/E911/Addresses/MapServer/0; https://online.encodeplus.com/regs/fayetteville-nc/export2doc.aspx?pdf=1&tocid=005.030.007; https://online.encodeplus.com/regs/fayetteville-nc/export2doc.aspx?pdf=1&tocid=005.030.005; https://www.fayettevillenc.gov/files/sharedassets/main/v/1/development-services/documents/historic-properties/historic-districts-map.pdf; https://www.cumberlandcountync.gov/docs/default-source/tax-documents/delinquent-taxes/delinquent-taxes__2023.pdf; https://www.cumberlandcountync.gov/docs/default-source/tax-documents/2025-revaluation/2025-sov-draft.pdf; https://www.faypwc.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/R.C.1-Res-Water-Svc-Inside-City-5.1.26.pdf; https://www.faypwc.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/R.D.1-Res-SS-Svc-Inside-City-5.1.25.pdf; https://www.fayettevillenc.gov/City-Departments/Public-Services/Stormwater/Stormwater-Utility-Fee-Structure-Updates; http://www.davidbcraig.com/; https://www.cumberlandcountync.gov/docs/default-source/tax-documents/delinquent-taxes/delinquent_taxes__2024.pdf; https://www.cumberlandcountync.gov/docs/default-source/tax-documents/delinquent-taxes/delinquent_taxes__2025.pdf; https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_105/GS_105-375.html; https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_47E/GS_47E-2.html
Rocky Mount (Nash / Edgecombe),NC,"city $0.69 FY27 (up 7 cents) + Nash $0.63 FY27 or Edgecombe $0.89 FY27 = 1.32 or 1.58 per $100 of the 2024 revaluation value; the COUNTY bills the county levy only (Edgecombe WebPAAS; Nash county portal) and the CITY bills its own levy through Tyler Munis Citizen Self Service (rockymountnc.munisselfservice.com/css/citizens/RealEstate); no solid-waste, stormwater or recreation line on either bill - refuse, stormwater, water, sewer, electric and gas are on the RMPU utility account; 9/25: subject 2026 = county 610.21 + city 473.08 = 1,083.29","Rocky Mount Telegram 7/9/26; Nash budget adoption; Edgecombe budget; city FY2027 budget adoption news flash 6/22/2026 (69 cents, $269.7M, $30 vehicle fee); WebPAAS and Munis bills for PIN 3759-99-9614",Nash 2024 -> 2032; Edgecombe 2024 -> 2032,"NO (G.S. 160D-1207); Community Code cases (dept 159) are logged in Munis and published on the city's ArcGIS Online as ViolationsAddress (137,504 geocoded cases) and Code_test_map picompln; primary-violation codes seen: GRAS (overgrowth), PN01 (public nuisance), Z001 (zoning/fence permit); status CBO = complied by owner","n/a. Instruments (9/25): city AGOL org 4MdqIsNzxG7xyTvf (928 feature services; search q=orgid:...): External_Viewer_WFL1 (54 AddressPoints with MUNIS_PIN suffixes per dwelling, 55 Buildings with type and year, 17 Zoning, 10 Neighborhoods, 22 Flood Data 2010, 5/9 historic districts, 4 garbage zones, 45 contours), CRM_Parcel_Master 67 (OwnerName, Bookpage, values, Ward), All_Crimes_for_FS_New 16 (geox/geoy in EPSG 6543 feet; a 4326 point errors), ViolationsAddress 10, PermitsAddress 0, Permit_Application_Entry 11 (Munis piapphdr: permits since 2007 by address and parcel), Edge_Parcels_Dilapidated_1123 63 (housing-code-violation parcels), Down_East/Happy_Hill liens maps, Edgecombe_City_Owned_Flood_Lots1, Edgecombe_Parcels_Flood_Lots 89, CRMGIS_Urban_FEMA_Buyout 16, Property_Acquisition_Plan_Lots, Redevelopment_Commission, Zoning_Sec_Codes 75, Survey123 service-line layers; Edgecombe WebPAAS (search with ITEMSPERPAGE; pDetail/pBLDG/pLAND/pSALE/pCOLL; owner search); Munis CSS real estate (postback; ViewBill by year; AllBills); Cott ROD guest (cotthosting.com/ncedgecombeexternal); county 2025 Delinquent Tax Liens PDF; Google photometa; Municode API job 458641 product 11483",n/a,"no public lookup found (9/25); RMPU's LCRR inventory exists (city Survey123 'Water Service Line Material Survey' and 'Lead Service Line Field Survey' results layers hold 13, 133, 2 and 81 records, none within 300 m of Daughtry); ask RMPU for the classification per address",RMPU / Utility Services 252-972-1250 (Call Center); AGOL survey123 results layers (partial),"LDC on Municode Supp. 89 codified through O-2024-41 (6/24/2024); adopted text amendments since, per the city LDC page (read 9/25): O-2024-58 (8/26/2024 sign amortization), O-2024-82 (12/9/2024 fences and walls), O-2025-5 (1/13/2025 plat certificates), O-2025-6 (1/13/2025 clarifying edits: deletes the 'Dwelling, single-family' rows, B-4/B-5 intent, notice tables, board of adjustment reversals at four-fifths, Sec. 1205), O-2025-64 (9/8/2025 pocket neighborhoods in R-8, R-6, R-6MFA, PDR, O-I; 15,000 sf; 4-12 dwellings), O-2026-xx (4/13/2026 internet cafes); outdoor lighting pending; none touches Chapter 11 or the R-10 two-family cell","Sec. 503 Table 5-1: 'Dwelling, two- to four-family' x only in R-6 MFA and PDR (and O-I, O-I(2), B-1 in Table 5-2); blank in A-1, R-15, R-10, R-8, R-6, MHP; no special-use route; 'Accessory dwelling' x in EVERY residential district incl. R-10 under Sec. 507.C (one extra self-contained unit, same lot and ownership, at most 50% of the principal's gross floor area, no owner-occupancy clause); Sec. 601: R-10 10,000 sf / 10,000 per DU / 75 ft width; R-6MFA two-family 7,000 sf / 3,500 per DU / 60 ft; 50 x 150 platted lots are nonconforming lots of record (602/1102) - Daughtry (id 2) NONCONF use + NONCONF lot","Ch. 11 (read verbatim 9/25): 1105.A.3 land uses cease > 180 days -> conform, 'nonconforming uses that have existed for over fifty (50) years are exempt'; 1105.B.4 a nonconforming use of a structure 'discontinued or abandoned for a period of one hundred eighty (180) consecutive days' may not resume; 1107.A 180 consecutive days 'or for more than eighteen (18) months in any three (3) year period'; 1103.B and 1107.B: damage above 66 2/3% of replacement cost -> rebuild only in conformity (appeal to the board of adjustment); 1101.B.1 'no change of title, possession or right to possession of property shall be construed to prevent the continuance of a nonconforming use'; 1105.B.1 no enlargement or structural alteration; STATE: G.S. 160D-108 and S.L. 2025-94 s.29 per files 40/41; ask for a written 160D-108(h) determination",see Fayetteville row,"$1,143 (Rocky Mount MSA FY2026); FY2027 (10/1/2026) 2BR $1,167, 1BR $972; SAFMR 27801 2BR $1,130 (FY2027; FY2026 was $1,110), 27864 $1,130; not a mandatory SAFMR metro; RMHA 2025 utility allowances (City of Rocky Mount): water 2BR $29, sewer $42, trash $16","LGC: Rocky Mount placed on the September 2026 Unit Assistance List (LGC release 9/4/2026, FY2025 audits, with Cary, Greensboro, Zebulon); 4/1/26 LGC warning; S.L. 2026-27 bars electric and gas transfers; WRAL 9/11/2026: fund balance $100M to $20M, at least $30M of cuts, 'good progress', three residents died after summer-2026 power disconnections. UTILITIES: council 3/30/2026 raised rates about 15% effective 4/1/2026 (electric +14.75%, gas +10.58%, water +15.08% = $23.51 per 3,000 gal, sewer +15.05% = $29.28 per 3,000 gal, environmental services +14.86% = $21.25 a month, stormwater $6 to $8 per ERU; about $45 a household a month); residential deposits up to $325. ENVIRONMENT (Edgecombe side, N Daughtry): DSCA dry-cleaner sites DC330003 Prestige Cleaners (620 E Thomas St, Assessment, groundwater risk Higher) and DC330002 Thorne's (502 Rose St, NFA); five closed gas-station USTs on N Raleigh St; no brownfield, inactive hazardous site or landfill within 500 m; 50 housing-code-violation parcels within 300 m of Daughtry (11/2023 layer)","22 Pine (Nash), 21 Star (Nash), 2 Daughtry (Edgecombe), r10a Pinetops (Edgecombe county rate only); 9/25 late: 2 Daughtry rebased (advisory 48, file 42): PARK-HOLD, G6 FAIL on the documented roll, P 0.03",2026-09-25,https://www.rockymountnc.gov/CivicAlerts.aspx?AID=159; https://www.nctreasurer.gov/news/press-releases/2026/04/01/local-government-commission-warns-rocky-mount-no-further-missteps-will-be-tolerated; https://house.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/SessionLaws/PDF/2025-2026/SL2026-27.pdf; https://www.nctreasurer.gov/news/press-releases/2026/09/04/lgc-applies-financial-oversight-standards-larger-local-governments; https://www.wral.com/news/local/rocky-mount-financial-crisis-progress-brad-briner-treasurer-auditor-september-2026/; https://www.wral.com/news/local/rocky-mount-utility-rate-increase-financial-recovery-march-2026/; https://www.rockymountnc.gov/m/newsflash/home/detail/141; https://www.rockymountnc.gov/m/newsflash/home/detail/185; https://www.rockymountnc.gov/DocumentCenter/View/105/Water-and-Sewer-Retail-Rates-PDF; https://www.rockymountnc.gov/170/Rates-Fees; https://www.rockymountnc.gov/234/Land-Development-Code; https://www.rockymountnc.gov/DocumentCenter/View/7526/O-2025-6-Clarifying-Edits-and-Corrections-2024; https://www.rockymountnc.gov/DocumentCenter/View/7527/O-2025-64-Pocket-Neighborhoods-Cottage-Courts; https://www.rockymountnc.gov/DocumentCenter/View/226/Required-Permits-List-PDF; https://api.municode.com/CodesContent?jobId=458641&nodeId=PTIICOOR_APXALADECO_CH11NO&productId=11483; https://api.municode.com/CodesContent?jobId=458641&nodeId=PTIICOOR_APXALADECO_CH6DIDIST&productId=11483; https://api.municode.com/CodesContent?jobId=458641&nodeId=PTIICOOR_APXALADECO_CH5ZOUSRE&productId=11483; https://taxpa.edgecombecountync.gov/paas/?DEST=pSearch; https://rockymountnc.munisselfservice.com/css/citizens/RealEstate/Default.aspx?mode=new