Pinetops / Edgecombe,NC,"county $0.89 + Town $0.58 = $1.47 per $100 (FY2024-25 through FY2026-27); Town 0.46 in FY2022-23, 0.58 from FY2023-24 and held through the 2024 reappraisal (county 0.95 -> 0.89); NO county solid-waste fee inside the Town (the $150 fee bills unincorporated residents and Leggett); the county collects the Town's tax (tax code C03); 2026 bills levied 9/1, interest from 1/6/2027","NCDOR 2022-23, 2023-24, 2024-25 workbooks; Town FY27 budget ordinance DOC004; WebPAAS bill 26A470433368300 ($419.35 on $28,527)","county reappraisal effective 1/1/2024 (notices 2/2024), eight-year cycle, next 2032; non-reappraisal-year changes for physical improvements under G.S. 105-287(a)(2b) at the 2024 schedule of values; the WebPAAS card's 'Date Last Appraised' field is stale","NO (G.S. 160D-1207); the county Inspections Office 're-inspects vacant buildings' and issues building permits for Pinetops (252-641-7808, permit@edgecombeco.com); Town minimum-housing/demolition ordinances used on S Second St (205, 512, 309) with demolition costs as a tax lien reaching the owner's other property within the Town or one mile","n/a. Instruments: NC OneMap parcels (owner names; county layer 10 was empty 9/25); Edgecombe WebPAAS taxpa.edgecombecountync.gov (POST search by PIN ####-##-####-##, then ?DEST=pDetail with pKEY, then pBLDG/pLAND/pCOLL with txtPIN: card, land, 20-year bill list); Cott ROD eSearch guest (index; images via the HTML5 viewer); county 'Delinquent Tax Listings' PDF; county E911 address points layer 5; Pinetops zoning layer 17 (pre-2021 names); Town documents at townofpinetopsnc.com/documents/288/; EPA ECHO DFR and effluent chart for NC0020435; DWR moratorium list; DEQ distressed lists; Google photometa/streetviewpixels for dated Street View",n/a,Town completed its service-line inventory (2025 CCR: 'prepared an inventory of all service lines ... visit the Town Hall to request a copy'); four groundwater wells,"Town Hall, 101 E Hamlet St, 252-827-4435 (copy on request)","Town Zoning Ordinance Revised 2021 (NCGS 160D amendment adopted 6/1/2021; 'does not affect the zoning of any property'); districts A-1, AR, R-30, R-20, R-20MH, R-12, R-10MH, R-7, RMF, B-1, B-2, B-3, O-I, LI; the county-hosted layer 17 still uses AR-20, RMH-7, R-7, R-12, B-1, B-2, B-3, M-1; the Town's posted map is a 2022 'Proposed Zoning' scan; the Town called M-1 'Light Industrial' in its 11/17/2022 planning agenda; zoning permit $25, required for accessory structures, additions and new homes, NOT for interior repairs (Town FAQ)","Two-Family Dwelling P by zoning permit in R-30, R-12, R-10MH, R-7, RMF and O-I; not permitted in LI, B-1, B-2, B-3, A-1, AR, R-20, R-20MH; duplex minimum lot 15,000 sf / 85 ft (R-7, RMF), 18,000 / 95 (R-10MH), 20,000 / 100 (R-12), 40,000 / 120 (R-30); two-family side yards 15-20 ft; a 50 x 150 in-town lot is nonconforming for a duplex everywhere","Article VIII 70.05.A.3 and 70.06.A.6: a nonconforming use that ceases by vacancy or non-use for more than 180 continuous days may resume only in conformity (the lot judged as a whole; one empty apartment does not end the right); 70.05.A.2 no increase in units; 70.06.A.2 major repair, reconstruction or damage above 60% of tax value rebuilds only in conformity (repairs within 12 months, complete in two years); 70.06.A.5 the Board may approve restoring an 'existing and occupied' one- or two-family residence damaged by fire or other causes, on the same footprint if on a nonconforming lot; 70.08 protects work under a building permit issued before an amendment. STATE: G.S. 160D-108(d) 24-month discontinuance applies to statutory vesting from a development permit, not to this common-law clock; 160D-108(h) written vested-rights determination with de novo appeal; S.L. 2025-94 s.29 (10/6/2025) rewrote 160D-108(c)","H765 'Save the American Dream Act' (would enact 160D-108.2: nonconformities protected from local amendments, reconstruction by right, inconsistent ordinances void from 10/1/2025) stuck in House Finance since 5/6/2025, no 2026 action; S.L. 2025-94 s.29 enacted only the vested-rights clarification","Rocky Mount MSA FY2026 2BR $1,143 (1BR $918); SAFMR 27864 1BR $860; FY2027 2BR $1,167, 1BR $972, SAFMR 27864 2BR $1,130 (not a mandatory SAFMR metro)","Pinetops WWTP NC0020435 (0.3 MGD): DWR '90% Rule imposed' 5/19/2021 (15A NCAC 02T .0118: no sewer-line extension permits until expansion plans are filed; not a statutory moratorium), Town letter to DEQ 8/2026 to lift it; flows 48% of permit in 2025; ECHO: 7 state penalties since 11/2021 ($4,779), NOVs 10/2024-6/2026, fecal coliform 525% over limit Q3 2025, BOD 41% Q2 2026, 4 of 12 quarters in noncompliance. DEQ distressed unit (list 2/16/2026, score 7); not on the FY2024 UAL; electric fund transfers $312,924 to the general fund (22.6%). Utilities: water 14.17 + 4.22-4.60, sewer 28.85 + 8.29-8.75 (+19% since 2023), storm 2, sanitation 25/account, electric 15.49 + 0.1542/kWh (from Wilson wholesale), taps 1,350/1,000, rental meter deposit 475 (FY27). Flood: Zone X at the subject; Hurricane Matthew 2016 modelled flooding along the creek corridor about 1 km SE and near the WWTP; 200+ rescued in the Pinetops area 10/9/2016. Legacy ECHO registrations on E Cobb St (advisory 50, not re-verified)","r10a 610-612 S 2nd St (file 40, 9/25/2026)",2026-09-25,https://townofpinetopsnc.com/documents/288/ARTICLE_8_-_NONCONFORMING_SITUATIONS.pdf; https://townofpinetopsnc.com/documents/288/ARTICLE_4_-_Dimen._Standards.pdf; https://townofpinetopsnc.com/documents/288/Table_of_Uses_final_revisions__revised.pdf; https://townofpinetopsnc.com/documents/288/ARTICLE_10_Administration.pdf; https://townofpinetopsnc.com/documents/288/ZONINGMAP.pdf; https://townofpinetopsnc.com/building-permits-and-inspections; https://townofpinetopsnc.com/documents/288/DOC004.pdf; https://townofpinetopsnc.com/documents/288/Water_Rates.pdf; https://townofpinetopsnc.com/documents/288/Electric_Rates.pdf; https://townofpinetopsnc.com/documents/288/JUNE1MINU