.25.pdf; https://www.fayettevillenc.gov/City-Departments/Public-Services/Stormwater/Stormwater-Utility-Fee-Structure-Updates; http://www.davidbcraig.com/; https://www.cumberlandcountync.gov/docs/default-source/tax-documents/delinquent-taxes/delinquent_taxes__2024.pdf; https://www.cumberlandcountync.gov/docs/default-source/tax-documents/delinquent-taxes/delinquent_taxes__2025.pdf; https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_105/GS_105-375.html; https://www.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/Statutes/HTML/BySection/Chapter_47E/GS_47E-2.html
Rocky Mount (Nash / Edgecombe),NC,"city $0.69 FY27 (up 7 cents) + Nash $0.63 FY27 or Edgecombe $0.89 FY27 = 1.32 or 1.58 per $100 of the 2024 revaluation value; the COUNTY bills the county levy only (Edgecombe WebPAAS; Nash county portal) and the CITY bills its own levy through Tyler Munis Citizen Self Service (rockymountnc.munisselfservice.com/css/citizens/RealEstate); no solid-waste, stormwater or recreation line on either bill - refuse, stormwater, water, sewer, electric and gas are on the RMPU utility account; 9/25: subject 2026 = county 610.21 + city 473.08 = 1,083.29; 9/25 night (Nash side, 918 Star): the COUNTY bills through its own Munis CSS (nashcountync.munisselfservice.com, parcel 030537, bill-number search) while the card sits on iasWorld (taxdata.nashcountync.gov); 2026 = county 493.92 + city 540.96 = 1,034.88 on 78,400; a 2025 renovation shows on the 1/1/2026 value (18,060 -> 78,400; card 'Remodeled Year 2025') under G.S. 105-287(a)(2b) - read both Munis AssessmentHistory pages before modelling a 'seller-year' tax","Rocky Mount Telegram 7/9/26; Nash budget adoption; Edgecombe budget; city FY2027 budget adoption news flash 6/22/2026 (69 cents, $269.7M, $30 vehicle fee); WebPAAS and Munis bills for PIN 3759-99-9614",Nash 2024 -> 2032; Edgecombe 2024 -> 2032,"NO (G.S. 160D-1207); Community Code cases (dept 159) are logged in Munis and published on the city's ArcGIS Online as ViolationsAddress (137,504 geocoded cases) and Code_test_map picompln; primary-violation codes seen: GRAS (overgrowth), PN01 (public nuisance), Z001 (zoning/fence permit); status CBO = complied by owner","n/a. Instruments (9/25): city AGOL org 4MdqIsNzxG7xyTvf (928 feature services; search q=orgid:...): External_Viewer_WFL1 (54 AddressPoints with MUNIS_PIN suffixes per dwelling, 55 Buildings with type and year, 17 Zoning, 10 Neighborhoods, 22 Flood Data 2010, 5/9 historic districts, 4 garbage zones, 45 contours), CRM_Parcel_Master 67 (OwnerName, Bookpage, values, Ward), All_Crimes_for_FS_New 16 (geox/geoy in EPSG 6543 feet; a 4326 point errors), ViolationsAddress 10, PermitsAddress 0, Permit_Application_Entry 11 (Munis piapphdr: permits since 2007 by address and parcel), Edge_Parcels_Dilapidated_1123 63 (housing-code-violation parcels), Down_East/Happy_Hill liens maps, Edgecombe_City_Owned_Flood_Lots1, Edgecombe_Parcels_Flood_Lots 89, CRMGIS_Urban_FEMA_Buyout 16, Property_Acquisition_Plan_Lots, Redevelopment_Commission, Zoning_Sec_Codes 75, Survey123 service-line layers; Edgecombe WebPAAS (search with ITEMSPERPAGE; pDetail/pBLDG/pLAND/pSALE/pCOLL; owner search); Munis CSS real estate (postback; ViewBill by year; AllBills); Cott ROD guest (cotthosting.com/ncedgecombeexternal); county 2025 Delinquent Tax Liens PDF; Google photometa; Municode API job 458641 product 11483; NASH SIDE (9/25 night): iasWorld taxdata.nashcountync.gov (POST inpParid + btSearch on search/commonsearch.aspx?mode=parid, then Datalets/Datalet.aspx?mode=profileall|sales|land|residential|valuesall&sIndex=0&idx=1; values/sketch 500), Nash Munis CSS (ParcelIDTextBox 6-digit parcel; BillNumberTextBox; AssessmentHistory; AllBills lists Outstanding prior-owner years), Nash 2024 Delinquent Tax List PDF (DocumentCenter/View/4578; 16 pages, liens for the year 2024), Cott NCNashExternal guest (in-app browser + javascript_tool for the Quick Name grid; HTML5Viewer/wscottfilexfer.asmx/Load?requestID=&idx= serves the page images to a plain urllib session once the request id is read from the browser), Happy_Hill_Liens_Map_WFL1 layers 3/7 (per-parcel F2012-F2021 taxes, Weed_Cutti, Dem_Water, TOTALS as of 9/2/2021; Down_East_Liens_Map_WFL1 for the Edgecombe side), Permit_Application_Entry/11 ENDS 11/13/2023 (outStatistics max piah_init_app; 0 records 2024-2026) - not evidence about 2024+ work; Munis CSS Permits and General Billing are behind Tyler Portico sign-in; ViolationsAddress keys cases by Match_addr (query the address, not the parcel id)",n/a,"no public lookup found (9/25); RMPU's LCRR inventory exists (city Survey123 'Water Service Line Material Survey' and 'Lead Service Line Field Survey' results layers hold 13, 133, 2 and 81 records, none within 300 m of Daughtry); ask RMPU for the classification per address",RMPU / Utility Services 252-972-1250 (Call Center); AGOL survey123 results layers (partial),"LDC on Municode Supp. 89 codified through O-2024-41 (6/24/2024); adopted text amendments since, per the city LDC page (read 9/25): O-2024-58 (8/26/2024 sign amortization), O-2024-82 (12/9/2024 fences and walls), O-2025-5 (1/13/2025 plat certificates), O-2025-6 (1/13/2025 clarifying edits: deletes the 'Dwelling, single-family' rows, B-4/B-5 intent, notice tables, board of adjustment reversals at four-fifths, Sec. 1205), O-2025-64 (9/8/2025 pocket neighborhoods in R-8, R-6, R-6MFA, PDR, O-I; 15,000 sf; 4-12 dwellings), O-2026-xx (4/13/2026 internet cafes); outdoor lighting pending; none touches Chapter 11 or the R-10 two-family cell","Sec. 503 Table 5-1: 'Dwelling, two- to four-family' x only in R-6 MFA and PDR (and O-I, O-I(2), B-1 in Table 5-2); blank in A-1, R-15, R-10, R-8, R-6, MHP; no special-use route; 'Accessory dwelling' x in EVERY residential district incl. R-10 under Sec. 507.C (one extra self-contained unit, same lot and ownership, at most 50% of the principal's gross floor area, no owner-occupancy clause); Sec. 601: R-10 10,000 sf / 10,000 per DU / 75 ft width; R-6MFA two-family 7,000 sf / 3,500 per DU / 60 ft; 50 x 150 platted lots are nonconforming lots of record (602/1102) - Daughtry (id 2) NONCONF use + NONCONF lot","Ch. 11 (read verbatim 9/25): 1105.A.3 land uses cease > 180 days -> conform, 'nonconforming uses that have existed for over fifty (50) years are exempt'; 1105.B.4 a nonconforming use of a structure 'discontinued or abandoned for a period of one hundred eighty (180) consecutive days' may not resume; 1107.A 180 consecutive days 'or for more than eighteen (18) months in any three (3) year period'; 1103.B and 1107.B: damage above 66 2/3% of replacement cost -> rebuild only in conformity (appeal to the board of adjustment); 1101.B.1 'no change of title, possession or right to possession of property shall be construed to prevent the continuance of a nonconforming use'; 1105.B.1 no enlargement or structural alteration; STATE: G.S. 160D-108 and S.L. 2025-94 s.29 per files 40/41; ask for a written 160D-108(h) determination; Sec. 602.B (9/25 night): a duplex or multifamily structure 'in accordance with the table of permitted uses and lot area regulations may be constructed and occupied on a lot having less than sixty (60) feet of lot frontage' with 8 and 10 ft side yards; Table 6-2 prior lots of record (50 ft before 8/15/1946: 15 ft front, 20 ft rear); with 1102 (area) an R-6MFA duplex on a 50 x 100 lot of record can be rebuilt",see Fayetteville row,"$1,143 (Rocky Mount MSA FY2026); FY2027 (10/1/2026) 2BR $1,167, 1BR $972; SAFMR 27801 2BR $1,130 (FY2027; FY2026 was $1,110), 27864 $1,130; not a mandatory SAFMR metro; RMHA 2025 utility allowances (City of Rocky Mount): water 2BR $29, sewer $42, trash $16","LGC: Rocky Mount placed on the September 2026 Unit Assistance List (LGC release 9/4/2026, FY2025 audits, with Cary, Greensboro, Zebulon); 4/1/26 LGC warning; S.L. 2026-27 bars electric and gas transfers; WRAL 9/11/2026: fund balance $100M to $20M, at least $30M of cuts, 'good progress', three residents died after summer-2026 power disconnections. UTILITIES: council 3/30/2026 raised rates about 15% effective 4/1/2026 (electric +14.75%, gas +10.58%, water +15.08% = $23.51 per 3,000 gal, sewer +15.05% = $29.28 per 3,000 gal, environmental services +14.86% = $21.25 a month, stormwater $6 to $8 per ERU; about $45 a household a month); residential deposits up to $325. ENVIRONMENT (Edgecombe side, N Daughtry): DSCA dry-cleaner sites DC330003 Prestige Cleaners (620 E Thomas St, Assessment, groundwater risk Higher) and DC330002 Thorne's (502 Rose St, NFA); five closed gas-station USTs on N Raleigh St; no brownfield, inactive hazardous site or landfill within 500 m; 50 housing-code-violation parcels within 300 m of Daughtry (11/2023 layer). NASH SIDE (918 Star): no DSCA / IHS / brownfield / landfill / NPDES in 500 m; UST incidents 173-492 m and closed USTs 163-468 m in the Gold / Pine / Carter warehouse district (I-1 / I-2 zoning 76-99 m from the Happy Hill R-6MFA block). STATUTES: G.S. 105-378(a) ten-year bar on tax-lien enforcement (Nash still carries 2008-2010 and 2015 bills on 918 Star); G.S. 45-36.24(b)(1)a: a pre-10/1/2011 deed of trust with a stated maturity expires 15 years after maturity and is deemed satisfied of record (918 Star's 2007 purchase-money DT expired 5/1/2025)","22 Pine (Nash), 21 Star (Nash), 2 Daughtry (Edgecombe), r10a Pinetops (Edgecombe county rate only); 9/25 late: 2 Daughtry rebased (advisory 48, file 42): PARK-HOLD, G6 FAIL on the documented roll, P 0.03; 9/25 night: 21 Star rebased (advisory 49, file 43): OUT, withdrawn from both markets 9/21-9/23, P 0.01",2026-09-25,https://www.rockymountnc.gov/CivicAlerts.aspx?AID=159; https://www.nctreasurer.gov/news/press-releases/2026/04/01/local-government-commission-warns-rocky-mount-no-further-missteps-will-be-tolerated; https://house.ncleg.gov/EnactedLegislation/SessionLaws/PDF/2025-2026/SL2026-27.pdf; https://www.nctreasurer.gov/news/press-releases/2026/09/04/lgc-applies-financial-oversight-standards-larger-local-governments; https://www.wral.com/news/local/rocky-mount-financial-crisis-progress-brad-briner-treasurer-auditor-september-2026/; https://www.wral.com/news/local/rocky-mount-utility-rate-increase-financial-recovery-march-2026/; https://www.rockymountnc.gov/m/newsflash/home/detail/141; https://www.rockymountnc.gov/m/newsflash/home/detail/185; https://www.rockymountnc.gov/DocumentCenter/View/105/Water-and-Sewer-Retail-Rates-PDF; https://www.rockymountnc.gov/170/Rates-Fees; https://www.rockymountnc.gov/234/Land-Development-Code; https://www.rockymountnc.gov/DocumentCenter/View/7526/