Gate 3 pass","9.2.1A: nonconforming only if the use existed in the city on 9/16/1968 (county 4/3/1967) or legally existed at a later effective date, and continues; 9.2.8: more than one year of discontinuance 'for any reason' ends it, intent not a factor (an active building permit within a year and a CO within two preserve it); 9.2.3: one 25 percent expansion by BOA special use permit; G.S. 160D-108(d) as rewritten by S.L. 2026-59 s.42: statutory vesting expires after 24 consecutive months of intentional and voluntary discontinuance (tolled by BOA/court proceedings and emergency declarations)","S.L. 2026-59 (SB 445, signed 8/11/2026): G.S. 160D-917 ADU mandate (effective 1/15/2027; ordinances by 7/1/2027 or ADUs allowed without limitation); s.42 vesting rewrite; s.43 residential-in-commercial applies only to cities of 80,000+ in counties of 1,000,000+ (not Forsyth). S.L. 2026-39 (HB 162, signed 7/6/2026): no minimum dwelling square footage and no minimum off-street parking counts in development regulations, effective 1/1/2027. S.L. 2025-94 (HB 926): resubmittal waits and vested rights (UDO-CC34 implemented it). No duplex or middle-housing mandate; H765 dead in Finance since 5/6/2025; H627 / S495 in Rules","$1,232 (Winston-Salem HMFA); FY2027 HMFA 2BR 1,332 (1BR 1,224); SAFMR 27104 2BR 1,590 (1BR 1,460, 3BR 2,090), 27101 1,370, 27105 1,220; mandatory SAFMR metro; ASPIRE (formerly HAWS) payment standards 27104 2BR 1,440 effective 1/1/2026 (100 percent of FY2026 SAFMR; 1,485 in 2025 at 110 percent); 1/1/2027 table expected at 100 percent","none checked; 306 Auburndale (9/25): FEMA Zone X (NFHL 37067C_2447) and county Zone X; three unnamed stream features within 200 m; two 12-inch RCP storm pipes (1997 inventory) within 60 m; DEQ: NC DEQ feature services (orgid kCu40SDxsCGcuUWO; 37 services queried at 500 m): UST incident 44796 at 307 AUBURNDALE ST (directly across the street, 101-104 m): a residential heating-oil tank release of about 11/6/2016, reported 11/8/2016, init