ount (deposit 200 + set-up fee),City of Oxford PWSID 02-39-010 (all water purchased from Kerr Lake Regional Water System 02-91-010): 2024 CCR reports a service line inventory prepared and lead 90th percentile 8-9 ppb (June 2023; AL 15; 0 sites above); RFQ for Lead Service Line Inventory professional services issued 7/24/2026 (verification / replacement planning); inventory not published as a map,oxfordnc.org/community/city_services/utility_services/water_quality_report.php (CCR text); oxfordnc.org/newslist.php (LSLI RFQ 7/24/2026); City Engineer Kevin Heaphy; DEQ PWS inventory portal (not queried),"Unified Development Ordinance adopted 7/1/2021 (160D); zoning map 2024 (county-hosted layer); 2023 Comprehensive Land Use Plan (Oxford_LUP_Final_20230426); no 2024-2026 text amendment on duplexes or density found (the city posts amendments after 1/15/2026 on its ordinances page: IPMC, social district, vacant commercial property only); Planning Director Cheryl Hart 919-603-1117; zoning letters 75","UDO 2.4.3: Dwelling, Duplex = P (permitted) in GR5, GR10, O&I, CBD, RMU, NMU; not permitted in RA, GR3, NB, HB, IPD, LI, HI, CMU; Dwelling, Multi-Family P in GR10, O&I, CBD, RMU, NMU, CMU; Accessory Dwelling PS in RA, GR3, GR5, GR10, O&I, CBD, RMU, NMU, CMU (3.2.1); definition: a two-unit building divided horizontally or vertically, each unit with its own outside entrance or a common vestibule. Table 2.3.1 GR5: density 5 du/acre (max; footnote: subject to overlays), lot 8,000 sf, width 60 ft, street setback 20 ft, side 10 ft, rear 25 ft, height 35 ft; GR3 3 du/acre and 10,000 sf; GR10 10 du/acre and 5,000 sf. No lot-of-record or existing-building density saving clause: a 0.38-acre duplex (5.24 du/acre) needs a zoning letter on whether density applies to the existing building","UDO 13.5E: a nonconforming USE of a structure discontinued more than 120 calendar days (vacancy counts regardless of intent) is lost, unless the structure is a contributing historic structure in a local hi