Cherryville / Gaston,NC,"FY2026-27: Gaston County 0.599 (held; levied by the FY2027 budget ordinance Section II, adopted 5/12/2026; 0.81 -> 0.61 at the 2023 reappraisal, 0.599 since FY2025) + City of Cherryville 0.48 (held; Section 6 of the city's FY2026-27 budget ordinance) = 1.079 per 100 of the 1/1/2023 reappraisal value; no fee lines on the county bill (sanitation is on the city utility bill at 17 a cart); 307 S Jacob: 2,152.39 on 199,480 (2024-2026), 2,174.33 in 2023 (county 0.61); bills due 9/1, interest from 1/6; the county collects for the city","gastonnc.devnetwedge.com parcel view (taxing districts and payment history, data date 2026-09-24); gastongov.com FY2027 adopted budget PDF (DocumentCenter/View/9277); cityofcherryville.com 2026-2027 proposed budget PDF (ugd/3f73de_81ac672f...); read 9/25/2026 (round 16)","Gaston: FOUR-YEAR cycle adopted by the commissioners in 2025; last reappraisal 1/1/2023 (307 S Jacob 67,980 -> 199,480, +193 percent; ring ratios to 2021-2026 sales 0.73-1.53, median 1.08), next 1/1/2027 (notices of value February 2027, values online late February, informal appeal 30 days from the notice, bills July 2027; public meetings 9/29, 10/7, 10/8/2026); the 2019 reappraisal preceded it; NC does not reassess on sale; SL 2026-8 does not touch Gaston","NONE (no rental registration or periodic inspection); City Code Ch. 8 Article V (8-121 to 8-134) is the unsafe-buildings / unfit-dwellings article under G.S. 160A-441 et seq. (complaint by a public authority or five residents, or the inspector's own motion; hearing 10-30 days; repair or vacate orders; the city manager sets the procedure); building, electrical and plumbing codes are the county's, enforced by the Gaston County inspection department inside the city (8-37, 8-62, 8-92); no IPMC adoption found","n/a. Gaston / Cherryville instruments (9/25/2026): county property record gastonnc.devnetwedge.com/parcel/view/<6-digit parcel>/<tax year> (plain curl: class, tax code, neighbourhood, assessed