ded lot short on area or width may be used for any permitted use if the structure meets the yard requirements; 8.6 front-setback relief to the block average (15 ft floor); 8.3.4: a residential structure damaged below 80 percent of its tax value may be reconstructed at similar size and shape, and for ANY destruction a building permit must be secured within 180 days or reconstruction 'shall not be allowed' unless the Board of Adjustment grants relief (advisory 53 read); G.S. 160D-108(d) 24-month statutory vesting lapse","Cherryville (6,078 in 2020) is far below the 50,000 threshold of G.S. 160D-917 (S.L. 2026-59 s.44 ADU mandate): not applicable; S.L. 2026-39 (no minimum dwelling size, no minimum parking counts) applies from 1/1/2027; S.L. 2025-94 vesting; no duplex or middle-housing mandate reaches Cherryville; R-9 already permits two-family by right","Charlotte-Concord-Gastonia NC-SC HUD Metro FMR Area (METRO16740M16740), a MANDATORY SAFMR metro: FY2027 metro FMR 1BR 1,640 / 2BR 1,785; 28021 SAFMR FY2026 1BR 930 / 2BR 1,030, FY2027 (10/1/2026) 0BR 980 / 1BR 1,020 (918-1,122) / 2BR 1,120 (1,008-1,232); PHA = Gastonia Housing Authority (340 W Long Ave Gastonia, 704-349-5098; administers the HCV for Gaston County; 'located in a designated SAFMR area'; payment standards and allowances unpublished; 9/2026 notice of downward standard adjustments in certain ZIPs; FY2027 plan 'limited voucher issuance'); GHA's 2001 HQS variations: 100 amps per dwelling unit minimum, GFCI/grounding, screens unless central air, R-19 ceilings, treated-lumber steps, no unvented fuel-burning room heaters","FEMA Zone X at 307 S Jacob (NFHL 37071C); Cherryville WWTP NPDES NC0044440 (736 Tot Dellinger Rd; major POTW 2.0 MGD at about 650,000 gpd): ECHO 'Violation Identified' in 11 of 12 quarters to 6/30/2026, 0 SNC, 4 informal actions (NOV 12/9/2022), no penalty, permit expired 7/31/2026 'Admin Continued'; own water plant on Indian Creek; DEQ viability score 5 (2025; 7-8 in 2021-2022), NOT designate