d) damaged 51 percent or more of current assessed value 'may not be restored or reconstructed, except as a conforming use'; 5.1.3 owner's burden; 5.1.5 runs with the land; 5.6.5C/D no expansion, renovation allowed; 5.6.10 rezoning must be to a permitting district; formal determination by the Planning Director (2.3.11, Type I, appealable; fee 500, resubmittal 250); G.S. 160D-108(d) 24-month statutory discontinuance clause is an open question against the 180-day local clock","Clayton (26,307 in 2020; about 32,600 in 2025) is below the 50,000 threshold of G.S. 160D-917 (S.L. 2026-59 s.44 ADU mandate): not applicable; S.L. 2026-39 (no minimum dwelling size or parking counts) applies from 1/1/2027; SB 497 (middle housing by right) in Senate Rules since 3/26/2025; no duplex mandate reaches Clayton","Raleigh-Cary NC HMFA (mandatory SAFMR metro): FY2026 2BR FMR 1,750; FY2027 (10/1/2026) 2BR 1,689; SAFMR 27520 FY2027 2BR 1,640; PHA = Johnston County Housing Assistance Payments Program (107 E Johnston St Smithfield, 919-989-5070): county-wide HCV, waiting list CLOSED (9/25/2026), payment standards unpublished on its pages (90-110 percent of the SAFMR = 1,476-1,804 gross)","FEMA Zone X across the subject parcel (NFHL polygon; panel 3720166900K effective 6/20/2018), nearest SFHA about 400 m; Neuse River Basin riparian buffer (UDO 6.12 / 15A NCAC 02B .0714) on the creek that forms the subject's boundary; Town of Clayton Sam's Branch WRF NPDES NC0025453 (major POTW; ECHO to 6/30/2026: 12 of 12 quarters in noncompliance, 0 SNC, 14 informal actions, no penalties; permit to 3/31/2030); DEQ within 500 m of the subject: 7 UST incidents (nearest 247 m, closed) and 1 AST incident (127 m, closed), no dry-cleaner, hazardous-site, landfill or brownfield records; Clayton and Johnston County absent from the LGC Unit Assistance List (10/6/2025 and 9/4/2026 additions); National Register Clayton Historic District (2010) over downtown with no local overlay standards","w6 307 N Church St (9/26 ro