 "_danville_udc_note": "Danville repealed and re-adopted its zoning code effective 2026-01-01 (Unified Development Code, April 2026 print at danvilleva.gov/DocumentCenter/View/39083). OT-R was converted to UR (Urban Residential) or MR (Multi-Unit Residential). Table 3.A-2: Dwelling, duplex = SUP in UA/TR/UR/MHPR, P in MR; multi-unit not permitted in UR. Nonconforming use lost after 2 years discontinuance incl. pre-2026 time (41.6.E.3). The CityWorks zoning polygon layer (layer 2) is STILL the 2004 map; the parcel layer's ZONING field is being migrated (UR 10,517 parcels vs OTR 7,871 on 9/15).",
 "nc_nominal_combined_rate_2025_26": {
  "_note": "NCDOR 2025-2026 county and municipal tax rates workbook (read 9/16/26): nominal county + municipal rate per $100 as a fraction of assessed value; use with the assessed value, not price. FY27 changes known: Rocky Mount city 0.69, Charlotte city 0.2930. File 33b carries the sales ratios. 9/19/26: Laurinburg is now 0.699 + 0.40 = 0.01099 on 2026 values (the 0.0139 entry was the pre-reappraisal 0.99 + 0.40). 9/25/26: Spring Lake corrected 0.0124 -> 0.0129 (the 0.05 recreation district levy is on the bill). 9/25/26 (round 14): Winston-Salem 0.011022 -> 0.01143 for FY2026-27 (Forsyth 0.5540 + city 0.5890; county 2026 rate table; confirmed on the 306 Auburndale 2026 bill); rows r6b and 1.",
