 "johnston_revaluation": "general reappraisals 2019 and 1/1/2025 (six-year gap; Clayton values +55 percent, revenue-neutral 45 cents; 307 N Church 152,590 -> 196,130, +28.5 percent); NEXT 1/1/2029 per NCDOR's 2026-2027 schedule (four-year cycle); G.S. 105-286(a)(3) (S.L. 2008-146) obliges a county of 75,000+ (Johnston listed in the 2008 presentation) to advance the schedule when the DOR sales-assessment ratio falls below 0.85 or exceeds 1.15, with new values by 1/1 of the third year after notice; neighbourhood 00380 current-sales ratio median 0.916 (62 qualified sales 1/2022-9/2026), Clayton township 0.981 (2,996 sales 1/2024-9/2026); FY2026-27 county rate 0.51 (cut from 0.52 on 6/15/2026)",
 "clayton_udo_rules": {
  "_note": "Read 9/25-26/26 from the Town's PDFs (UDO 7134 current, 6789 as amended 4/15/2024, 6431 original; ordinance 6433).",
  "duplex_table_history": "Table 4.2.5 Duplex Dwelling: 1/2/2024 P in RMD and RHD (and RMF/NCM/MXD); from 4/15/2024 (UDOTA 1-24, ordinance 2024-04-04, recorded 6661/920) P only in RMF, NCM, MXD and C in CZR, CZM, CZD; unchanged through 6/15/2026; note [1] Downtown Boundary bar; the RHD purpose statement dropped duplexes on 4/15/2024, the RMD statement (3.2.15A) still says 'permits duplex dwellings'",
