␀␀␀a␀␀CLAUDE CODE 39 (9/24 evening; advisory 45 verified): OUT stands, P 0.01 (chain 0.05 x 0.45 x 0.50 x 0.85 = 0.0096). LIEN READ at the Register of Deeds: the 2018 Quicken purchase loan (DT 10246/0808) was satisfied 8/28/2023 (11810/0152) after a NEW deed of trust to Rocket Mortgage recorded 8/10/2023 (11798/0072, 18 pages): a $140,000 note dated 8/9/2023 maturing 9/1/2053 with the 1-4 Family Rider (assignment of leases on default, cross-default; occupancy covenant deleted) on a building bought for $103,000 in 2018 - a cash-out refinance at 2023 rates; the payoff today is about $136,000 (assumption: 7.5%%), so the framework's reopen line ($153,000 at $1,025 rents) nets the seller about nothing and the in-place 8%% price ($117,000) is a short sale. Nationstar on the 2026 bill = the same Rocket loan serviced by Mr. Cooper after the 10/1/2025 acquisition. TAX DEFAULT PATTERN (county bills, not a single unpaid bill): 2023 paid 2/29/2024 with interest; 2024 paid 6/30/2025 through DAVID B. CRAIG, ATTORNEY, who represents Cumberland County in tax foreclosures (his site, verbatim), so the parcel was redeemed out of a county tax-foreclosure file; 2025 paid 4/6/2026 by ROCKET MORTGAGE/CORELOGIC with $133.25 interest (servicer advance); 2026 $3,256.38 open. The record owner's three other Cumberland parcels show the same pattern (one paid through the foreclosure attorney in 5-6/2025, one with 2025 AND 2026 open and advertised 6/21/2026, one with 2026 open); the ROD index shows two other parcels sold in 2024 and two refinanced in 2023. THIRD SELLER TEXT (Trulia/Zillow record 80879434, undated, before the 8/27/2026 FSBO.com listing): 'Tenants on month to month leases at $875.00', 'AC last replaced 10 years ago', 'Roof replace 12 years ago', 'floor have been recently replaced in both units', 'washer and dryer hookups', 'tenant pays all utilities', 'No owner financing', 'looking to sale as soon as possible' - so the stated rent FELL from $875 to $850, the tenancies are month to month (not 'established'), and the seller's own roof years disagree (2016 in the 2017 MLS remarks and the 2026 text; 12 years ago in the third). The owner's own 2/2024 ask for unit A was $1,000 (Trulia unit record, removed 2/12/2024). METERS: PWC 120Water carries one service-line asset for 741 and one for 745 (two meters, per-unit) - advisory 45's 'two lids' assumption confirmed; owner_paid 0 stands. E911: 741 (LT 37 A, east) and 745 (LT 37 B, west) both typed APT on the PIN, assigned 10/11/2002 (reproduced). ASSESSMENT HISTORY: $86,700 (2012-2016) -> $43,300 at the 2017 revaluation -> $238,100 at the 2025 revaluation; the 2017 halving was sector-wide (711 Tamarack half $47,300 -> $29,400 while the single-family house at 737 rose to $104,400), so it is not a damage event; the county's sales-comparison factor is 1.85x cost for the two whole-duplex parcels against 1.35x for the 96 halves (an appeal argument only if a record error can be shown; G.S. 105-287). STORMWATER: the 2026 line is $168 because the city's FY2027 residential fee is tiered by impervious building area (tier 2 = 2,501-4,800 sf = $14/month); the '$84 per parcel' convention in 32b is corrected. CRIME (city layers, 2-year window 9/24/2024-9/24/2026): 400 m ring 90 persons / 169 property / 12 society (Pecan was 15 / 50 / 14) - the ring holds the 620-unit Lake in the Pines complex (700-946 Tamarack) and the Rosehill Rd strip; 60 m ring 1 / 2 / 0; at the units: vandalism at 741 on 3/13/2024 and larceny by trickery at 745 on 3/2/2024, a simple domestic at 741 on 4/24/2023 (unfounded) and three 2022 reports at 745. FEMA Zone X; tract 37051002402. RENT: achieved Stoneleigh $1,025 (reproduced); NEW asks 3545 Torbay $1,099 (renovated, 9/2026) and the renovated 1176 Landau half $1,250 (11/2/2025, removed in 19 days); Lake in the Pines 2BR $873-1,419 with a free month through 10/6/2026. At the ask: CoC -3.5%% in place, 0.6%% at the owner's $1,000, 1.3%% at $1,025, 7.3%% only at $1,250 renovated; 8%% needs $1,275 a unit; renovating both units to $1,250 (assumption $40,000) reaches 8%% only at $160,000 and is 25%% of price against file 08's 10%% cap. INSURANCE: advisory 45a re-applied the 10/1/2026 step ($1,680 already carries it; $1,764 is 10/2027) - its recomputed grid is the 10/2027 grid; 45c's grid at $1,680 is the current one and reproduces. HOA: 'Stoneleigh Villas Homeowner Association' is a live NC non-profit (SOS 1093388, formed 4/16/2009, office on this block); neither listing discloses dues; %s. NC next reval 2031 (45 and 45c said 2033; 45a corrected). Photo basis void (2017 FRAR set) reproduced; novice YELLOW unverified.z	utf-8-sigc␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ó␀␀␀€␀␀␀U[␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀U␀$␀␀␀P!␀)N)ÚO)ÚiÚkws␀␀␀&,r␀␀␀Úovr␀␀␀Ž␀␀␀s␀␀␀␀Ø„A€aƒDr
