␀␀Ú!rent_claimed_potential_note_0924tz€$1,300 a unit exceeds every Stoneleigh ask except the renovated $1,250 half; it presupposes a renovation the seller has not doneÚcomps_0924ta—␀␀2026 whole-building pair sales in VCS 3116MF (deed stamps repeated on both halves; 751/755 and 3592/3594 MLS-confirmed): 3541/3545 Torbay $245,000 (4/1/2026); 3592/3594 Torbay $263,000 (6/25/2026, renovated, $2,200 in place); 751/755 Hedgelawn $239,000 (7/15/2026); 759/763 Hedgelawn $239,000 (7/24/2026). Single halves 2025: 3540 Torbay $93,000 (3/28, to a Woodbridge VA LLC), 3552 Torbay $110,000 (4/2), 3543 Rolls $130,000 (3/14), 739 Hedgelawn $135,000 (5/15). The sector's only other whole-duplex parcel, 1176 Landau (lot 20 A-B, PARCEL_PK 179382), was CREATED 5/1/2025 when the same Woodbridge LLC combined lots 20A and 20B (deed 12225/0269, $0 stamps); Redfin's public-record lines show $160,000 and $183,000 sales that day, so the pair cost one of those (assumption: $183,000 for both halves, in line with the LLC's $93,000 half six weeks earlier); that LLC holds 17 Cumberland parcels, 12 of them half-duplexesÚpair_rtp_0924tz«0.84% (3592/3594 at $2,200) to 0.86% (751/755 at $1,025 x 2) on the 2026 pairs; 1.10% for the 2025 Landau assembly if $183,000 and $1,250 x 2 after renovation (assumption)Úask_vs_pair_median_0924tzE$205,000 is 15.3% under the 2026 pair median of $242,000 (reproduced)Úsubmarket_0924taž␀␀VCS 3116MF reproduced 9/24: 98 parcels (Hedgelawn 41, Torbay 32, Rolls 15, Tamarack 7, Landau 3), 96 halves (846-1,024 sf, every one carded 2BR/2 full baths) and 2 whole-duplex parcels; half values $79,700-119,300, median $107,800; 39 entity owners (advisory: 38), 17 owners mailing to the property, 15 New York mailing addresses; sales-comparison factor over cost: halves median 1.35, the two wholes 1.85 and 1.79Útax_year1_0924tÚtax_basis_0924ta]␀␀2026 bill $3,256.38 re-read line by line (county 0.4990 x $238,100 = $1,188.12; county solid waste $260 = 2 x $130; city 0.4495 = $1,070.26; city solid waste $570 = 2 x $285; stormwater $168 = tier 2 of the FY2027 impervious-area schedule); due 9/1/2026, interest from 1/6/2027; 1.59% of the ask; fixed to the 2031 revaluation (45 and 45c said 2033)Úassessed_history_0924ta¼␀␀Billed value $86,700 (2012-2016, the 2009 reval) -> $43,300 (2017-2024, the 2017 reval) -> $238,100 (2025-2026, the 2025 reval). The 2017 halving was sector-wide (711 Tamarack half $47,300 -> $29,400; 1176 Landau half $51,800 -> $32,500 on Redfin's tax history) while the single-family 737 Tamarack rose $86,700 -> $104,400: a submarket markdown, not a damage event. The 2025 re-rating was 5.5x on the subject against 3.3x on the halves because the county applies 1.85x cost to the whole-duplex parcels and 1.35x to halves; the 2026 pair trades ($239,000-263,000) support the $238,100, so no market appeal case; a record-error appeal (bath count is the only candidate) would lower value, not raise itÚtax_bill_history_0924tÚtax_payments_0924tÚtax_delinquency_pattern_0924ta}␀␀2012-2022 paid on time (the 1987-2018 owners to 2018; then the owner, then '2020/2021/2022 - 700' escrow batches with Quicken/CoreLogic flags). 2023: paid 2/29/2024 by the record owner with $37.61 interest. 2024: paid 6/30/2025 by DAVID B. CRAIG, ATTORNEY ($1,576.62 incl. $85.73 interest) - Mr. Craig 'represents the County of Cumberland in the tax foreclosure matters' (davidbcraig.com, verbatim) and takes payoffs only by certified funds, so the parcel had been referred to the county's foreclosure attorney and was redeemed; the same day $17.25 was applied to the 2025 bill through his office (costs allocation, assumption). 2025: paid 4/6/2026 by ROCKET MORTGAGE/CORELOGIC ($3,268.38 incl. $133.25 interest) = a servicer advance three months after interest began. 2026: $3,256.38 UNPAID, lender flag NATIONSTAR MORTGAGE LLC (Mr. Cooper, Rocket's servicer since the 10/1/2025 acquisition). The parcel does NOT appear in the county's 2024 advertisement (published 6/15/2025,