lien_0924tak␀␀CURRENT LIEN: deed of trust 11798/0072, filed 8/10/2023 3:15 PM, Rocket Mortgage LLC (MERS beneficiary, MIN 1000390352974594-70, loan 3529745947), securing a $140,000 note dated 8/9/2023 with monthly payments and maturity 9/1/2053; Fannie/Freddie uniform instrument with the 1-4 Family Rider (Form 3170: fixtures and appliances added to the collateral, borrower will not change the use or zoning without lender consent, occupancy covenant deleted, assignment of leases and deposits on lender's request after default, cross-default with any other note the lender holds); Exhibit A = Lot 37, Stoneleigh Villas Section One, plat book 50 page 63, 'subject to covenants of record'; prepared by Rocket, submitted by a Fayetteville closing firm. The 2018 purchase deed of trust (10246/0808, Quicken) was satisfied 8/28/2023 (11810/0152). Payoff estimate $136,000 (assumption: 7.5% 30-year, 37 payments made; $135,500-136,700 across 7.0-8.0%); P&I about $979/month at 7.5% plus $411/month tax and insurance escrow = about $1,390/month against $1,700 gross - the building does not carry its own debt at the stated rents (assumption on rate)Úseller_break_even_0924tap␀␀Seller net at 7% costs less the $136,000 payoff estimate and the open 2026 bill: $205,000 -> about $51,400; $190,000 -> $37,400; $180,000 -> $28,100; $170,000 -> $18,800; $160,000 -> $9,500; $153,000 -> $3,000; $140,000 -> -$9,100 (short sale). The framework's reopen price is therefore the seller's zero line, and the in-place 8% price ($117,000) needs lender consentÚ	hoa_0924ta¢␀␀'Stoneleigh Villas Homeowner Association' = NC non-profit corporation, SOS ID 1093388, formed 4/16/2009 (Articles filed 4/16/2009), status Current-Active on the city-data mirror, principal office 731 Tamarack Dr (the single-family house two doors east) with a PO Box in 28311; neither listing states dues (Redfin 'HOA Dues -', Zillow '$-- HOA'); the 2023 deed of trust's Exhibit A is 'subject to covenants of record'. zŒ. Ask the seller for the declaration, dues and any rental or leasing restriction before any offer; a leasing cap would be a framework killerÚstormwater_tier_0924ta␀␀City FY2027 residential stormwater fee is tiered by impervious building area: tier 1 under 2,500 sf $7/month ($84), tier 2 2,501-4,800 sf $14/month ($168), tier 3 over 4,800 sf $21/month ($252) (city Stormwater Utility Fee Structure Updates page; 77% / 22% / 1% of parcels); the subject's 2,166 sf footprint plus patios and pads puts it in tier 2 on the 2026 bill ($168, up from $84 in 2025); Pecan (1,221 sf) sits in tier 1. The '$84 per parcel' convention in 32b and the fee stack is corrected to the tier tableÚcrime_0924ta$␀␀City police layers, two-year window 9/24/2024-9/24/2026 (round-8 convention): 400 m ring persons %d / property %d / society %d (Pecan 15 / 50 / 14); 120 m ring %d / %d / %d; 60 m ring %d / %d / %d. Top ring addresses: %s - the Lake in the Pines complex (700-946 Tamarack) and the 3931-3949 Rosehill Rd strip carry the ring. Since 2024-01-01 the 400 m ring counts 119 / 232 / 19. FEMA NFHL Zone X (area of minimal flood hazard); Census tract 37051002402, block 370510024022005; file 14's crime grade stays a ZIP-level F pending a tract-level rebuildÚPersons_400m_2yÚProperty_400m_2yÚSociety_400m_2yÚPersons_120m_2yÚProperty_120m_2yÚSociety_120m_2yÚPersons_60m_2yÚProperty_60m_2yÚSociety_60m_2yÚpolice_at_units_0924tz+All years at 741/745 Tamarack (8 reports): z{. Read: tenant-reported incidents at both units in 2022-2024 (both occupied by tenants; the 2010 reports predate the owner)Úzoning_0924ta␀␀City zoning layer at the centroid: SF-6 (ZNTYPE SF-6, CAMA SF6; county ZONING field agrees). Two- to four-family P since Ord. S2025-008 (4/14/2025); lot 11,285 sf by parcel shape (0.26 ac deeded) against 12,000 sf for two units = density-nonconforming structure; the file 38 casualty routing applies (30-7.C.1 -> C.5 unless the city reads B.8.a.3 broadly; P(two-unit rebuild letter) 0.35; the one Development