prob_0924tÚprob_chain_0924tc␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀#␀␀␀óF␀␀␀€␀␀S␀F␀␀␀ ␀␀€␀␀␀D␀␀v␀␀qQ␀V1*␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀w␀€	␀␀␀J␀␀	␀␀P!␀3h)z	%s = %.2fr␀␀␀)rX␀␀␀rw␀␀␀rf␀␀␀s␀␀␀&  r␀␀␀rZ␀␀␀rZ␀␀␀Ä␀␀␀s␀␀␀ùºué␀␀¹u±t°q˜k¨Q¨F×2Ó2»uùry␀␀␀z; product %.4f, displayed %.2fÚreopen_trigger_0924taZ␀␀Only a lender-consented short sale or a trustee sale reaches the framework: a contract price at or under about $153,000 with both leases at $1,025 or more (or vacant delivery), interiors walked, HVAC and roof dated, the HOA declaration read; on the $850 leases the year-one 8% price is $117,000. Watch instruments: (1) ROD name search for a Substitution of Trustee or Notice of Foreclosure Hearing on 11798/0072; (2) eCourts Cumberland special proceedings (SP) for a trustee foreclosure, and the county tax-foreclosure attorney's sale list at davidbcraig.com; (3) the 2026 bill's payer after 1/6/2027 (servicer advance again = default deepening); (4) Zillow/FSBO price cuts (72 saves at 29 days say the retail bid is there at or near $205,000); (5) the 2025 and 2026 bills on the owner's Worthington parcel (a county foreclosure there would precede one here)Úverdict_0924taË␀␀OUT stands. The advisory's verdict, record reads and $1,680 grid reproduce; the row is worse than advisory 45 knew: the seller carries a $140,000 2023 refinance against a $103,000 basis, three years of tax default with one redemption from the county's foreclosure attorney, a portfolio in the same condition, and a third listing text that lowers the stated rent to a month-to-month $875-then-$850; the ask cannot fall to the framework price without the lenderÚ
asks_0924ta␀␀Only if reopened (all of advisory 45's list) PLUS: the HOA declaration, dues ledger and any leasing restriction; the Rocket/Mr. Cooper payoff letter (loan 3529745947) and any short-sale approval; both leases (month to month per the seller's own earlier text); the 2/2024 unit-A lease if one was signed near $1,000; the reason the 2024 bill went to the county's foreclosure attorney; the RPOADS and MOG disclosures (47E, not exempt); HVAC data plates and the roof invoice (the seller's own texts give 2016 and '12 years ago')Úcorrections_0924taÀ␀␀To advisory 45a: (1) the $1,764 insurance line re-applies the 10/1/2026 step (the board's $1,680 already carries it; $1,764 is 10/2027) - 45c's $1,680 grid is the current one. To advisories 45 and 45c: (2) next revaluation 2031, not 2033 (45a already said so); (3) 'tax_unpaid_flag: not a distress signal' is true of the 2026 bill alone but the 2023-2025 history is a distress pattern (foreclosure-attorney redemption 6/30/2025, servicer advance 4/6/2026); (4) 'the Nationstar tax-service flag points to escrow payment' - the flag is the servicer of the 8/2023 Rocket refinance after the Mr. Cooper acquisition, and the 2025 bill was paid by the servicer only after interest accrued; (5) the 'two water meters' assumption is now a PWC record (two service-line assets); (6) the rent band tops out at $1,100 renovated in advisory 45 but a renovated Stoneleigh half asked $1,250 in 11/2025 and left the market in 19 days; (7) 'seller unlikely to go to $153,000' is now arithmetic: $153,000 nets the seller about $3,000 after the payoff. To 35a/38a row r4d: base zoning columns REVIEW -> P / PASS; evid rewritten; flags_0920 '2026 bill unpaid' bracketed with the pattern. To 32b: stormwater is tiered, not $84 per parcelÚpipeline_0924ta¬␀␀Adopted from 45c: photo-provenance hash against prior-listing images (rule), Redfin fallback when the Zillow capture is thin, suppress the bare 'bill unpaid' flag 9/1-1/5 BUT read the payer column of every prior bill (a foreclosure-attorney or servicer payer is the distress signal), repeated-stamp pair rule, submarket yield screen under 0.90%, listing_source column. NEW from this pass: (a) read every bill's PAYER, not only its status - 'DAVID B CRAIG, ATTORNEY' = county tax-foreclosure file, 'ROCKET MORTGAGE/CORELOGIC' or any servicer paying after the interest date = escrow advance; (b) run the county OWNER LIKE query for an individual seller and read the other parcels' bills (a portfolio in default changes the price path); (c) search the ROD by owner name before pricing any reopen line - the current deed of trust's note amount sets the seller's floor; (d) pull the Trulia unit-level records ('#A', '#B') and the property's second Zillow zpid for earlier owner texts and rent asks; (e) the city's stormwater line is a tier signal for impervious area; (f) the 2024 and 2025 advertisements live at delinquent_taxes__YYYY.pdf (single-word underscore pattern), not the 2023 hyphen patternÚtransport_0924ta3	␀␀Plain fetch served: Cumberland parcel layer (subject in 4326/2264, PHYADDR_STR='TAMARACK', VCS='3116MF', LOCATION_ADDR LIKE '%LANDAU%', OWNER LIKE for the record owner and the Woodbridge LLC), camapwa cards (PropertySummary, BuildingDetails, DeedDetails, DocumentDetails, SaleDetails, LandDetails, OutbuildingDetails for 68495; BuildingDetails for 68818, 68505, 179382; IncomeDetails/PermitDetails/NotesDetails/SalesComparison answered 'Application Unavailable' all evening), bill search and 15 + 15 + 15 + 1 + 4 + 3 + 3 bill details with a cookie jar, county E911 layer (envelope and PIN), city zoning and three police layers (DATE window and Address LIKE), FEMA NFHL 28, Census geocoder, county building footprints, county code-enforcement and permit layers (0 within 300 m; county jurisdiction), Imagery CC2001/2008/2013/2017/2021 ImageServer exportImage and CC2023 export (all served at 4326 this evening), PWC 120Water GraphQL (17 address searches), the special-assessment POST (NO DATA FOUND), the county's 2024 and 2025 advertisements (delinquent_taxes__2024.pdf / __2025.pdf), the Fayetteville stormwater fee page, ncleg 47E-2 and 105-375, davidbcraig.com (Bright Data), city-data's SOS mirror, RentCafe. Apify web-fetch on fabdb3db served FSBO.com's JSON-LD (the page itself is JavaScript-only for WebFetch and Bright Data), Zillow's listing block and realtor.com; the 8ff1a9a7 and d6dc1e15 copies of the same actor answered 'tool not found' on second calls. Bright Data 2b7b1243 served Redfin (1176 Landau), hotpads and davidbcraig.com; 57ad3277 served Zillow and Trulia pages (truncated at the price-history block); 1d64e66b returned an empty SERP. Register of Deeds (Logan Blazor app) driven in the in-app browser: Acknowledge -> Full System -> Human name search -> Directory -> Index Detail (17 rows read from the tree grid) -> row -> 'Image - 18 page(s)' -> the 'Open in new tab' link PDFs/User_0_<timestamp>.pdf served the 18-page deed of trust to curl (image-only; rendered with PyMuPDF); fetching it logged the browser session out (re-entered). Zillow refused the in-app browser ('Access to this page has been denied'); the Wayback Machine was offline; hotpads 403 to WebFetch; rent.com rate-limited. Not used: Composio, Reddit (no experiential question). By hand: eCourts (SP index), NC SOS (HOA status), the FSBO.com seller-contact formÚidÚPÚzoning_statusÚPASSÚ
