2015-04-24að␀␀Book 3227 Page 1543-1545 (instrument 2015014155, 4:20 PM): general warranty deed, the 2001-2015 owner 'Free Trader' (High Point address) to BIG SOUTH PROPERTIES, LLC (4216 Indica Ct, Charlotte), excise 220 (110,000); 'All or a portion of the property herein conveyed does not include the primary residence of the Grantor'; subject only to easements and restrictions of record and current-year taxes; Exhibit A identical to 1998 and 2001; prepared by Donald M. VonCannon, mail to Allman Spry Box 8Úoccupancy_reada]␀␀2/2001-4/2001 the lot was one of an LLC's rental tracts; 4/20/2001 it passed to the LLC's member, who took a 76,800 bank purchase-money-type deed of trust the same day (RE 2168/5240; grantee address Clemmons); on 8/30/2012 and 1/7/2013 that owner and spouse gave the CITY OF WINSTON-SALEM deeds of trust of up to 13,150 and 13,843.05 (RE 3082/1649, satisfied RE 3100/1864; RE 3100/1865, satisfied RE 3246/1886 on 8/20/2015) each carrying a 'Rider Forbidding Not Occupying Premises as Principal Residence' and a two-year review clause: a City housing-rehabilitation loan, which means the house was OWNER-OCCUPIED in 2012-2013 (assumption: the certification was true) and rehab work was done under the City's program then; by the 4/24/2015 sale it was no longer the grantor's primary residence (deed recital; High Point address). With the listing's upper tenant 'of over 10 years' (since before 9/2016), the likeliest configuration is an owner-occupant in one unit and a tenant in the other by 2012-2015, then two tenants under the LLC. The earlier inference that no owner of record lived at 306 after 2001 is WITHDRAWNÚaddress_repositoryÚ306a␀␀one point, ADDRID 69594, RECORD_STAT ACT, no UNIT/UNITTYPE, LANDUSE_DESC 'Residential Single Family', INSP_LU_DESC 'Residential Building, Single Family', CENSUS_STATUS RES; created 2009-04-04 (GISADMIN), last edited 2025-10-20 (HAMBYME; attribute change unknown)Ú309a>␀␀309 AUBURNDALE ST UNIT 1/2, ADDRID 230208, PIN 6815-12-4167.00, land use Single-Family, inspections land use Residential Building, Single Family; created 2008-11-07 (inside the 9.2.9B registration window 1/1/2008-1/1/2009; inference: a registered converted building received a unit sub-address), last edited 2025-07-28Ústreet_and_ringa&␀␀31 Auburndale points; 342 points within 400 m: 258 'Residential Building, Single Family', 74 'Residential Building, Condominium' (3818-3830 Country Club Rd, the RM18 polygon), 1 clubhouse, 1 church, 1 offices; 77 points carry a UNIT, 76 of them the Country Club Rd condos and one 309 AuburndaleÚfieldszsthe layer carries CO_DATE, DEMO_DATE, UTILITY_NOTES, FIELD_NOTES, ADDR_PROBLEMS, ADDR_CHANGE1/2 (all blank for 306)Úzoning_layersÚdistricta4␀␀RS9, ZONING_JURISDICTION WS (Planning_Inspection layer 1); corporate limits WS; zoning jurisdiction WS; ZIP 27104; Growth Management Area 3 (2030 and 2045 layers); ward Southwest; inspectors work area 10: zoning John Floyd, building Lester Barlow, electrical Darrell Mabe, mechanical and plumbing Trenton DayÚoverlayszÀno NRSA, no park, no Opportunity Zone, no zoning-history case on the parcel, no historic sign, no National Register district or property, no historic marker, no locally zoned historic districtÚ	ring_250mz_RS9 (23,638-acre polygon) and one RM18 polygon of 7.42 acres (the Country Club Rd condominiums)Úzoning_history_600ma%␀␀13 cases 1992-2022, none on Auburndale St and none residential: LB/HB/GB/NO/LO/IP special-use cases along Country Club Rd and Silas Creek Pkwy (W1758, W1853 withdrawn, W1897, W2031, W2546 SUP, W2641, W2649, W2754 denied, W3099, W3248, W3323, W3449, ZOAction023); no RM rezoning near the streetÚ
annexationz›ordinance D-17176-1, adopted 11/18/1963, effective 6/1/1964, 'Area One', 'Northwest area, Old Vineyard Rd to Polo Rd', city initiated, 3,143 recorded acresÚudo_textÚsourcezÂUDO ClearCode full PDF, 799 pages, footer LAST UPDATED: 8.17.26 (14.9 MB, plain fetch 9/25/2026; copy at records_2026-09-25/udo_full.pdf; section texts extracted to udo_*.txt; page 269 rendered)Útable_5_1_1a;␀␀PDF page 269 (UDO 5-8): 'Residential Building, Duplex (Lo)' carries Z in RSQ, RM5, RM8, RM12, RM18, RMU, NO, LO, NB, PB and MU-S and P in E; the YR, AG, RS40, RS30, RS20, RS15, RS12, RS9 and RS7 cells are blank (image read); 'Residential Building, Single Family (Lo)' is Z in every RS district with condition 5.2.72Údefinition_converteda␀␀Table 11.2.2 (PDF page 755): 'RESIDENTIAL BUILDING, CONVERTED: A residential building originally constructed as a detached single family dwelling unit which has been modified, expanded, reconfigured or reconstructed in part or in its entirety into one or more occupiable separate living units. This converted residential building does not meet the definition of Residential Building, Single Family and/or the residents would not meet the requirements in the definition of Family living together as a single housekeeping unit.'Údefinition_duplexa␀␀'RESIDENTIAL BUILDING, DUPLEX: A residential building which contains two (2) dwelling units and which occupies one zoning lot.' 'RESIDENTIAL BUILDING, SINGLE FAMILY: A residential building which contains one dwelling unit and which occupies its own zoning lot.'Údefinition_dwelling_unitaÛ␀␀PDF page 726: 'DWELLING UNIT: One or more rooms used as a place of residence for one family, in which there is no area completely closed off for separate living quarters, and there is common access, and kitchen and bathroom facilities, and a single electrical meter.' 'DWELLING UNIT, ACCESSORY, ATTACHED: A second dwelling unit connected to or located within three (3) feet of a residential building, which is restricted in area and purpose in accordance with Section 5.3.4B'Údefinition_family_featuresa␀␀PDF page 729 (Family): 'the presence of certain structural features to the dwelling unit, including, but not limited to, (1) separate double key or other locking mechanisms on internal bedroom doors ..., (2) multiple mailboxes on the house or property, (3) locked or partitioned inside stairwells or doors physically separating parts of the house, (4) separate electrical meters, (5) separate kitchens, or (6) multiple exterior entrances to living areas, shall constitute evidence that there is not a single housekeeping unit established'Ú	sec_9_2_1a<␀␀PDF page 678: nonconforming if 'not permitted in the zoning district' and 'existed ... in the City of Winston-Salem on September 16, 1968, and continues to exist, the use legally existed as of the effective date of this Ordinance, or the use legally existed as of the effective date of subsequent amendments thereto'Ú	sec_9_2_8a-␀␀PDF page 683: 'a nonconforming use that discontinues, for any reason, for a continuous period of more than one (1) year may not be reestablished. Intent shall not be a factor'; C and D: an active building permit issued within one year of discontinuance preserves status if a CO issues within two yearsÚsec_9_2_9_Ba½␀␀PDF page 684 (W): B.1 'Any residential building modified, expanded, reconfigured or reconstructed before July 6, 2004 which meets the definition of residential building, converted and is located in any RS (single-family) or RSQ District, shall be required to register with the City of Winston-Salem between January 1, 2008 and January 1, 2009.' B.2 registration discloses kitchens, bathrooms, 'all interior and exterior access to the units; the number of electrical meters; the number of separately occupied living units per floor'. B.3 'within three (3) years after the end of the registration period (January 1, 2012), all these registered residential buildings, converted shall be discontinued or brought into compliance with the definitions of family and residential building, single family' unless the City Council lengthened or eliminated the period. B.4 'Failure to register ... by January 1, 2009 shall constitute a violation'. B.5 'Any residential building modified, expanded, reconfigured or reconstructed after July 6, 2004 which meets the definition of residential building, converted ... shall constitute a violation of this Ordinance and subject to the zoning enforcement provisions of Section 10.2'Úsec_9_2_9_Dzo(W) single-family houses with more than four unrelated adults: register 2008, discontinue or reduce by 1/1/2012Úsec_5_3_4_B_1_Fa­␀␀PDF page 389 (county only): a. STRUCTURE 'The principal building shall not be altered in any way so as to appear from a public street to be multiple family housing' (prohibited: multiple entranceways, multiple mailboxes, multiple nameplates; access by existing doors; no new street-facing stairways); iv. UTILITIES 'Electric and/or gas utilities shall be supplied to both units through a single meter'; b. 50 percent and 1,000 sfÚsec_5_3_4_B_2_Wap␀␀PDF page 390 (city): 'Within the City of Winston-Salem, the Zoning Officer shall issue a zoning permit for an attached accessory dwelling if the following requirements are met (W): a. PRINCIPAL USE An accessory dwelling unit shall be subordinate in nature to the principal use residential building, single-family. b. RESERVED c. SIZE OF UNIT i. An attached accessory dwelling unit shall occupy no more than fifty percent (50%) of the heated floor area of the principal building, but in no case shall be greater than one thousand (1,000) square feet. ii. The sum of all accessory uses, including home occupations, in a principal residential building shall not exceed fifty percent (50%) of the total floor area of the building. d. PARKING No additional parking is required for an attached dwelling unit. e. NUMBER OF ACCESSORY DWELLINGS No more than one accessory dwelling, whether attached or detached, shall be located on a lot. f. HEIGHT The height of an attached accessory dwelling shall not exceed that of the principal structure.' The 'b. RESERVED' slot is where UDO-CC15 (2/7/2022 city, 4/7/2022 county) removed the earlier clauseÚudo_cc15ae␀␀amendments table (PDF page 21): UDO-CC15, 2/7/22 and 4/7/22, 'Revisions to Accessory Dwelling Unit (ADU) Provisions', Chapters 5, 6 and 11: 'to revise provisions regarding Dwelling, Accessory (Attached and Detached); parking requirements ...; and the definition of a dwelling unit, Accessory Dwelling Unit (Attached), and Accessory Dwelling Unit (Detached)'Úsec_10_2_1_BaÆ␀␀PDF page 705 (W): civil penalty 'one hundred dollars ($100.00)' per violation, assessed after notice by the Director of Inspections and 'Failure to correct the violation within five (5) days of the date of service of the notice', 'Each day of continuing violation shall constitute a separate violation'; C: injunctive relief through the city attorney; settlement authority requires that 'All zoning violations for the property ... have first been abated'Úadu_fitaI␀␀upper story finished 582 of 1,478 heated sf = 39.4 percent (under 50 percent and 1,000 sf); equal 2BR/1BA programs on both floors leave 'subordinate in nature' to the officer; the ADU definition ('a second dwelling unit') against the dwelling-unit definition ('a single electrical meter') leaves the meter question to the officerÚflood_and_siteÚfemazžNFHL layer 28 at the point and within 300 m: FLD_ZONE X, 'AREA OF MINIMAL FLOOD HAZARD', SFHA_TF F, DFIRM 37067C, FLD_AR_ID 37067C_2447 (one polygon in 300 m)Úcounty_floodzàEnvironmental_Planning_Inspection layer 1: Zone X (ZONE_LID 4002); no regulated watershed; three stream features within 200 m (unnamed); two 12-inch RCP storm pipes of the 1997 inventory within 60 m (40 ft and 77 ft, ACTIVE)ÚcensuszŸ2020 tract 39.03 (GEOID 37067003903), block 1013; Winston township; Winston-Salem city; State Senate 32, House 71, Congressional 10 (Cen