govus 404, corporationwiki dead; the only datum is the bizapedia search snippet: 'BIG SOUTH PROPERTIES LLC in Mint Hill, NC ... is a Domestic Limited-Liability Company organized under the laws of the State of North Carolina. The business was filed on January ...' (year truncated); active status, registered agent, principal office and annual-report years unverified: by hand at sosnc.govÚportfolio_2015_2026a(␀␀six Forsyth houses bought 2015-2018 (four from the county table today plus 2709 Eastwood Dr and 1427 Marne St, both bought from Hawkeye Properties LLC by special warranty deed in 3/2015 and 3/2018 and sold in 2026); the 2015 no-stamp instrument 3222/3381 carried Kentucky and Eastwood in togetherÚliquidation_2026aŽ␀␀three listings this spring through the same agent: 1427 Marne St listed 5/12/2026 (the subject's list day) and SOLD 6/10/2026 at 73,000 (26 percent under list, 16 days); 2709 Eastwood Dr listed 4/22/2026 at 99,000, cut 6/25 and 7/11 (the subject's cut days), pending 7/22, SOLD 8/10/2026 at 75,000 (24.2 percent under the original list; at the 2025 value 75,600); the subject is the third; 1808 Kentucky, 2724 Eastwood and 741 Barney are off market on Zillow (Zestimates 70,700 / 76,800 / 82,700; rent Zestimates 1,312 / 1,276 / 1,167): the advisory's 'not a liquidation pattern' is REFUTED for the LLC's 2026 behaviour, though not every parcel is listedÚpublic_record_searchz¼Google SERP for the entity with eviction, summary ejectment, small claims, plaintiff, defendant, lawsuit: nothing; eCourts not queried (gated); Mecklenburg parcels not checked (JS portals)Úcode_amendmentsÚamendment_tableañ␀␀the ClearCode PDF's own history (PDF pages 11-12) runs to UDO-CC36 while the city's web table stops at CC25 (2/19/2024): CC26 day care (5/20/24, 8/15/24); CC27 BOA procedures (9/16/24, 12/19/24); CC28 single-family standards in RM districts (4/10/25); CC29 historic provisions to G.S. 160D (1/21/25, 4/10/25); CC30 county park signs (11/20/25); CC31 replace Legacy 2030 with Forward 2045 (12/1/25, 1/29/26); CC32 remove the graded-slope rules (12/1/25, 5/7/26); CC33 county billboard corridors (5/7/26); CC34 comply with HB 926 (5/18/26, 8/13/26: resubmittal waits, vested rights 2.7.2.C, split jurisdiction 4.3.2.D); CC35 reserved; CC36 Flood Insurance Rate Map date 6/10/2026 (8/17/26, 8/13/26); none touches Table 5.1.1's duplex row, 5.3.4B or 9.2.9BÚpendingzUDO-CC37 (PRD bufferyards): Planning Board hearing 8/13/2026, recommended approval; no elected-body action recorded in the 9/10/2026 agenda bookÚhousing_choice_signala‘␀␀8/13/2026 Planning Board minutes (CC37 item): staff 'anticipates bringing forward additional amendments related to expanding housing choice in the future' after Realtor-association suggestions; Forward 2045 housing page: five public meetings 8/26-9/4/2025 and a 252-response survey asked whether duplexes, triplexes and quadraplexes should be allowed 'in single-family zoning districts in the city' (in-person dot tally: duplex 39, triplex 28, quadraplex 25, none 8), whether RS districts should be regulated by density instead of minimum lot size, and about a 5,000 sf citywide minimum lot; no draft ordinance, docket number or hearing date as of 9/25/2026Úrewrite_statuszµUDO ClearCode WAS the rewrite (adopted 12/2019, effective 1/1/2020, replacing the 1994 UDO); no new comprehensive rewrite is docketed; the section numbers in advisory 51 are currentÚ	state_lawÚsl_2026_59_s44a©␀␀S.L. 2026-59 (Senate Bill 445, Regulatory Reform Act of 2026), ratified 8/6/2026, signed 8/11/2026: new G.S. 160D-917 'Accessory dwelling units': '(a) A local government shall allow the development of at least one accessory dwelling unit which conforms to the North Carolina Residential Code ... for each single-family detached dwelling in areas zoned for residential use that allow for development of single-family detached dwellings.' (b) the local government shall not '(1) Prohibit the use of the primary single-family detached dwelling and the accessory dwelling for long-term rentals by separate households. (2) Require placement in a conditional zoning district. (3) Establish minimum parking requirements ... (4) Prohibit the connection of the accessory dwelling unit to existing utilities systems serving the primary single-family detached dwelling, provided the utility service ... has capacity to serve both dwellings. (5) Charge any fees in excess of those charged for the permitting of a single-family detached dwelling similar in nature. (6) Set a maximum accessory dwelling unit size of less than 800 square feet or greater than 1,000 square feet.' (c) the local government may require a 10-ft setback or less, side-or-rear placement, and 'that accessory dwelling units be smaller than the primary single-family detached dwelling'. (e) exempts private covenants, historic districts, National Historic Landmarks and units not connected to water and sewer. (g) 'accessory dwelling unit' means an attached or detached residential structure ... that has less total square footage than the primary single-family detached dwelling. (h) applies only to non-coastal cities of 50,000 or more. Section 44(c): regulations must be adopted by July 1, 2027, failing which 'accessory dwelling units shall be allowed in that local government without any limitations'; 44(d): subsection (a) effective January 15, 2027 for permit applications on or after that dateÚfitaÿ␀␀Winston-Salem (about 250,000, non-coastal) is covered; the city's 5.3.4B.2 already permits attached ADUs by zoning permit without owner-occupancy or parking clauses, but its 50 percent cap (739 sf on this 1,478 sf house) must rise to at least 800 sf; the 582 sf upper story fits under both; the statute presupposes one primary single-family dwelling plus one ADU and lets the city keep 'smaller than the primary', so it does not legalize a duplex; the primary-and-ADU may be rented to separate households (b)(1)Ú
sl_2026_39a␀␀S.L. 2026-39 (House Bill 162, Parking Lot Reform/Stormwater Control), signed 7/6/2026: G.S. 160D-702(c) rewritten so a regulation shall not set a minimum square footage for Residential Code structures or require a minimum number of off-street parking spaces; effective 1/1/2027Úsl_2026_59_otheraý␀␀s.42 rewrites G.S. 160D-108(d) (statutory vesting for a nonconforming use expires after 24 consecutive months of intentional and voluntary discontinuance, tolled by BOA and court proceedings and now by emergency declarations); s.41 extends site-specific vesting to five years; s.43 (residential by right in commercial districts) applies only to cities of 80,000+ in counties of 1,000,000+ (not Forsyth); no duplex or middle-housing mandate and no limit on amortizing nonconforming residential uses was enactedÚ
dead_billsa@␀␀H765 (Save the American Dream Act, an ADU mandate for cities of 125,000+) re-referred to Finance 5/6/2025; H627 and S495 (Regulation of Accessory Dwelling Units) in Rules since 2025; their substance rode into S445 s.44; the codified G.S. 160D-917 page still reads 'Reserved for future codification purposes' on 9/25/2026Úlender_rulesÚfannie_b4_1_3_05aW␀␀(06/04/2025) 'Whether a property is defined as a one-unit property with an ADU or a two- to four-unit property will be based on the characteristics of the property, which may include, but are not limited to, the existence of separate utility meter(s), a unique postal address, and whether the unit can be legally rented. The appraiser must determine compliance with this definition as part of the analysis in the Highest and Best Use section of the appraisal.'; an ADU 'contained within or part of the primary dwelling with interior access and above grade' is included in the primary's finished areaÚfannie_b2_3_04a€␀␀(10/08/2025) 'Only one ADU is permitted on the parcel of the primary one-unit dwelling. ADUs are not permitted with a two- to four-unit dwelling.' The ADU 'must be subordinate in size to the primary dwelling' with separate ingress/egress, kitchen, sleeping, bathing and bathroom facilities; 'Some ADUs may predate the adoption of the local zoning ordinance and therefore be classified as legal nonconforming. An ADU should always be considered legal if it is allowed under the current zoning code for the subject property. If it is determined that the property contains an ADU that is not allowed under zoning (where an ADU is not allowed under any circumstance), the property is eligible under the following additional conditions: The lender confirms that the existence will not jeopardize any future property insurance claim ... The appraisal requirements related to zoning for an ADU are met.'Úfannie_b3_3_8_02a␀␀(09/02/2026) Rental Income from the Subject Property: eligible property types 'two-to four-unit principal residences, or one-to four-unit investment property, or one-unit Accessory Dwelling Unit (ADU) allowed with a one-unit primary residence only'; ADU limitations: 'Rental income is only allowed from one existing ADU. Purchase or limited cash-out refinance transactions only. The qualifying rental income amount from the ADU is limited to 30 percent of the total qualifying income.' B3-3.1-08 is now 'General Rental Income Information' and defers to it; neither rental page carries a legal-or-nonconforming condition (those sit in B2-3-04 and B4-1.3-05)a¡␀␀for Ogo (investor, not occupant) the property would be a ONE-UNIT investment property whose rent is documented under Form 1007 and leases; the ADU-income carve-out is for owner-occupants; whether an appraiser reports the half-story's rent on the 1007 is the lender ask; the screened DSCR matrix (constants.lender_property_screen) accepts 'legal ADU acceptable, limited to one' and lists 'Zoning Violations' ineligibleÚfreddiezGGuide 5601.2 / 5306.1 not read (guide.freddiemac.com JS app; Apify 401)Úagencyzbthe Housing Authority of Winston-Salem now operates as ASPIRE (haws.org redirects to aspirews.org)Úpayment_standard_2026aÔ␀␀'NEW Payment Standards Effective 1/1/2026' (2026-Payment-Standards-100.xlsx): Zip Code-27104: efficiency 1,160 / 1BR 1,260 / 2BR 1,440 / 3BR 1,880 / 4BR 2,220 / 5BR 2,553 = 100 percent of the FY2026 SAFMR (SAFMRs-FY-2026.pdf row 27104: 1,160 / 1,260 / 1,440 / 1,880 / 2,220); adopted by Resolution 2302 at the 10/14/2025 board meeting; the January 2026 Administrative Plan: 'the PHA used the HUD-posted SAMFRs and multiplied them by between 90 percent and 110 percent'Úpayment_standard_2025a,␀␀effective 1/1/2025 (archived haws.org page): 27104 2BR 1,485 = 110 percent of the FY2025 SAFMR 1,350; the 2BR standard FELL 45 in 2026 as the PHA moved from 110 to 100 percent; hold-harmless: 'The payment standards will remain at their current level until the SAFMR standards meet the current amount'Úfy2027_timinga␀␀October board adoption, January 1 effective date; at 100 percent the 27104 2BR standard would be 1,590 from 1/1/2027 (band 1,431-1,749 gross rent); the site banners 'Important HUD Program Changes - Effective January 1, 2027'; portability caps county-wide 1,660 / 1,730 / 1,900 (0-2BR)Úpermits_and_lettersÚzoning_lettera•␀␀'Administrative Letter - Zoning' from Winston-Salem/Forsyth County Planning and Development Services, Suite 328, 100 East First Street, (336) 727-2624: 'Zoning Letters are available to provide a written response to questions like What is the property zoned, Are there any open zoning or building code cases, Are there any variances, or Is the use a permitted use in the zoning district'; request by email (residential: Yolanda Price, yolandap@cityofws.org), 'most take between 10 to 12 business days', fee 50 per letter payable after the letter is ready (Inspections Division Fee Schedule 7/1/2024: 'Zoning, DMV and ABC letters - Fee 50.00'); the standard letter does not by its terms address legal-nonconforming status, a 2008 registration or rebuild rights, so those must be asked explicitly; the 336-747-7064 number in advisory 51 appears on no page fetched (Planning Board 336-747-7040; Kirk Ericson 336-747-7045)Úpermit_portalad␀␀BuildIT, https://buildit.cityofws.org/wsfcpermit (Timmons Group, 2019; the Inspections Division is city-county for all of Forsyth except High Point, Kernersville and King): guest access without an account to 'Search for permits, View inspection comments, View the status of a permit, View the status of a plan review', behind an hCaptcha ('Please verify you are not a bot'); not attempted by the agent (a CAPTCHA); records begin about 2019, so a 2004-era conversion permit needs a records request to the Inspections Division; GeoCivix (winston-salem.idtplans.com) is the plan-submission portal (account required)Ú	utilitiesÚwater_sewer_fy27aÞ␀␀FY2026-27 User Rate & Fee Manual (cityofws.org DocumentCenter/View/38803): readiness-to-serve 5/8-inch water 8.14 and sewer 10.59 a month (standard rate); water 0.0279/CF to 401 CF, 0.0432 to 936 CF, 0.0478 above; sewer 0.0507 per water CF; two units on one account at 8-10 CCF a month = 88-107 a month = 1,053-1,281 a year; service initiation 30, deposit up to 150; sewer-only flat rate for 'Single-family, two family residence' 60.82 bimonthly where city water is not providedÚwho_paysa˜␀␀the 12/2025 rental ad: 'Water is included and tenant is responsible for electricity' -> the owner carries the water and sewer account (one meter; assumption that the upper unit is on the same account); electricity separately metered per unit is implied by 'tenant is responsible for electricity' (assumption: two Duke meters, which the family definition treats as evidence against a single housekeeping unit)ÚrefusezŠWinston-Salem residential collection is tax-funded; the FY27 solid-waste sheet lists only landfill tipping fees; no owner-side refuse lineÚpoliceÚsummarya×␀␀CrimeMapping.com (WSPD agency 413, the department's only public incident map; it serves about 180 days): 3/29-9/24/2026, 23 records in the 2.3 x 1.6 km extent around the parcel; within 402 m: 3, all fraud (249 S Gordon Dr 4/6/2026 at 191 m, 4051 Gordon Ct 4/6/2026 at 379 m, identity theft 130 Tucker Ave 9/15/2026 at 348 m), no violent, burglary, larceny, vehicle or weapons record inside the quarter mile; within 500 m: 6 (adds vandalism 237 S Cliffdale 9/3, communicating threats 228 S Cliffdale 4/7, simple assault 110 Hedgecock Ave 7/12); nearest burglary 108 N Gordon Dr 9/19/2026 at 561 m; the Country Club Rd strip (510-540 m) holds 9 of the 23 (vandalism, fraud, one aggravated assault 5/10); WSPD Beat 321, District 3Ú
