asks_0925aa␀␀CITY (Administrative Letter - Zoning, yolandap@cityofws.org, 50, 10-12 business days): current lawful use of PIN 6815-12-2578 (single-family or two-family), any 9.2.9B registration 2008-2009 or enforcement case, any converted-building, ADU, building or CO record for the second unit, and whether an attached-ADU zoning permit under 5.3.4B.2 can issue for the 582 sf half-story as configured (subordinate test with two 2BR/1BA units; the dwelling-unit definition's single electrical meter; what building permits and inspections legalization triggers; whether the ADU may carry its own address and meter); INSPECTIONS (BuildIT guest search by hand, then a records request for pre-2019 permits): any permit on 306 Auburndale since 2000, including the February-May 2022 re-roof and chimney removal; COMMUNITY DEVELOPMENT (records request): the 2012-2013 owner-occupied rehabilitation loan file for 306 Auburndale (work write-up, inspection reports, unit count at the time); CLOSING ATTORNEY: payoff statement and cancellation of the private deed of trust RE 3227/1546 (110,661.23 to an individual, due 2045); AGENT (Marcel Perez-Ayala): both leases with rent, deposit, term, utilities and start dates (the lower unit's 12/2025 ask was 850 with water included; who holds the deposits, Vista Realty or the owner), when and how the upper unit was created, meter counts (electric, gas, water) and which HVAC system and water heater serve which unit, photos of the upper unit, its entrance and stair, the rear and the mechanicals, the NC Residential Property Disclosure Statement, and why 2709 Eastwood and 1427 Marne closed at 74-76 percent of list; LENDER: eligibility of a one-unit investment house with one attached ADU (DSCR now, conventional after 10/13/2026) and whether the half-story's rent is reported on the 1007; NAJUM: the Gate 3 reading; SOS by hand: Big South Properties LLC status, registered agent, annual reportsÚcorrections_0925aan
␀␀advisory 51: (1) 'not a liquidation pattern' REFUTED - the LLC sold 1427 Marne (6/10/2026, 73,000, 26 pct under list) and 2709 Eastwood (8/10/2026, 75,000, 24 pct under the original list) through the same agent this summer, with the subject's cut days shared; (2) 'in-place rents unknown' ADVANCED - the lower unit was marketed at 850 with water included 12/3/2025-3/10/2026, so the documented roll is about 1,700 and the row fails G5 and G6 under gate6_basis_rule; (3) the 2001 deed is not a purchase but a no-consideration transfer of five tracts from Cook's Properties LLC to its member (the Kings-to-LLC deed is missing from the county chain; investor-held since at least 4/2001); (4) the 'effective year 2004 = conversion year' assumption is weakened to 'the 2005 field review saw the finished half-story by 2004'; (5) owner-paid water is confirmed by the ad, not merely plausible; (6) the tax record is extended from two bills to twenty (assessed series 88,600 -> 220,500; five late payments with interest since 2018; a 2014 escrow payment under the prior owner); (7) the rate stamp is PMMS 7.03 (9/24), not 6.95; (8) the 336-747-7064 number is not the letter office ((336) 727-2624, email request, 50, 10-12 business days); (9) the UDO amendment table runs to CC36 with CC37 pending and staff signalling housing-choice amendments; (10) S.L. 2026-59 s.44 (G.S. 160D-917) gives the ADU cure statutory backing from 1/15/2027 with an 800 sf floor on the size cap; (11) ASPIRE's 27104 2BR standard is 1,440 (100 pct of FY2026 SAFMR), down from 1,485 in 2025; (12) probability 0.04 -> 0.03 conditional, with the documented-roll factor replacing the rent-or-price factor; (13) 'Register of Deeds grantor search not run' - run: the only open lien is the LLC's own 4/24/2015 deed of trust RE 3227/1546 to a private individual (110,661.23, due 2045), a payoff item; every prior deed of trust is satisfied; (14) the 2001-2015 owner was an OWNER-OCCUPANT under City of Winston-Salem rehabilitation deeds of trust in 2012-2015 (RE 3082/1649, RE 3100/1865 with the principal-residence rider), which the advisory's investor-conversion story and this pass's first inference both missed; (15) the chimney standing in the 2012 Street View and the 2015 county photo was removed with the February-May 2022 re-roof (no permit trail), so the card's two fireplaces are decommissioned; (16) police: 3 records within 402 m in the 180 days the public map serves, all fraud, none violent; 7 code cases at 306, all weeds or trash; (17) DEQ: a heating-oil release with a land-use restriction on the parcel across the street (307 Auburndale, 2016-2017) and a dry cleaner in monitoring at 483 mÚtransport_0925ac␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀#␀␀␀ó@␀␀␀€␀␀S␀F␀␀␀ ␀␀€␀␀␀D␀␀oQ␀U*␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀w␀€	␀␀␀J␀␀	␀␀P!␀3h)z%s: %s (%s)r␀␀␀)r,␀␀Úts␀␀␀& r␀␀␀r-␀␀r-␀␀á␀␀s␀␀␀ùÂ)é␀␀Á)¸Q }°q×'8Ó'8Ã)ùs␀␀␀‡zrow r6b not foundÚw)ÚnewlinerJ␀␀␀)Ú
