ink missing); Table 5.1.1 duplex blank in RS9; 9.2.9B converted-building rule; 5.3.4B.2 city ADU (39 pct) + G.S. 160D-917 from 1/15/2027; seller sold 1427 Marne and 2709 Eastwood this summer at 74-76 pct of list; ASPIRE 27104 2BR 1,440; Zone X; tract 39.03z"file 14 row r6 Auburndale hits: %dÚjurisdictionzWinston-Salemaj␀␀FY2026-27: Forsyth 0.5540 + Winston-Salem 0.5890 = 1.143 per 100 (county 2026 rate table; 306 Auburndale 2026 bill 2,520.32 on 220,500 = 1,221.57 + 1,298.75); FY2025-26 was 0.5352 + 0.567 = 1.1022; no owner-side city fee on the real-property bill (the 30 city fee is on vehicles); the 2025 reappraisal raised 306 Auburndale 85 percent (119,400 -> 220,500) [was: Úreal_estate_tax_rateÚ]zaco.forsyth.nc.us/Tax/taxRates.aspx (2026 table) and the bcpwa bill API, read 9/25/2026 (round 14)Úrate_source_and_fyzµ2025, next 2029 (four-year cycle confirmed on the 306 Auburndale bill values: steps in 2009, 2013, 2017, 2021, 2025); county page: NC requires reappraisal at least every eight yearsÚreassessment_cycleañ␀␀n/a. Forsyth instruments (9/25/2026): NCPTS card API lrcpwa.ncptscloud.com/api (SimpleParcelSearch, getParcelDetails, GetParcelImage Photo/Sketch; header X-Tenant: forsyth), bill API bcpwa.ncptscloud.com/api (SimpleBillSearch by PIN with .000, GetbillDetails, GetBillHistory: line items by rate, payers, interest since 2007), forsythdeeds.com view_image.php?file=re/<book6>/<page6>.tif&type=pdf (deed images, no text layer), maps.co.forsyth.nc.us ArcGIS (NCPTS/PWA_table 0 and 1 - use a where clause, the point query returns the whole 50,000-row table; Master_Address_Repository 0 with UNIT/INSP_LU_DESC; Planning_Inspection 0-15; FC_Annex_History; Development_And_Permits = calendar 2021 only; TaxReappraisal/PERMITS = 11/2017-9/2019; Tax/SalesApp misses street sales; WS_CommDev DQ layer 0 = Feb-2019 delinquency snapshot; Foreclosures_WebMap 11; Housing/Institutional_Home_Buyers 7-9; Environmental_Planning_Inspection flood/streams; Stormwater/SW_Reference; WSPD = beats only), BuildIT permit portal buildit.cityofws.org/wsfcpermit (guest search behind hCaptcha; 2019 on), Administrative Letter - Zoning (yolandap@cityofws.org, 50, 10-12 business days), UDO ClearCode PDF (footer LAST UPDATED), Forward 2045 housing page, ASPIRE (ex-HAWS) payment standards xlsxÚrid_lookup_instrumenta␀␀␀UDO ClearCode (adopted 12/2019, effective 1/1/2020, replacing the 1994 UDO); consolidated PDF LAST UPDATED 8.17.26 with amendments through UDO-CC36 (the city web table stops at CC25); CC37 (PRD bufferyards) pending after an 8/13/2026 Planning Board hearing; staff 'anticipates bringing forward additional amendments related to expanding housing choice' (8/13/2026 minutes) after the Forward 2045 housing survey (8-9/2025) asked about duplexes, triplexes and quadraplexes in single-family districts; no docket yetÚzoning_code_statusaÚ␀␀Table 5.1.1: Residential Building, Duplex is Z (zoning-officer permit) in RSQ, RM5, RM8, RM12, RM18, RMU, NO, LO, NB, PB, MU-S and P in E; BLANK in YR, AG and every RS district (RS40-RS7); LI blank (Poplar NONCONF stands). Section 9.2.9B (W): a house converted into separate living units in an RS or RSQ district before 7/6/2004 had to register 1/1/2008-1/1/2009 and be discontinued or brought into compliance by 1/1/2012; failure to register and any post-7/6/2004 conversion are violations (10.2.1: 100 a day after a five-day notice). Cure: 5.3.4B.2 (W) attached ADU by zoning permit (subordinate; at most 50 percent of heated area and 1,000 sf; one per lot; no owner-occupancy, single-meter or parking clause in the city text since UDO-CC15 of 2022) and, from 1/15/2027, G.S. 160D-917 (S.L. 2026-59 s.44): one ADU per single-family house by right in cities of 50,000+, size cap not under 800 sf, no bar on separate-household long-term rental, utilities connection allowed, ordinances due 7/1/2027. Definitions: dwelling unit requires 'a single electrical meter'; the Family definition treats multiple mailboxes, partitioned stairwells, separate meters, separate kitchens and multiple entrances as evidence against a single housekeeping unitÚduplex_permission_summaryaH␀␀9.2.1A: nonconforming only if the use existed in the city on 9/16/1968 (county 4/3/1967) or legally existed at a later effective date, and continues; 9.2.8: more than one year of discontinuance 'for any reason' ends it, intent not a factor (an active building permit within a year and a CO within two preserve it); 9.2.3: one 25 percent expansion by BOA special use permit; G.S. 160D-108(d) as rewritten by S.L. 2026-59 s.42: statutory vesting expires after 24 consecutive months of intentional and voluntary discontinuance (tolled by BOA/court proceedings and emergency declarations)Únonconforming_use_lapseam␀␀S.L. 2026-59 (SB 445, signed 8/11/2026): G.S. 160D-917 ADU mandate (effective 1/15/2027; ordinances by 7/1/2027 or ADUs allowed without limitation); s.42 vesting rewrite; s.43 residential-in-commercial applies only to cities of 80,000+ in counties of 1,000,000+ (not Forsyth). S.L. 2026-39 (HB 162, signed 7/6/2026): no minimum dwelling square footage and no minimum off-street parking counts in development regulations, effective 1/1/2027. S.L. 2025-94 (HB 926): resubmittal waits and vested rights (UDO-CC34 implemented it). No duplex or middle-housing mandate; H765 dead in Finance since 5/6/2025; H627 / S495 in RulesÚstate_preemption_statusÚhud_fy2026_fmr_2bra3␀␀; FY2027 HMFA 2BR 1,332 (1BR 1,224); SAFMR 27104 2BR 1,590 (1BR 1,460, 3BR 2,090), 27101 1,370, 27105 1,220; mandatory SAFMR metro; ASPIRE (formerly HAWS) payment standards 27104 2BR 1,440 effective 1/1/2026 (100 percent of FY2026 SAFMR; 1,485 in 2025 at 110 percent); 1/1/2027 table expected at 100 percentÚsuperfund_or_environmentalz¶; 306 Auburndale (9/25): FEMA Zone X (NFHL 37067C_2447) and county Zone X; three unnamed stream features within 200 m; two 12-inch RCP storm pipes (1997 inventory) within 60 m; DEQ: ÚPENDINGÚboard_rows_affectedzÄ; 9/25 late: r6b Aub