deeds with image URLs, photo date, values, neighborhood text); /api/GetParcelImage?ImageType=Photo|Sketch&ParcelId=<pk>&BuildingPk=<bpk> ('Photograph' returns 400)Ú	tax_billsa¹␀␀https://bcpwa.ncptscloud.com/api/SimpleBillSearch?query=<PIN with dashes and .000>&pageIndex=0&pageSize=20 (twenty bills 2007-2026 with status); /api/GetbillDetails?BillId=<id> (line items by rate and district, realValue, dueDate, interestBeginDate, lastPaymentDate, interestPaid, transactions with paidBy and processedBy: DPC, LOCKBOX / DPC, EPAY / DPC, MORTGAGE = escrow servicer); /api/GetBillHistory?BillId=<id>; header X-Tenant: forsythÚdeed_imagesa:␀␀http://forsythdeeds.com/view_image.php?file=re/<6-digit book>/<6-digit page>.tif&type=pdf (image PDFs, no text layer; render with PyMuPDF and read as images); the county deeds array carries the URLs; a no-stamp deed is not a purchase (306 Auburndale's 2001 instrument was an LLC-to-member multiple-tracts transfer)Úlayersa␀␀https://maps.co.forsyth.nc.us/arcgis/rest/services: NCPTS/PWA_table/MapServer/1 (assessment TABLE - query with a where clause on PROPERTYADDRESS or CURRENTOWNERNAME1; a geometry query ignores the point and returns the first 50,000 rows) and /0 (tax polygons: TAXPIN, PARCEL_PK, BLK, LOT); Addressing/Master_Address_Repository/MapServer/0 (ADDRESS, UNIT, UNITTYPE, LANDUSE_DESC, INSP_LU_DESC, created_date, last_edited_date, CO_DATE, DEMO_DATE); Planning_Inspection/Planning_Inspection/MapServer 0 corporate limits, 1 zoning, 2 jurisdiction, 3 ZIP, 4 NRSA, 5/15 growth management 2030/2045, 6 parks, 7 wards, 8 inspectors by work area, 9 Opportunity Zones, 10 zoning history (DOCKETNUMBER, ZONEFROM/TO, FINALACTION, Laserfiche link), 11 historic signs, 12/13 National Register, 14 markers; FC_Annex_History/0; Locally_Zoned_Historic_District/0; Development_And_Permits/0 (calendar 2021 only); TaxReappraisal/PERMITS/1 (11/2017-9/2019); Tax/SalesApp/0 (misses street sales); WS_CommDev/DQ_Parcels_and_City_Owned_Parcels/0 (Feb-2019 delinquency snapshot, TotalAmoun); Foreclosures/Foreclosures_WebMap/11 (bank foreclosures 2010-2021 with lender and amount); Housing/Institutional_Home_Buyers/7-9 (investor, institutional, megafirm buyers); Environmental/Environmental_Planning_Inspection 0 floodway, 1 flood zone, 2 streams, 3 watersheds; Stormwater/SW_Reference/0 (pipes); WSPD/WSPD (beats and districts only, no incidents); imagery Imagery/Imagery_2022, ORTHOS_2018_NEW, ORTHOS2005, Imagery/Imagery_1968, Imagery/Imagery1951 (export with bbox)Úrateszêhttps://www.co.forsyth.nc.us/Tax/taxRates.aspx (county 0.5540, Winston-Salem 0.5890 for 2026; city vehicle fee 30); revaluation page /Tax/revaluation.aspx (2025 reappraisal; NC eight-year statutory maximum; the county runs four years)Úpermits_cityaf␀␀BuildIT https://buildit.cityofws.org/wsfcpermit (guest access to permit search, inspection comments and status behind an hCaptcha; records from about 2019); pre-2019 permits by records request to the Inspections Division (city-county for all of Forsyth except High Point, Kernersville, King); GeoCivix winston-salem.idtplans.com for plan submission (account)aû␀␀Administrative Letter - Zoning: Planning and Development Services, Suite 328, 100 East First Street, (336) 727-2624; request by email (residential yolandap@cityofws.org, commercial jeffv@cityofws.org); 50 per letter paid after preparation; 10-12 business days; covers zoning, open cases, variances and permitted use - ask explicitly for nonconforming status, 9.2.9B registration and rebuild rights (instruction sheet cityofws.org/DocumentCenter/View/20295; Inspections fee schedule DocumentCenter/View/1012)Úudoa‘␀␀https://www.udoclearcode.org/_files/ugd/eea745_e5a7fcf655484924a9e21c2ddc7d542a.pdf (799 pages; footer LAST UPDATED; amendment history pages 11-12; Table 5.1.1 page 269; 5.3.4B pages 389-390; 9.2 pages 677-685; definitions 726, 729, 755; enforcement 705); the city web table (wshome.cityofws.org/1593) lags the PDF; Planning Board agenda books at cityofws.org/DocumentCenter/View/37064 (current month)Úvoucher_standardszªASPIRE (formerly HAWS) https://aspirews.org/hcv-downloads/ (Payment Standards by Zip Code xlsx, SAFMR pdf; January 1 effective dates adopted at the October board meeting)zãCity of Winston-Salem User Rate & Fee Manual (cityofws.org/1318/Rates -> DocumentCenter/View/38803 for FY27): water and sewer readiness-to-serve and consumption tiers, inside-city standard rate; residential refuse is tax-fundedÚcoverage_warningsaW␀␀Tax/SalesApp misses 2024-2025 Auburndale sales and carries null addresses; Development_And_Permits holds calendar 2021 only; TaxReappraisal/PERMITS holds 11/2017-9/2019; the NCPTS deeds array can omit an intermediate conveyance (306 Auburndale: the 1998-2001 Kings-to-LLC deed); the county card's totalUnits field is blank for converted housesÚforsyth_instrumentsznRead verbatim 9/25/26 from the ClearCode PDF LAST UPDATED 8.17.26 (round 14). Re-check the footer at each use.Útable_5_1_1_duplexz±Z in RSQ, RM5, RM8, RM12, RM18, RMU, NO, LO, NB, PB, MU-S; P in E; blank in YR, AG, RS40, RS30, RS20, RS15, RS12, RS9, RS7 and all commercial, industrial and LI/GI/CI/IP/C cellsÚsec_9_2_9_B_Was␀␀converted buildings in RS/RSQ: pre-7/6/2004 conversions register 1/1/2008-1/1/2009 (kitchens, baths, access, electrical meters, units per floor, occupants) and are discontinued or brought into compliance by 1/1/2012 unless the council lengthened the period; failure to register and any post-7/6/2004 conversion = violation under 10.2 (100 per day after a five-day notice)zëoriginally a detached single-family dwelling unit, 'modified, expanded, reconfigured or reconstructed in part or in its entirety into one or more occupiable separate living units' and not meeting the single-family or family definitionsztone or more rooms for one family with common access, kitchen and bathroom facilities 'and a single electrical meter'Úfamily_structural_evidencezÝseparate double-key bedroom locks, multiple mailboxes, locked or partitioned inside stairwells or doors, separate electrical meters, separate kitchens, multiple exterior entrances = evidence of no single housekeeping unitÚsec_5_3_4_B_2_W_aduaN␀␀attached ADU by zoning permit: subordinate to the single-family principal use; 'b. RESERVED'; at most 50 percent of heated floor area and 1,000 sf; all accessory uses within 50 percent; no added parking; one ADU per lot; height within the principal; no owner-occupancy or single-meter clause (UDO-CC15, 2/7/2022 city, 4/7/2022 county)Úsec_5_3_4_B_1_F_adua␀␀county version adds: no alteration to appear as multiple-family from the street (no multiple entranceways, mailboxes or nameplates), access by existing doors, no new street-facing stairways, 'Electric and/or gas utilities shall be supplied to both units through a single meter'Úsec_9_2_1_Az¦nonconforming only if not permitted in the district AND existed in the city on 9/16/1968 (county 4/3/1967) or legally existed at a later effective date, and continuesz discontinuance for more than one year for any reason ends the status; intent is not a factor; active building permit within a year and CO within two preserve itÚ	sec_9_2_3z]one expansion of up to 25 percent by BOA special use permit; burden of proof on the applicantÚsec_10_2_1_B_Wzšcivil penalty 100 per day after a five-day correction notice; injunctive relief through the city attorney; settlement only after all violations are abatedÚ
amendmentsz½consolidated through UDO-CC36 (8/17/2026); CC37 PRD bufferyards pending; housing-choice amendments anticipated by staff (8/13/2026 minutes); no docket on RS duplexes or ADUs as of 9/25/2026Úws_udo_ruleszyRead 9/25/26 (round 14) from S445v7.pdf on ncleg.gov; the codified G.S. 160D-917 page still read 'Reserved' on 9/25/2026.ac␀␀G.S. 160D-917: a local government 'shall allow the development of at least one accessory dwelling unit which conforms to the North Carolina Residential Code ... for each single-family detached dwelling in areas zoned for residential use that allow for development of single-family detached dwellings'; shall not prohibit separate-household long-term rental of the primary and the ADU, require conditional zoning, set parking requirements, prohibit connection to the primary's utilities (capacity permitting), charge fees above a single-family permit, or set a size cap under 800 or over 1,000 sf; may require a 10-ft (or smaller district) setback, side-or-rear placement and that the ADU be smaller than the primary; exempts private covenants, historic districts, National Historic Landmarks and units without water and sewer; applies to non-coastal cities of 50,000+ÚdateszÈsubsection (a) effective 1/15/2027 for applications on or after that date; implementing regulations due 7/1/2027, failing which ADUs 'shall be allowed in that local government without any limitations'Úcampaign_readingay␀␀the statute legalizes ONE ADU with a single-family house, not a duplex; a Z-FAIL row in a covered city (Winston-Salem, Greensboro, Durham, Raleigh, Fayetteville, Charlotte, High Point, Concord, Gastonia, Cary, Wilmington is coastal-excluded) whose second unit is smaller than the first can carry Z-CURABLE-ADU with the 1/15/2027 date; the Gate 3 reading of SFR + ADU is Najum'sz›G.S. 160D-702(c) from 1/1/2027: no minimum dwelling square footage and no minimum off-street parking counts in development regulations (coastal exceptions)Úsl_2026_59_s42zÇG.S. 160D-108(d): statutory vesting for a nonconforming use expires after 24 consecutive months of intentional and voluntary discontinuance, tolled by BOA/court proceedings and emergency declarationsÚnc_adu_statute_2026zxRead 9/25/26 (round 14). The Housing Authority of Winston-Salem operates as ASPIRE (haws.org redirects to aspirews.org).Úeffective_2026_01_01Ú27104Ú0BRiˆ␀␀Ú1BRiì␀␀Ú2BRi ␀␀Ú3BRiX␀␀Ú4BRi¬␀␀Ú5BRiù	␀␀zC100 percent of the FY2026 SAFMR (Resolution 2302, 10/14/2025 board)Úeffective_2025_01_01iº␀␀iñ␀␀iÍ␀␀i›␀␀ið␀␀zl110 percent of the FY2025 SAFMR; hold-harmless rule keeps a standard at its level until the SAFMR catches upÚfy2027_expectationzZOctober 2026 board, 1/1/2027 effective; at 100 percent 27104 2BR = 1,590; band 1,431-1,749Úportability_capsi|␀␀iÂ␀␀il␀␀Úaspire_payment_standardszsCity of Winston-Salem User Rate & Fee Manual FY2026-27 (effective 7/2026), standard inside-city rate, read 9/25/26.Úwater_rts_monthly_5_8gHáz®G @Úsewer_rts_monthly_5_8g®Gáz.%@Úwater_per_cfz0-401g6Í;NÑ‘œ?z402-936g®Ø_vO¦?z	937-20052g·bÙ=y¨?Úsewer_per_water_cfg…|Ð³Yõ©?Útwo_units_one_meter_annualzA8-10 CCF a month = 1,053-1,281 a year; the campaign line is 1,150Úservice_initiationÚdeposit_maxz5tax-funded residential collection; no owner-side lineÚwsfc_utility_rates_fy27a-␀␀Adopted 9/25/26 (round 14, 306 Auburndale). Advisory 51's seven pipeline suggestions (forsyth_instruments, ws_udo_rules, the Winston-Salem rate, the RS two-unit check, the ADU pathway check, two DSCRs for ADU cases, the bill-payer read) are accepted; the entries below are what the verification added.Úws_rs_two_unit_checka\␀␀before accepting a two-unit label in a Winston-Salem RS district, read the card land class, building description and effective year and the address repository UNIT field; an SFD card with a two-unit listing is a 9.2.9B converted-building case; a sub-address point created inside 1/1/2008-1/1/2009 is weak evidence of a registration (309 Auburndale)Úadu_pathway_checka␀␀before any Z-FAIL is final, read the jurisdiction's ADU section AND G.S. 160D-917 (S.L. 2026-59 s.44, 1/15/2027) for cities of 50,000+; carry Z-CURABLE-ADU with the lender and Gate 3 questions attached and the size test (second unit smaller than the primary, at most 1,000 sf)Útwo_dscrs_for_aduzçcarry lender-style DSCR with the principal rent only beside the both-rents figure; Fannie B3-3.8-02 (9/2/2026) counts ADU rent only for a one-unit principal residence, so an investor's loan qualifies on the property's own 1007 rentÚbill_payer_reada␀␀on every NC row read the county bill API for payers, payment dates and interest paid across all years served (Forsyth serves twenty): a servicer payer proves an escrowed loan; repeated post-interest-date payments are a liquidity signal (306 Auburndale: five of the last eight)Úrental_history_before_proxyzßsearch HotPads, Trulia, Zillow and SERP for '<address> #<unit>' before carrying any SAFMR proxy: a unit's own recent ask is the documented rent for gate6_basis_rule (306 Auburndale lower unit 850 with water, 12/2025-3/2026)Úutilities_in_the_adz®read the rental ad's utilities line ('Water is included and tenant is responsible for electricity') as the owner-paid-services source and price it from the city's rate manualÚseller_sibling_salesa␀␀search the seller entity's other parcels for 2026 listings and closings (homes.com and Redfin detail pages serve via Apify): shared list days, shared cut days and the accepted discount to list are the seller's demonstrated floor (Big South: 74-76 percent of list twice)Údeed_chain_gapszÙwhen the county deeds array shows a 'price null' transfer, read the image: an LLC-to-member no-consideration deed means an earlier deed into the LLC is missing from the county chain; search the ROD index under the LLCÚeffective_year_fieldz˜the NC CAMA effective year is a reappraisal-cycle field-review construct, not a permit or conversion date; use the bill value series to date the reviewsÚ