- `2026-09-24 session` - files 51/51a/51b/51c (306 Auburndale St Winston-Salem, board id r6b: eight-frame photo read, Forsyth card, deeds, address repository, UDO text, bills, the ADU cure and the Gate 3 framework question), 52/52a/52b/52c (503 Granville St Oxford, id r4c) and 53/53a/53b/53c (307 S Jacob St Cherryville, id r5a). File 51 assimilated 2026-09-25 late night as main files 44/44a/44b/44c (round 14): the card, the 2026 bill and rate, the address repository, Table 5.1.1, Sections 9.2.9B and 5.3.4B.2, the grid and the lender-style DSCRs all reproduce. CORRECTIONS - the lower unit's own 12/2025 ask (850 with water included) makes the documented roll about 1,700, so the row FAILS Gate 5 and Gate 6 under gate6_basis_rule; the seller sold two other Winston-Salem houses this summer at 74-76 percent of list (liquidation, not 'not a liquidation pattern'); the 2001 deed is an LLC-to-member multiple-tracts transfer, so a 1998-2001 deed is missing from the county chain; the 'effective year 2004 = conversion' assumption is weakened; the rate stamp is PMMS 7.03. NEW - S.L. 2026-59 s.44 (G.S. 160D-917) gives the attached-ADU cure statutory backing from 1/15/2027; the UDO history runs to CC36 with housing-choice amendments signalled; ASPIRE's 27104 2BR standard is 1,440; twenty years of bills with five late payments; the zoning-letter office and BuildIT portal. Verdict PARK-HOLD, P 0.03 conditional on Najum's Gate 3 reading. Files 52 and 53 are queued.zfiles 51/51a/51b/51cÚaÚ
